//@version=5
// GENERATED by tools/make_strategy.py from ICT_SMT_IFVG.pine - do not edit by hand: edit the indicator and regenerate.
strategy("ICT SMT + IFVG in HTF FVG · Strategy", shorttitle = "ICT SMT/IFVG STRAT", overlay = true, max_boxes_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, pyramiding = 0, calc_on_every_tick = false, process_orders_on_close = true, initial_capital = 25000, default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1, commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract, commission_value = 1.0, slippage = 1, margin_long = 0, margin_short = 0)

// =====================================================================================
// BUY  = bullish SMT + bullish IFVG that sits in an HTF FVG (5m / 15m / 30m / 1H / 2H / 4H / D / W)
// SELL = the inverse.  Entry timeframes: 30s, 1m, 2m, 3m, 5m.  Closed bars only (no repaint).
//
// ENGINES (multi-timeframe)
//   The whole SMT + IFVG engine is a function (f_runEngine) that runs on a "Feed" = the closed
//   candles of ONE timeframe for BOTH markets.  The chart feed runs on every chart bar.  Up to four
//   extra feeds (default 2m / 3m / 5m / 15m) run on the closed candles of a HIGHER timeframe and
//   draw their SMTs / IFVGs / Buy / Sell marks on the chart you are viewing.  So a 3m BUY and a 15m
//   SMT are both visible on a 1m chart, each tagged with the timeframe it came from.
//   A feed's marks appear on the first chart bar AFTER the feed candle closes (no repaint).
//
// SMT ENGINE
//   * Every liquidity reference exists on BOTH markets with its OWN price (never compared across markets):
//       - feed-TF swings (both markets can anchor the swing; the other market's level = its extreme
//         inside +/- syncBars of the swing, so the two swings do not need the same candle)
//       - HTF swings (default 1H pivots) = major liquidity, e.g. a low from two days ago
//       - PDH/PDL, PWH/PWL
//   * UNIVERSAL PIVOT SMT (section 3b): every confirmed swing high / low of EITHER market is compared with
//     the other market on the SAME candle (exact timestamp alignment, optional +/- N window).  Bearish =
//     one market makes a higher high while the other fails to; bullish = one makes a lower low while the
//     other fails to.  A pivot SMT joins the same pipeline (confirmation, invalidation, pairing, alerts).
//   * Many references can be "armed" at once (a pool of unswept levels). A reference is used up when
//     both markets take it, or when it produces an SMT.
//   * A market TAKES a level when it trades beyond it by more than tolTicks x ITS OWN tick size.
//   * Exactly one market takes it -> DEVELOPING SMT. The sweeper may keep making deeper extremes: the
//     SAME SMT stays valid and its extreme is updated.
//   * The other market takes ITS level before confirmation -> SMT invalidated.
//   * smtConfirmBars after the sweep with the other market still not having taken it -> CONFIRMED.
// RISK
//   * Every Buy/Sell gets a stop (sweep extreme or IFVG far side), fixed-RR and/or HTF-swing targets,
//     and a contract count = Account risk / (stop distance in points x point value).
// FILTERS (all optional, OFF by default): key level, displacement, FVG, MSS.
// IFVG CONFLUENCE SCORE (section 1c): every IFVG gets a deterministic 0-100 rule-based score on its
//   inversion candle (selected HTF zone 25, SMT 20, session 15, displacement 15, liquidity sweep 15,
//   clean structure 10) and a grade A+/A/B/C/D.  Below 'Minimum IFVG Confluence Score' it cannot fire a
//   Buy/Sell or alert.  It is a confluence score, NOT a calibrated probability.  Never recomputed later.
// REQUIRE SMT (section 7): ON = a Buy/Sell needs an SMT paired with the IFVG.  OFF = the IFVG in an HTF
//   FVG fires on its own and an SMT only raises the 5-point confluence score (optional minimum score).
// HTF ZONES (Phase 1 enhanced)
//   * HTF FVGs and NDOGs (new day opening gaps) share one lifecycle: FRESH -> TOUCHED -> PARTIALLY_MITIGATED
//     -> CE_50_MITIGATED -> DEFENDED / FILLED -> INVALIDATED.  CE = fixed 50% of the ORIGINAL gap.
//   * A zone that is DEFENDED (price reached the CE and rejected it), FILLED or INVALIDATED stays on the
//     chart under the existing box rules but is no longer ELIGIBLE for HTF confluence (IFVG-in-HTF test).
//   * An LTF FVG must invert within 'Max Bars from FVG to Inversion' feed bars, or it is expired.
//   * Retention of old marks is measured in DAYS (timestamps), SMT labels at the same extreme are merged.
//   PHASE 2: first-retest tracking (OUTSIDE -> INSIDE transition), age in the zone's OWN timeframe bars
//   with an optional max age, and a deterministic PRIMARY zone when several eligible zones overlap.
//   Candidate = lifecycle AND age AND first-retest; the primary is context only, never a filter.
//   SELECTION ENGINE (section 2b): when candidate zones overlap / nest / stack, exactly ONE of them is
//   SELECTED (composite probability score, or strictly highest / lowest timeframe, or closest CE).
//   Eligible = candidate AND selected -> only the winner reaches the IFVG / SMT / signal engine; the
//   losers keep their lifecycle but are hidden and inactive until the winner drops out.
// DEBUG: table + gray notes on the chart + tooltips on SMT labels tell you WHY there was no signal.
// =====================================================================================

// ============================== 1) INPUTS ==============================
grpView = "0 · Display & debug"
showSMT        = input.bool(true, "Show SMT", group = grpView, tooltip = "Master switch for the SMT labels on the chart. The SMT engine keeps running underneath (alerts, tables, Buy/Sell) when this is off.")
showDeveloping = input.bool(true, "Show developing SMT", group = grpView, tooltip = "Also draw SMTs that are not yet CONFIRMED (their label ends with '?'). Off: only confirmed SMTs are drawn.")
showSmtLines   = input.bool(true, "Show SMT connector lines", group = grpView, tooltip = "Dotted line from the swept liquidity level to the sweep extreme of a liquidity-sweep SMT. The pivot SMT trendline has its own switch in section 3b.")
showRejected   = input.bool(true, "Show SMTs hidden by a filter (gray)", group = grpView, tooltip = "An SMT that was detected but hidden by the key-level filter (section 5) is shown in gray. Hover it to see why.")
showHTF        = input.bool(true, "Show HTF FVGs", group = grpView, tooltip = "Draw the higher-timeframe FVG / NDOG boxes (section 2). Off: the zones are still tracked for the Buy/Sell test, they are just not drawn.")
showIFVG       = input.bool(true, "Show IFVGs", group = grpView, tooltip = "Draw the inverted FVG boxes (section 1). Off: IFVGs are still detected and used for signals, they are just not drawn.")
showSignalMarks = input.bool(true, "Show Buy/Sell triangle marks", group = grpView, tooltip = "Turn off to hide the ▲ BUY / ▼ SELL markers near price. Alerts still fire either way — this only controls the marker on the chart.")
showSmtShapes  = input.bool(true, "Show SMT label shapes (colored boxes)", group = grpView, tooltip = "Off: the SMT text stays on the chart (in the SMT color) but the big colored box / pointer behind it is gone. Connector lines, tooltips, table logs, alerts and the SMT engine itself are NOT affected.")
smtLabelSize   = input.string("Tiny", "SMT label size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large"], group = grpView, tooltip = "Text size of the SMT labels.")
sigMarkSize    = input.string("Normal", "Buy/Sell mark size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large"], group = grpView, tooltip = "Text size of the ▲ BUY / ▼ SELL marks.")
showDebug      = input.bool(true, "Show debug information", group = grpView, tooltip = "Debug table (bottom right) plus small gray notes on the chart explaining why an IFVG did not pair with an SMT.")
showHtfDebug   = input.bool(false, "Show HTF zone debug table", group = grpView, tooltip = "Compact table (bottom left): every active HTF FVG / NDOG with timeframe, type, direction, lifecycle state, eligibility, age (own-TF bars), age expired, first retest available / used, and which zone is the PRIMARY context at the current close.")
keepHistory    = input.bool(true, "Keep SMT / signal marks on past bars", group = grpView, tooltip = "On: SMT labels, Buy/Sell marks and the HTF FVGs / IFVGs used by a signal stay on the chart when you scroll back, so you can review old days. TradingView still keeps only the newest 500 labels / lines / boxes. Off: marks are removed after the max-age inputs.")
keepAllIfvg    = input.bool(false, "Keep ALL IFVG boxes on past bars", group = grpView, tooltip = "Off: an IFVG box disappears when it is invalidated or too old (unless it produced a signal). On: every IFVG box stays (useful when reviewing, but can fill the 500-box limit).")

grpIFVG = "1 · IFVG (entry TFs only: 30s / 1m / 2m / 3m / 5m)"
maxHiddenFVG = input.int(120, "Hidden FVG memory", minval = 10, maxval = 500, group = grpIFVG, tooltip = "How many not-yet-inverted FVGs are remembered (per feed).")
maxFvgAge    = input.int(60, "Max hidden FVG age (bars)", minval = 5, maxval = 500, group = grpIFVG, tooltip = "An FVG that has not inverted within this many bars (of its own feed timeframe) expires.")
maxFvgToIfvgBars = input.int(30, "Max Bars from FVG to Inversion", minval = 1, group = grpIFVG, tooltip = "An FVG must be inverted within this many bars of its formation to count as a valid IFVG. Counted in the feed's own bars from the candle that completed the FVG. An FVG that price closes through LATER than this is treated as expired: no IFVG box and no Buy/Sell.")
minGapTicks  = input.int(0, "Minimum FVG size (ticks)", minval = 0, group = grpIFVG, tooltip = "Gaps smaller than this many ticks are ignored as FVG candidates. 0 = any size.")
fvgExtend    = input.int(15, "Extend boxes (chart bars)", minval = 0, group = grpIFVG, tooltip = "How many chart bars past the current bar the IFVG and HTF FVG boxes are extended to the right while they are alive.")
ifvgMaxAge   = input.int(50, "IFVG max age (bars)", minval = 1, group = grpIFVG, tooltip = "Counted (in feed bars) from the bar the FVG inverted. After this an IFVG can no longer be used for a signal.")
ifvgResolve  = input.string("Resolved anchor (1m → 2m → 3m → 5m)", "IFVG engine", options = ["Resolved anchor (1m → 2m → 3m → 5m)", "Per-feed (legacy)"], group = grpIFVG, tooltip = "Resolved anchor: only the CHART engine (chart must be 1m / 2m / 3m / 5m) confirms IFVGs. When the confirmed chart candle closes through several stacked (overlapping) FVGs of its own timeframe, the engine steps up through the 2m / 3m / 5m feed pools to find ONE anchor; it never looks above 5m. The signal is evaluated on that same inversion candle. Per-feed: every entry-timeframe engine inverts its own FVGs independently (previous behaviour).")
ifvgAnchor   = input.string("Inversion candle", "Anchor IFVG box at", options = ["Inversion candle", "Original FVG (gap candle)"], group = grpIFVG, tooltip = "Where the LEFT edge of the IFVG box sits: the candle that closed through the FVG (inversion), or the middle candle of the original 3-bar FVG.")
ifvgBullClr  = input.color(color.new(color.lime, 80), "Bullish IFVG (support)", group = grpIFVG, tooltip = "Color of bullish IFVG boxes: a bearish FVG that price closed back above, now acting as support.")
ifvgBearClr  = input.color(color.new(color.fuchsia, 80), "Bearish IFVG (resistance)", group = grpIFVG, tooltip = "Color of bearish IFVG boxes: a bullish FVG that price closed back below, now acting as resistance.")

grpFilter = "1b · IFVG quality filter"
filterMode         = input.string("Balanced", "IFVG filter mode", options = ["Off", "Loose", "Balanced", "Strict", "Custom"], group = grpFilter, tooltip = "Quality test on the candle that created the FVG before the gap may become an IFVG: gap size / ATR, body ratio, range / ATR, plus a clean-break buffer the inversion close must pass. Off = every gap qualifies. Loose / Balanced / Strict are presets; Custom uses the four values below.")
customMinGapAtr    = input.float(0.25, "Custom: min gap / ATR", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = grpFilter, tooltip = "Custom mode only: the gap must be at least this fraction of the ATR.")
customMinBodyRatio = input.float(0.50, "Custom: min body ratio", minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.05, group = grpFilter, tooltip = "Custom mode only: body / range of the gap candle must be at least this.")
customMinRangeAtr  = input.float(0.60, "Custom: min range / ATR", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = grpFilter, tooltip = "Custom mode only: the range of the gap candle must be at least this fraction of the ATR.")
customBreakAtr     = input.float(0.05, "Custom: clean break buffer / ATR", minval = 0.0, step = 0.01, group = grpFilter, tooltip = "Custom mode only: the inversion close must pass the gap boundary by at least this fraction of the ATR.")
atrLen             = input.int(14, "ATR length", minval = 1, group = grpFilter, tooltip = "ATR length shared by every ATR-based test in the script (IFVG quality filter, displacement, 50% CE rejection). Computed on each feed's own timeframe.")

grpScore = "1c · IFVG confluence score (rule-based 0-100, not a probability)"
i_minProbScore       = input.int(70, "Minimum IFVG Confluence Score for Signal", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = grpScore, tooltip = "Every IFVG is scored 0-100 on its inversion candle: selected HTF FVG confluence (25), SMT alignment (20), session (15), objective displacement (15), preceding liquidity sweep (15), clean structure / HTF step-up (10). An IFVG below this score can never fire a Buy/Sell or alert; everything else in the entry engine still applies. The score ranks rule-based confluence, it is NOT a statistical probability of a winning trade.")
i_liqLookbackBars    = input.int(20, "Liquidity sweep lookback (feed bars)", minval = 1, group = grpScore, tooltip = "The chart symbol must have swept a liquidity reference (PDH/PDL/PWH/PWL/HTF swing = external, feed swing = internal) on the IFVG's side at most this many feed bars BEFORE (or on) the inversion candle for full liquidity points; up to twice this window still earns 5. SMT recency reuses 'Max bars from SMT to IFVG' (section 7); displacement thresholds reuse section 6.")
i_colorByIFVGScore   = input.bool(true, "Color IFVG boxes by score", group = grpScore, tooltip = "Fill of the IFVG box by grade: A+/A green, B blue, C amber, D gray. The border keeps the bullish / bearish IFVG color of section 1. Off: fill uses the section 1 colors as before.")
i_showIFVGScoreLabels = input.bool(true, "Show score / grade on the IFVG box", group = grpScore, tooltip = "Appends 'A+ 91/100' to the IFVG box text (no extra labels are created).")
i_showIFVGScoreDebug = input.bool(false, "Show score breakdown (debug)", group = grpScore, tooltip = "Writes the six components (HTF 23/25, SMT 18/20, ...) under the score in the IFVG box text, and in the signal tooltip.")
i_scoreTz            = input.string("America/New_York", "Session scoring: times below are written in", options = ["America/New_York", "America/Los_Angeles", "UTC", "Exchange"], group = grpScore, tooltip = "The killzones were removed from the SMT filter earlier, so the session component has its own small time block here. Times are written in this zone and evaluated there (DST handled by TradingView), whatever the chart display zone.")
i_sessNyAm           = input.session("0700-1000", "  NY AM killzone (15 pts)", group = grpScore, tooltip = "IFVG inversion candle inside this session = 15 session points.")
i_sessLdn            = input.session("0200-0500", "  London killzone (15 pts)", group = grpScore, tooltip = "= 15 session points.")
i_sessNyPm           = input.session("1330-1600", "  NY PM session (10 pts)", group = grpScore, tooltip = "= 10 session points.")
i_sessOther          = input.session("2000-0000", "  Other active session (5 pts)", group = grpScore, tooltip = "= 5 session points (default Asia). Outside every session = 0. For higher-timeframe feeds the session is read on the chart bar that follows the feed candle's close.")

grpHTF = "2 · HTF FVG (the IFVG must sit in one)"
requireHTF    = input.bool(true, "Require HTF FVG for Buy/Sell", group = grpHTF, tooltip = "On: a Buy/Sell needs the IFVG to sit in an eligible HTF FVG / NDOG. Off: the HTF zone is only a confluence item (it still adds to the score in section 7).")
htfContain    = input.string("Overlapping", "IFVG counts as in the HTF FVG when it is", options = ["Overlapping", "Fully inside"], group = grpHTF, tooltip = "Overlapping: any overlap between the IFVG box and the HTF FVG. Fully inside: the whole IFVG box lies inside the HTF FVG.")
htfMatchDir   = input.bool(false, "HTF FVG direction must match the setup", group = grpHTF, tooltip = "On: bullish setups only use bullish HTF FVGs, bearish setups only bearish ones. Off: either direction counts.")
htfInvalidate = input.string("Close through", "HTF FVG is removed when price", options = ["Close through", "Wick through"], group = grpHTF, tooltip = "Close through: a candle closes beyond the far side of the gap. Wick through: any wick passes the far side. (Unchanged: this still removes the zone. The 50% CE state machine below only decides ELIGIBILITY.)")
htfEligOn     = input.bool(true, "Only ELIGIBLE zones count for HTF confluence (50% CE state)", group = grpHTF, tooltip = "Every HTF FVG / NDOG runs a lifecycle on confirmed chart bars: FRESH -> TOUCHED -> PARTIALLY_MITIGATED -> CE_50_MITIGATED -> DEFENDED / FILLED -> INVALIDATED. CE = the fixed 50% of the ORIGINAL gap. A zone that is DEFENDED (price reached the CE and rejected it), FILLED (a wick traded through the whole gap) or INVALIDATED is no longer eligible: it stays on the chart (dashed border, state in its text) but an IFVG inside it no longer counts as 'in HTF FVG'. Off: every zone in the list counts, as before.")
htfCeMethod   = input.string("Close Back Across CE", "50% CE Rejection Method", options = ["Wick Rejection", "Close Back Across CE", "Displacement Away From CE", "Close + Displacement"], group = grpHTF, tooltip = "How a zone becomes DEFENDED once price has reached its 50% CE (checked on the CE-hit bar and every confirmed chart bar after it). Wick Rejection: a bar wicks to/through the CE and closes back on the gap's defending side on that same bar. Close Back Across CE: any bar after the CE hit closes on the defending side of the CE. Displacement Away From CE: a displacement candle (section 6 'Displacement' thresholds, chart ATR) moving away from the CE. Close + Displacement: a close back across the CE AND a displacement candle away from it.")
htfMaxDays    = input.int(7, "HTF FVG / NDOG max age (days)", minval = 1, group = grpHTF, tooltip = "A zone older than this (measured from the chart bar that created it, by timestamp) leaves the active list. Its box follows the existing keep / delete rules.")
htfFirstRetest = input.bool(false, "Require First HTF FVG Retest", group = grpHTF, tooltip = "ON: a zone counts for HTF confluence only during its FIRST retest = the first time price re-enters the zone after having been fully outside it since creation. The creation bar never counts. The first retest is consumed (firstRetestUsed) when price leaves the zone again; later returns do not qualify. Applied through HTF eligibility only, on top of the lifecycle and age rules. OFF: Phase 1 behaviour.")
htfMaxAgeBars  = input.int(0, "Max HTF FVG Age (own-TF bars, 0 = OFF)", minval = 0, group = grpHTF, tooltip = "Age = (current bar time - creation time) / the zone's OWN timeframe length, so a 1H zone is aged in 1H bars on any chart (NDOG: days). Once age exceeds this, the zone is no longer eligible for HTF confluence. Lifecycle state is NOT changed and the box stays under the existing visual rules. 0 = OFF (Phase 1 behaviour).")
useNdog       = input.bool(true, "Use NDOG (New Day Opening Gap) as an HTF zone", group = grpHTF, tooltip = "NDOG = the gap between the last close of the previous trading day and the first open of the new day, read from the chart's own confirmed bars (no request.security). Gap up = bullish zone (support), gap down = bearish zone (resistance). It uses the same 50% CE lifecycle, the same 'removed when price' rule (checked on chart bars) and the same 'Max active per timeframe' cap as the HTF FVGs.")
htfAnchor     = input.string("Candle 2 (gap candle)", "Anchor HTF FVG box at", options = ["Candle 1 (first of the 3)", "Candle 2 (gap candle)"], group = grpHTF, tooltip = "The LEFT edge of the box is drawn on the historical HTF candle where the 3-candle FVG formed (time-anchored, so it sits on the right candles on any chart timeframe) instead of floating ahead of price.")
htfExtendMode = input.string("Extend with price", "HTF FVG box width", options = ["Extend with price", "Fixed to the 3 candles"], group = grpHTF, tooltip = "Extend with price: the right edge follows the current bar (+ 'Extend boxes' bars) until the gap is mitigated, then freezes. Fixed: the box only covers the 3-candle sequence (candle 1/2 to the close of candle 3).")
htfMaxPerTf   = input.int(6, "Max active FVGs per timeframe", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = grpHTF, tooltip = "Newest zones kept per HTF timeframe. When the cap is exceeded the oldest zone of that timeframe leaves the active list.")
htfMinGapTicks = input.int(0, "Min HTF FVG size (ticks)", minval = 0, group = grpHTF, tooltip = "HTF gaps smaller than this many ticks are ignored. 0 = any size.")
useHtf1 = input.bool(true, "Use", inline = "h1", group = grpHTF)
htfTf1  = input.timeframe("5", "HTF #1", inline = "h1", group = grpHTF, tooltip = "HTF slot #1: tick 'Use' and pick the timeframe whose FVGs are scanned (on that timeframe's closed candles).")
useHtf2 = input.bool(true, "Use", inline = "h2", group = grpHTF)
htfTf2  = input.timeframe("15", "HTF #2", inline = "h2", group = grpHTF, tooltip = "HTF slot #2 (see HTF #1).")
useHtf3 = input.bool(false, "Use", inline = "h3", group = grpHTF)
htfTf3  = input.timeframe("30", "HTF #3", inline = "h3", group = grpHTF, tooltip = "HTF slot #3 (see HTF #1).")
useHtf4 = input.bool(true, "Use", inline = "h4", group = grpHTF)
htfTf4  = input.timeframe("60", "HTF #4", inline = "h4", group = grpHTF, tooltip = "HTF slot #4 (see HTF #1).")
useHtf5 = input.bool(false, "Use", inline = "h5", group = grpHTF)
htfTf5  = input.timeframe("120", "HTF #5", inline = "h5", group = grpHTF, tooltip = "HTF slot #5 (see HTF #1).")
useHtf6 = input.bool(true, "Use", inline = "h6", group = grpHTF)
htfTf6  = input.timeframe("240", "HTF #6", inline = "h6", group = grpHTF, tooltip = "HTF slot #6 (see HTF #1).")
useHtf7 = input.bool(true, "Use", inline = "h7", group = grpHTF)
htfTf7  = input.timeframe("D", "HTF #7", inline = "h7", group = grpHTF, tooltip = "HTF slot #7 (see HTF #1).")
useHtf8 = input.bool(false, "Use", inline = "h8", group = grpHTF)
htfTf8  = input.timeframe("W", "HTF #8", inline = "h8", group = grpHTF, tooltip = "HTF slot #8 (see HTF #1).")
htfBull = input.color(color.new(color.blue, 75), "HTF bullish FVG", group = grpHTF, tooltip = "Color of bullish HTF FVG / NDOG boxes.")
htfBear = input.color(color.new(color.orange, 75), "HTF bearish FVG", group = grpHTF, tooltip = "Color of bearish HTF FVG / NDOG boxes.")

grpSel = "2b · HTF FVG selection engine (one winner among overlapping zones)"
i_htfSelectionMode = input.string("Highest Probability (Auto Engine)", "HTF FVG Selection Mode", options = ["Highest Probability (Auto Engine)", "Strictly Highest Timeframe", "Strictly Lowest HTF (Refinement)", "Deepest Consequent Encroachment (CE)"], group = grpSel, tooltip = "When several candidate HTF FVGs / NDOGs overlap, nest or stack, exactly ONE is selected and only that one counts for the IFVG-in-HTF test, the SMT tap, the primary context and the Buy/Sell. Highest Probability: the highest composite score (freshness, liquidity confluence, displacement quality, timeframe weight). Strictly Highest Timeframe: the largest timeframe wins, whatever the score. Strictly Lowest HTF: the smallest timeframe wins (refinement). Deepest CE: the zone whose 50% consequent encroachment is closest to the current confirmed close. Every mode falls through the same deterministic tie-breaker chain (score, freshness, timeframe, displacement, most recent, list order).")
i_htfSelectScope   = input.string("Overlapping zones only", "Selection scope", options = ["Overlapping zones only", "All candidate zones (one winner)"], group = grpSel, tooltip = "Overlapping zones only: candidates are grouped into clusters of mutually overlapping zones (a 1H inside a 4H, two partially overlapping gaps, a 4H/2H/1H stack) and one winner is picked per cluster; a zone that overlaps nothing does not compete and stays active. All candidate zones: one single winner across every candidate on the chart, whatever its price level.")
i_htfScoring       = input.bool(true, "Enable Probability Scoring", group = grpSel, tooltip = "Computes the composite score for every candidate (shown in the debug tables). OFF: the Auto mode and every tie use only the deterministic chain (fresher, higher timeframe, larger displacement, most recent). The strict / CE modes are unaffected by this switch except for their tie-breaks.")
i_wFresh           = input.float(0.35, "Freshness Weight", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = grpSel, tooltip = "Weight of the freshness / mitigation component. Freshness = state score (FRESH 1.0, TOUCHED 0.8, PARTIALLY_MITIGATED 0.55, CE_50_MITIGATED 0.3) x (1 - 0.5 x deepest penetration of the gap so far). DEFENDED / FILLED / INVALIDATED zones are never candidates (existing lifecycle). The four weights are normalised: score = sum(weight x component) / sum(weights), always 0..1.")
i_wConf            = input.float(0.20, "Liquidity/Confluence Weight", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = grpSel, tooltip = "Weight of the liquidity confluence component: PDH / PDL (1.0 each), PWH / PWL (1.0 each), previous-day and previous-week 50% equilibrium (0.5 each) and every unswept HTF swing of the chart engine (0.75 each) that lies inside the zone or within the proximity below. Points are divided by 'points for full score' and capped at 1.")
i_wDisp            = input.float(0.20, "Displacement Weight", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = grpSel, tooltip = "Weight of the displacement / gap-quality component, measured on the closed HTF candles that formed the gap and normalised by that timeframe's own ATR: gap / ATR (1.0 at 0.75 ATR), displacement-candle range / ATR (1.0 at 2 ATR), body / range of the displacement candle, and optionally relative volume. The average of the available sub-scores is used (an NDOG has a gap only).")
i_wTf              = input.float(0.25, "Timeframe Weight", minval = 0.0, step = 0.05, group = grpSel, tooltip = "Weight of the structural timeframe component: log-scaled rank of the zone's timeframe between the smallest and the largest ENABLED HTF slot (NDOG counts as 1 day), so it works for any HTF configuration. Structural preference only: a deeply mitigated 4H loses to a fresh, high-quality 1H under the default weights.")
i_confProxAtr      = input.float(0.5, "Level proximity (x chart ATR)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.1, group = grpSel, tooltip = "A liquidity level counts as confluence when it lies inside the zone or within this many chart ATRs of its edges. 0 = inside only.")
i_confSat          = input.float(2.0, "Confluence points for full score", minval = 0.5, step = 0.5, group = grpSel, tooltip = "Confluence points at which the confluence component reaches 1.0 (2.0 = two major levels, or one major level plus one equilibrium and one HTF swing).")
i_useRelVol        = input.bool(false, "Use relative volume in the displacement score", group = grpSel, tooltip = "Adds volume of the displacement candle / its 20-candle average (1.0 at 2x) to the displacement component. Off by default: only enable on symbols with real exchange volume (index futures yes, spot FX no). Missing volume is ignored, never scored.")
i_ceTieTicks       = input.int(4, "CE mode: proximity tie tolerance (ticks)", minval = 0, group = grpSel, tooltip = "Deepest CE mode: candidates whose CE distance to the current close differs by at most this many ticks are treated as equally close and the composite score / tie chain decides.")
i_htfHideLosers    = input.bool(true, "Hide non-selected overlapping zones", group = grpSel, tooltip = "Non-selected candidates keep their box object and lifecycle but are drawn fully transparent until they are selected (e.g. when the winner becomes DEFENDED or FILLED). The selected zone gets a 2-px border. No boxes are created or deleted by the selection engine.")
i_htfSelDebug      = input.bool(false, "Debug Selection Engine", group = grpSel, tooltip = "Table (middle left): every candidate with cluster, selected flag, composite score, freshness / confluence / displacement / timeframe components, state and CE. Off by default.")

grpSMT = "3 · SMT engine"
correlatedSym  = input.symbol("CME_MINI:ES1!", "Correlated symbol", group = grpSMT, tooltip = "ES for an NQ chart, NQ for an ES chart. Either market can be the one that takes the liquidity or makes the new swing.")
tolTicks       = input.int(2, "SMT tolerance (ticks)", minval = 0, group = grpSMT, tooltip = "A market only 'takes' a level (or makes a higher high / lower low) if it trades beyond it by MORE than this. Each market uses its OWN tick size.")
pivotLeft      = input.int(5, "Feed swing: bars left", minval = 1, group = grpSMT, tooltip = "Bars to the LEFT of a candle that must have lower highs / higher lows for it to be a swing (ta.pivothigh / ta.pivotlow). Used by the swing liquidity references (section 4) AND by the universal pivot SMT (section 3b).")
pivotRight     = input.int(5, "Feed swing: bars right", minval = 1, group = grpSMT, tooltip = "Bars to the RIGHT that must not exceed the swing. This is the delay before a swing is confirmed, and the only source of delay for swing references and pivot SMTs.")
syncBars       = input.int(3, "Swing sync window (bars)", minval = 0, group = grpSMT, tooltip = "Liquidity-sweep swings (section 4): the other market's level for a swing = its extreme within +/- this many bars of the swing. Used up to a maximum of the 'bars right' value. The pivot SMT has its own alignment window in section 3b.")
smtConfirmBars = input.int(3, "SMT confirmation bars", minval = 1, group = grpSMT, tooltip = "An SMT becomes CONFIRMED this many bars after the sweep / swing if the other market has not taken its level. The sweeper can keep making new extremes meanwhile; it does not reset the count.")
smtLifeBars    = input.int(30, "SMT setup lifetime (bars)", minval = 1, group = grpSMT, tooltip = "Counted from the sweeper's latest extreme. After this the SMT can no longer produce a signal.")
smtMaxDays     = input.int(7, "Max SMT age (days, 0 = OFF)", minval = 0, group = grpSMT, tooltip = "An SMT older than this (by timestamp, from the candle on which it was detected) EXPIRES: it can no longer confirm, pair with an IFVG, fire a Buy/Sell or count in the sequence, and it is removed from the active list on every bar. With 'Keep marks on past bars' ON its label stays on the chart as history; OFF deletes the label too. 0 = never expire by age.")
smtMerge       = input.bool(true, "Merge SMT labels that share the same extreme (high / low)", group = grpSMT, tooltip = "When several liquidity sweeps or pivot divergences (other references, other engine timeframes) produce SMTs anchored to the SAME price extreme, only one label is drawn and the others are appended to it ('+PDL[3m]'). Detection, alerts, tables and the state machine are not affected: this is label de-duplication only.")
smtMergeTicks  = input.int(0, "  merge tolerance (ticks)", minval = 0, group = grpSMT, tooltip = "Two SMT extremes count as the same edge when they are within this many ticks of each other. 0 = exactly the same price.")
smtBullClr     = input.color(color.teal, "Bullish SMT", group = grpSMT, tooltip = "Color of bullish SMT labels, connector lines and pivot trendlines.")
smtBearClr     = input.color(color.red, "Bearish SMT", group = grpSMT, tooltip = "Color of bearish SMT labels, connector lines and pivot trendlines.")
removeInvalidatedSMT = input.bool(true, "Remove an SMT immediately once it's broken/invalidated", group = grpSMT, tooltip = "On: the moment the other market also takes the level (whether that happens before or after the SMT confirmed), its label/connector line is deleted right away instead of lingering until it naturally expires. Off: restores the old behavior.")
minSmtTf       = input.timeframe("1", "Minimum timeframe for SMT display", group = grpSMT, tooltip = "Only SMTs found by an engine running on THIS timeframe or higher are drawn. Example: set to 15 on a 1m chart -> the 1m chart's own SMTs are hidden, but the 15m feed's SMTs (section 8) are still drawn on the 1m chart. The engines keep running underneath either way.")

grpPiv = "3b · Universal pivot SMT (every swing high / low vs the correlated market)"
usePivSmt     = input.bool(true, "Enable universal pivot SMT", group = grpPiv, tooltip = "Compares EVERY confirmed swing high / low (ta.pivothigh / ta.pivotlow with the swing lengths of section 3) of the chart symbol with the correlated symbol on the SAME candle, and every swing of the correlated symbol with the chart symbol. Bearish SMT: one market makes a higher high while the other fails to (lower or equal high). Bullish SMT: one market makes a lower low while the other fails to (higher or equal low). Nothing is limited to session or key levels. A pivot SMT joins the normal SMT pipeline: confirmation, invalidation when the failing market later takes its swing, label merging, IFVG pairing, Buy/Sell and alerts. It runs in every engine (chart + higher-timeframe feeds).")
pivSync       = input.int(0, "Alignment window (bars, 0 = same candle)", minval = 0, group = grpPiv, tooltip = "0: the other market's price is read on exactly the same candle as the swing (exact timestamp alignment). N: its extreme within +/- N candles of the swing is used instead, for markets whose swings print a candle or two apart. Capped at 'Feed swing: bars right'.")
pivMaxGap     = input.int(80, "Max bars between the two swings (0 = OFF)", minval = 0, group = grpPiv, tooltip = "A new swing is only compared with the previous swing of the same side (high vs high, low vs low) when they are at most this many feed bars apart. An older previous swing is not compared, but the new swing still becomes the 'previous' one for the next comparison.")
pivShowLine   = input.bool(true, "Draw divergence trendline (previous swing → new swing)", group = grpPiv, tooltip = "Line between the two swing points of the chart symbol that were compared. Uses the SMT colors of section 3 (faded while the SMT is only developing).")
pivLineWidth  = input.int(2, "  trendline width", minval = 1, maxval = 4, group = grpPiv, tooltip = "Width of the divergence trendline.")
pivLineStyle  = input.string("Solid", "  trendline style", options = ["Solid", "Dashed", "Dotted"], group = grpPiv, tooltip = "Style of the divergence trendline.")
pivShowMarker = input.bool(true, "Draw marker with the correlated market's two swings", group = grpPiv, tooltip = "Small text marker at the previous swing showing the other side of the divergence, e.g. '◆ ES1! 5210.25 → 5205.50 LH'. The chart can only plot the chart symbol's prices, so this is where the correlated market's swing prices are written.")

grpLiq = "4 · Liquidity references (each enabled type is its own SMT test)"
useSwing        = input.bool(true, "Feed-TF swing highs / lows (minor)", group = grpLiq, tooltip = "Feed-timeframe swing highs / lows as unswept liquidity: an SMT is detected when exactly one market trades THROUGH its swing level. Both markets can anchor the swing (see 'Swing sync window' in section 3). This is the sweep test; the pivot divergence test is section 3b.")
swingMaxRefs    = input.int(10, "  max unswept swings kept per side", minval = 1, maxval = 50, group = grpLiq, tooltip = "Pool size of unswept feed swings per side (highs / lows). The oldest unswept swing is dropped when the pool is full.")
swingRefMaxAge  = input.int(800, "  drop a feed swing after (bars)", minval = 10, group = grpLiq, tooltip = "An unswept feed swing older than this many feed bars is removed from the pool.")
useHtfSwing     = input.bool(true, "HTF swing highs / lows (major)", group = grpLiq, tooltip = "Pivots on a higher timeframe (default 1H). This is what lets a 1m chart see an SMT against a low from days ago. Also the pool used for 'HTF swing' take-profit targets.")
swTf            = input.timeframe("60", "  HTF swing timeframe", group = grpLiq, tooltip = "Timeframe on which the major swing highs / lows are computed (both markets).")
swL             = input.int(3, "  HTF swing bars left", minval = 1, group = grpLiq, tooltip = "Bars to the left of an HTF candle that must be lower / higher for it to be an HTF swing.")
swR             = input.int(3, "  HTF swing bars right", minval = 1, group = grpLiq, tooltip = "Bars to the right that confirm the HTF swing (delay in HTF bars).")
swSync          = input.int(1, "  HTF swing sync window (HTF bars)", minval = 0, group = grpLiq, tooltip = "The other market's level for an HTF swing = its extreme within +/- this many HTF bars of the swing.")
htfSwingMaxRefs = input.int(20, "  max unswept HTF swings kept per side", minval = 1, maxval = 50, group = grpLiq, tooltip = "Pool size of unswept HTF swings per side.")
usePD           = input.bool(true, "Previous day high / low (PDH / PDL)", group = grpLiq, tooltip = "Each market's previous DAILY bar (futures: 18:00-17:00 ET session).")
usePW           = input.bool(false, "Previous week high / low (PWH / PWL)", group = grpLiq, tooltip = "Each market's previous WEEKLY bar high / low as liquidity references.")

grpKey = "5 · Optional filter: key level"
keyFilter = input.bool(false, "Require SMT at a key level", group = grpKey, tooltip = "Key level = PDH/PDL/PWH/PWL, an HTF swing, or (option below) a sweep that taps an HTF FVG. A plain feed-TF swing SMT or pivot SMT in the middle of a range is rejected (shown gray when 'Show SMTs hidden by a filter' is on).")
keyHtfTap = input.bool(true, "A sweep that taps an HTF FVG counts as a key level", group = grpKey, tooltip = "The sweep candle (or the pivot candle of a pivot SMT) overlapping an ELIGIBLE HTF FVG / NDOG satisfies the key-level filter.")

grpConf = "6 · Optional filters: structure after the sweep"
reqDisp       = input.bool(false, "Require displacement after the sweep", group = grpConf, tooltip = "Buy/Sell only when a displacement candle (thresholds below) in the SMT's direction has closed after the sweep / swing.")
reqSetupFvg   = input.bool(false, "Require same-direction FVG after the sweep", group = grpConf, tooltip = "Buy/Sell only when a 3-candle FVG in the SMT's direction has formed after the sweep / swing.")
reqMSS        = input.bool(false, "Require MSS after the sweep", group = grpConf, tooltip = "Bullish: a close above the last feed swing HIGH that existed when the sweep began. Bearish: a close below the last feed swing LOW.")
dispAtrMult   = input.float(1.0, "Displacement: body >= x ATR", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = grpConf, tooltip = "A candle is a displacement candle when its body is at least this many ATRs (feed ATR) AND it passes the body / range test below AND it closes in the setup's direction. Also used by the '50% CE Rejection Method' of section 2.")
dispBodyRatio = input.float(0.60, "Displacement: body / range >=", minval = 0.1, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.05, group = grpConf, tooltip = "Body divided by the candle's full range must be at least this (0.60 = wicks take at most 40% of the candle).")

grpSignal = "7 · Buy / Sell signal"
i_requireSMT    = input.bool(true, "Require SMT for Buy/Sell", group = grpSignal, tooltip = "ON: a Buy/Sell needs a valid SMT (liquidity-sweep or pivot SMT) paired with the IFVG, as before. OFF: an IFVG that passes the HTF / Phase 3 gates fires on its own on its inversion candle; a same-direction SMT is then an optional confluence that only raises the score below (and is consumed by the signal when present). Without an SMT the stop loss falls back to the IFVG side and the Phase 3 sequence filter is skipped.")
minScore        = input.int(0, "Minimum confluence score (0 = OFF)", minval = 0, maxval = 5, group = grpSignal, tooltip = "Score = HTF gap (1) + SMT (1) + SMT confirmed (1) + displacement (1) + HTF direction aligned (1). A Buy/Sell fires only when its score is at least this. Mostly useful with 'Require SMT' OFF, where an SMT is not mandatory but still counts. The score is written in the signal tooltip and the alert text.")
reqConfirmedSMT = input.bool(true, "Require confirmed SMT for Buy/Sell", group = grpSignal, tooltip = "On: the SMT must be CONFIRMED. Off: a developing SMT is enough (the SMT can still disappear later). Ignored when 'Require SMT' is OFF.")
confluenceBars  = input.int(10, "Max bars from SMT to IFVG", minval = 1, group = grpSignal, tooltip = "Feed bars between the SMT's latest extreme and the IFVG inversion candle. Further apart = they do not pair.")
ifvgAfterSweep  = input.bool(true, "IFVG must form at/after the SMT", group = grpSignal, tooltip = "Off: the IFVG may also have formed up to N bars BEFORE the SMT appeared.")
signalMaxDays   = input.int(7, "Remove Buy/Sell marks after (days)", minval = 1, group = grpSignal, tooltip = "Only used when 'Keep marks on past bars' is OFF. Measured by timestamp from the signal bar.")

grpMtf = "8 · Multi-timeframe feeds (higher-TF SMTs & signals on lower charts)"
useMtf = input.bool(true, "Run the engine on extra (higher) timeframes", group = grpMtf, tooltip = "Each enabled feed runs the FULL SMT + IFVG engine on that timeframe's CLOSED candles (both markets) and draws its SMTs, IFVGs and Buy/Sell marks on the chart you are viewing, tagged with the feed timeframe (e.g. 'BUY 3m' on a 1m chart). A feed is skipped when it is not higher than the chart timeframe. Buy/Sell only fire from entry timeframes (30s/1/2/3/5m); a 15m feed still shows its SMTs. Feed marks appear on the first chart bar after the feed candle closes.")
useF1  = input.bool(true, "Use", inline = "f1", group = grpMtf)
tfF1   = input.timeframe("2", "Feed #1", inline = "f1", group = grpMtf, tooltip = "Feed #1: tick 'Use' and pick a timeframe HIGHER than the chart. In 'Resolved anchor' IFVG mode the 2m / 3m / 5m feeds also serve as the stacked-FVG escalation ladder.")
useF2  = input.bool(true, "Use", inline = "f2", group = grpMtf)
tfF2   = input.timeframe("3", "Feed #2", inline = "f2", group = grpMtf, tooltip = "Feed #2 (see Feed #1).")
useF3  = input.bool(true, "Use", inline = "f3", group = grpMtf)
tfF3   = input.timeframe("5", "Feed #3", inline = "f3", group = grpMtf, tooltip = "Feed #3 (see Feed #1).")
useF4  = input.bool(true, "Use", inline = "f4", group = grpMtf)
tfF4   = input.timeframe("15", "Feed #4", inline = "f4", group = grpMtf, tooltip = "Feed #4 (see Feed #1).")

grpP3 = "9 · Phase 3: HTF direction · displacement · sweep → SMT sequence"
htfDirFilter = input.string("OFF", "HTF Direction Filter", options = ["OFF", "REQUIRE SAME DIRECTION", "ALLOW OPPOSITE DIRECTION"], group = grpP3, tooltip = "Compares the LTF setup direction (bullish SMT + bullish IFVG) with the direction of the PRIMARY HTF zone (Phase 2 selection) recorded when the IFVG formed. REQUIRE SAME DIRECTION: the primary zone must have the same bias. ALLOW OPPOSITE DIRECTION / OFF: direction is not checked. The Phase 2 primary itself is unchanged.")
dispFilter   = input.string("OFF", "Displacement Filter", options = ["OFF", "OPTIONAL", "REQUIRED"], group = grpP3, tooltip = "Objective displacement, measured on the feed's own candles. OPTIONAL: computed and shown in debug / tooltips only. REQUIRED: a same-direction displacement event must exist at most 'Max bars displacement → IFVG' bars before (or on) the IFVG inversion candle. Defaults are starting values, not recommendations.")
dispAtrMultP3 = input.float(1.0, "  Displacement: body >= x ATR", minval = 0.0, step = 0.1, group = grpP3, tooltip = "ATR length = the shared 'ATR length' input (section 1b), computed on each feed's own timeframe. 0 disables this component.")
dispBodyPctP3 = input.float(0.60, "  Displacement: body / range >=", minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.05, group = grpP3, tooltip = "0 disables this component.")
dispConsec    = input.int(1, "  Required consecutive directional candles", minval = 1, group = grpP3, tooltip = "Every candle of the run must be directional (close > open for bullish, close < open for bearish) and meet the ATR / body thresholds. The event is recorded on the last candle of the run.")
dispReqSwing  = input.bool(false, "  Require swing break", group = grpP3, tooltip = "Bullish displacement must also close above the last confirmed feed swing high; bearish below the last confirmed feed swing low (same swings the MSS filter uses).")
dispMaxToIfvg = input.int(10, "  Max bars displacement → IFVG (0 = OFF)", minval = 0, group = grpP3, tooltip = "Feed bars from the displacement event to the IFVG inversion candle. Older displacement does not qualify the IFVG.")
seqFilter    = input.bool(false, "Require Liquidity → SMT Sequence", group = grpP3, tooltip = "ON: Buy/Sell only when the events happened in this order: liquidity sweep → SMT detection → SMT confirmation → displacement (if the displacement filter is REQUIRED) → LTF IFVG, each inside the windows below. OFF: Phase 2 behaviour. Skipped for signals that fire without an SMT ('Require SMT' OFF).")
seqMaxSweepSmt = input.int(0, "  Max bars sweep → SMT (0 = OFF)", minval = 0, group = grpP3, tooltip = "In this engine the SMT is detected on the sweep candle itself, so the distance is normally 0; the window is kept explicit and testable.")
seqMaxSmtDisp  = input.int(10, "  Max bars SMT confirmation → displacement / IFVG (0 = OFF)", minval = 0, group = grpP3, tooltip = "With the displacement filter REQUIRED: confirmation → displacement. Otherwise: confirmation → IFVG.")

grpRisk = "10 · Risk: stop loss / take profit / position size"
showTrade     = input.bool(true, "Draw entry / SL / TP lines on Buy/Sell", group = grpRisk, tooltip = "Draw the entry, stop and target lines plus the plan label (contracts, risk) for every Buy/Sell. The lines follow price and mark SL / TP hits.")
slMode        = input.string("Sweep High/Low", "Stop loss mode", options = ["Sweep High/Low", "IFVG High/Low"], group = grpRisk, tooltip = "Sweep High/Low: Long = lowest low of the SMT sweep leg (chart market), Short = highest high. IFVG High/Low: Long = bottom of the IFVG box, Short = top of the IFVG box. A signal without an SMT ('Require SMT' OFF) always uses the IFVG side.")
slBufTicks    = input.int(2, "Stop loss buffer (ticks)", minval = 0, group = grpRisk, tooltip = "Extra ticks added beyond the stop level.")
tpMode        = input.string("Fixed RR", "Take profit mode", options = ["Fixed RR", "HTF swing", "Fixed RR + HTF swing"], group = grpRisk, tooltip = "Fixed RR: TP1/TP2 at the risk:reward ratios below. HTF swing: the nearest UNSWEPT opposing liquidity beyond the entry (HTF swing / PDH / PDL / PWH / PWL, falling back to a feed swing, then to the last HTF pivot).")
tp1RR         = input.float(2.0, "TP1 risk:reward (1:x)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.5, group = grpRisk, tooltip = "First target at this multiple of the stop distance.")
tp2RR         = input.float(3.0, "TP2 risk:reward (1:x, 0 = off)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.5, group = grpRisk, tooltip = "Second target at this multiple of the stop distance. 0 = no TP2.")
tradeMaxBars  = input.int(200, "Close an open trade plan after (chart bars)", minval = 5, group = grpRisk, tooltip = "A plan that has hit neither its stop nor all its targets is marked EXPIRED after this many chart bars.")
maxPlans      = input.int(20, "Trade plans kept on the chart", minval = 1, maxval = 60, group = grpRisk, tooltip = "Older plans (lines + label) are deleted when more than this are on the chart.")
acctRisk      = input.float(100.0, "Account risk ($)", minval = 0.0, step = 10.0, group = grpRisk, tooltip = "Dollar amount you are willing to lose if the stop is hit.")
pointValue    = input.float(2.0, "Point value ($ per 1.0 point per contract)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.5, group = grpRisk, tooltip = "MNQ = 2, NQ = 20, MES = 5, ES = 50, MYM = 0.5, YM = 5. Contracts = Account risk / (stop distance in points x point value), rounded DOWN.")
autoPointValue = input.bool(false, "Use the symbol's own point value instead", group = grpRisk, tooltip = "On: ignores the field above and uses TradingView's syminfo.pointvalue for the chart symbol.")

// short name of the correlated market for labels / tooltips (needed by the draw helpers below)
corrName = str.contains(correlatedSym, ":") ? array.get(str.split(correlatedSym, ":"), 1) : correlatedSym

grpStrat = "S · Strategy (backtest only)"
s_from       = input.time(timestamp("2024-01-01T00:00:00"), "Test window start", group = grpStrat, tooltip = "Entries are only taken inside the window. Tune settings on one window (in-sample), then re-run on a later window the tuning never saw (out-of-sample) and keep only changes that hold up there.")
s_to         = input.time(timestamp("2030-01-01T00:00:00"), "Test window end", group = grpStrat)
s_qtyMode    = input.string("Risk module contracts", "Quantity", options = ["Risk module contracts", "Fixed 1 contract"], group = grpStrat, tooltip = "Risk module contracts = the count from section 10 (Account risk / (stop distance x point value)). 0 contracts = the signal is skipped, so set Account risk and Point value for the symbol you test.")
s_exitModel  = input.string("TP1", "Exit model", options = ["TP1", "TP2", "Swing TP (fallback TP1)", "Half at TP1, rest at TP2", "Stop / time only"], group = grpStrat, tooltip = "Which of the risk module's targets closes the trade. Every model uses the section 10 stop. Half at TP1 needs at least 2 contracts. Stop / time only = no target, the trade runs until the stop or the time stop.")
s_timeStop   = input.bool(true, "Time stop = 'Close an open trade plan after' bars", group = grpStrat, tooltip = "Closes the position at market after the section 10 'Close an open trade plan after (chart bars)' input.")
s_allowRev   = input.bool(false, "Opposite signal reverses an open position", group = grpStrat, tooltip = "Off: a signal against the open position is ignored. On: the position is closed and reversed.")
s_useAlerts  = input.bool(false, "Fire strategy order alerts", group = grpStrat, tooltip = "Adds strategy order events to 'Any alert() function call' alerts (for broker / webhook forwarding). The indicator alerts stay as they are.")

// ============================== TYPES ==============================
type RawFVG
    float top
    float bottom
    int   dir
    int   age
    int   id
    int   formBar
    float gapAtr
    float bodyRatio
    float rangeAtr
    int   formT

type IFVGZone
    bool   isBull
    float  top
    float  bottom
    int    invBar
    string htfTag
    string primaryTag = ""
    string resTf = ""
    int    fvgId
    bool   primaryBull = false
    int    dispBar
    int    dispTime
    bool   dispOk = false
    bool   used = false
    box    b
    // confluence score (section 1c), frozen on the inversion candle
    int    confScore = 0
    int    sHtf = 0
    int    sSmt = 0
    int    sSess = 0
    int    sDisp = 0
    int    sLiq = 0
    int    sStruct = 0
    string grade = "D"
    string sessName = ""

type HtfFVG
    bool   isBull
    float  top
    float  bottom
    string tf
    int    slot
    bool   used = false
    box    b
    // lifecycle (HZ_* constants) + HTF confluence eligibility.  top / bottom are the ORIGINAL
    // creation boundaries and are never changed; ce = (top + bottom) / 2 at creation.
    int    state = 0
    bool   eligible = true
    float  ce
    int    bornT
    int    firstTouchTime
    int    firstTouchBar
    float  firstTouchPrice
    int    firstCEHitTime
    int    firstCEHitBar
    bool   ceCloseBack = false
    // Phase 2: age (own-TF bars), first retest, primary-context flag.  Lifecycle 'eligible' above is
    // untouched; f_hzEligible() combines lifecycle AND age AND first retest.
    int    tfSec
    int    createdBar
    int    createdTime
    int    ageBars = 0
    bool   ageExpired = false
    bool   wasOutside = false
    bool   firstRetestAvailable = false
    bool   firstRetestUsed = false
    int    firstRetestTime
    int    firstRetestBar
    int    retestCount = 0
    bool   isPrimary = false
    // Selection engine (section 2b).  Displacement metrics are frozen at creation from the CLOSED HTF candles
    // that formed the gap (own-TF ATR); the scores are recomputed on every confirmed chart bar.
    bool   candidate = false
    bool   selected = true
    bool   hiddenBySel = false
    int    cluster = -1
    float  deepest = 0.0
    float  gapAtr
    float  rangeAtr
    float  bodyRatio
    float  relVol
    float  freshS = 0.0
    float  confS = 0.0
    float  dispS = 0.0
    float  tfS = 0.0
    float  score = 0.0

type SMTSetup
    bool   isBull
    string refName
    bool   isKey
    int    sweeper
    int    sweepBar
    int    legBar
    int    legTime
    float  legExt
    float  legPrice
    float  sweepExt
    float  lvlA
    int    lvlTime
    float  mssLevel
    bool   htfTap = false
    string htfTag = ""
    bool   active = true
    bool   confirmed = false
    bool   dispDone = false
    bool   fvgDone = false
    bool   mssDone = false
    bool   ifvgSeen = false
    bool   dead = false
    bool   expired = false
    bool   used = false
    string tip = ""
    string note = ""
    label  lbl
    line   ln
    int    anchorId = -1
    int    hostId = -1
    // fixed detection timestamp (never updated) + Phase 3 event layer
    int    detectTime
    int    sweepTime
    float  sweepPrice
    float  sweptLevel
    int    confirmBar
    int    confirmTime
    int    seq = 1
    bool   ageExpired = false
    // universal pivot SMT (section 3b): the level the failing market must not take, the correlated
    // market's two swing prices (for the marker) and the marker label itself
    bool   pivMode = false
    float  failLvl
    float  prevB
    float  curB
    label  mk

// one drawn SMT label per (direction, extreme price): other SMTs at the same edge join it
type SmtAnchor
    int    id
    bool   isBull
    float  price
    label  lbl
    string extra = ""
    bool   alive = true

type LiqRef
    string   name
    bool     isHigh
    int      kind = 0
    float    lvlA
    float    lvlB
    int      lvlBar
    int      lvlTime
    int      state = 3
    SMTSetup cur

// last confirmed swing of one pivot-SMT track (one per side and per anchoring market, in each engine):
// pA / pB = both markets' prices at that swing candle, bar / t = the swing candle (feed index / time)
type PivTrack
    float pA
    float pB
    int   bar
    int   t

type SigMark
    int   markBar
    int   markTime
    label lbl

// one closed candle of ONE timeframe for BOTH markets (what an engine consumes)
type Feed
    bool   isNew
    int    t
    int    tMid
    int    pivT
    float  o
    float  h
    float  l
    float  c
    float  h2
    float  l2
    float  atr
    float  phA
    float  plA
    float  winHiA
    float  winLoA
    float  postHiA
    float  postLoA
    float  ch
    float  cl
    float  phB
    float  plB
    float  winHiB
    float  winLoB
    float  postHiB
    float  postLoB
    float  corrTick
    // pivot SMT alignment (section 3b): both markets' extreme within +/- pivSync bars of the swing candle,
    // and their extreme over the bars AFTER that window up to the current candle
    float  pvHiA
    float  pvLoA
    float  pvHiB
    float  pvLoB
    float  pvPostHiA
    float  pvPostLoA
    float  pvPostHiB
    float  pvPostLoB

// the complete state of one SMT + IFVG engine (one per feed timeframe)
type Engine
    string tfName
    bool   enabled
    bool   entryTf
    bool   ifvgTf = false
    bool   isChart = false
    int    tfSec
    int    fvgSeq = 0
    string ifvgDbg = "-"
    bool   smtOk
    int    idx = 0
    array<RawFVG>   rawList
    array<IFVGZone> ifvgList
    array<SMTSetup> setups
    array<LiqRef>   refs
    int    lastRejBullBar
    int    lastRejBearBar
    int    lastBuyBar
    int    lastSellBar
    float  lastPHA
    float  lastPLA
    int    cntSmtDev = 0
    int    cntSmtConf = 0
    int    cntSmtInv = 0
    int    cntSmtExp = 0
    int    cntIfvgBull = 0
    int    cntIfvgBear = 0
    int    cntIfvgRej = 0
    int    cntIfvgOld = 0
    int    cntBuy = 0
    int    cntSell = 0
    string logSmt = "-"
    string logIfvg = "-"
    string logPair = "-"
    string lastIfvgTag = ""
    int    bullRun = 0
    int    bearRun = 0
    int    lastBullDispBar
    int    lastBullDispTime
    int    lastBearDispBar
    int    lastBearDispTime
    int    lastIfvgBar
    int    lastIfvgTime
    string lastSeq = "-"
    // last liquidity sweep by the CHART market per side (section 1c liquidity score): feed bar + external flag
    // (external = PDH/PDL/PWH/PWL/HTF swing, internal = feed swing / pivot)
    int    lastSweepHiBar
    bool   lastSweepHiExt = false
    int    lastSweepLoBar
    bool   lastSweepLoExt = false
    int    cntIfvgScoreRej = 0
    // universal pivot SMT tracks: highs / lows anchored on the chart market (A) and on the correlated market (B)
    int    cntPivSmt = 0
    PivTrack tHiA
    PivTrack tLoA
    PivTrack tHiB
    PivTrack tLoB

// what an engine hands back when it fires a Buy/Sell
type SigInfo
    bool   isBull
    string tfName
    float  entry
    float  slSweep
    float  slIfvg
    float  tpSwing
    string info
    string tag = ""

type TradePlan
    bool   isBull
    string tfName
    int    startBar
    float  entry
    float  sl
    float  tp1
    float  tp2
    float  tpSw
    int    contracts
    float  riskPts
    float  riskUsd
    string txt
    bool   open = true
    bool   tp1Hit = false
    bool   tp2Hit = false
    bool   swHit = false
    string status = "OPEN"
    line   lnE
    line   lnS
    line   lnT1
    line   lnT2
    line   lnSw
    label  lbl

// ============================== STATE ==============================
var array<HtfFVG>    htfList = array.new<HtfFVG>()
var array<SmtAnchor> smtAnchors = array.new<SmtAnchor>()
var array<int>       smtAnchorSeq = array.new_int(1, 0)
var array<SigMark>   sigList = array.new<SigMark>()
var array<TradePlan> plans   = array.new<TradePlan>()
var int    lastSigBar  = na
var bool   lastSigBull = false
var string lastSigTxt  = "No Trade"
var string lastPlanTxt = "-"
// last plan numbers [entry, sl, tp1, tp2, swing tp, contracts] (functions may mutate an array, not a global);
// read by the strategy twin generated from this file, harmless here
var array<float> lastPlan = array.new_float(6, na)
var int stratOrders = 0
var int stratSkipped = 0
chartMs = timeframe.in_seconds() * 1000
dayMs = 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000
// HTF FVG / NDOG lifecycle states
HZ_FRESH = 0
HZ_TOUCHED = 1
HZ_PARTIAL = 2
HZ_CE50 = 3
HZ_DEFENDED = 4
HZ_FILLED = 5
HZ_INVALID = 6

// ============================== HELPERS ==============================
f_minGapAtr() =>
    filterMode == "Off" ? 0.0 : filterMode == "Loose" ? 0.15 : filterMode == "Balanced" ? 0.25 : filterMode == "Strict" ? 0.40 : customMinGapAtr

f_minBodyRatio() =>
    filterMode == "Off" ? 0.0 : filterMode == "Loose" ? 0.40 : filterMode == "Balanced" ? 0.50 : filterMode == "Strict" ? 0.60 : customMinBodyRatio

f_minRangeAtr() =>
    filterMode == "Off" ? 0.0 : filterMode == "Loose" ? 0.40 : filterMode == "Balanced" ? 0.60 : filterMode == "Strict" ? 0.85 : customMinRangeAtr

f_breakBufferAtr() =>
    filterMode == "Off" ? 0.0 : filterMode == "Loose" ? 0.00 : filterMode == "Balanced" ? 0.05 : filterMode == "Strict" ? 0.10 : customBreakAtr

f_qualityPass(float gapAtrIn, float bodyRatioIn, float rangeAtrIn) =>
    bool gapOk = gapAtrIn >= f_minGapAtr()
    bool bodyOk = bodyRatioIn >= f_minBodyRatio()
    bool rangeOk = rangeAtrIn >= f_minRangeAtr()
    filterMode == "Off" or (gapOk and bodyOk and rangeOk)

// "30s", "1m", "3m", "15m", "1H", "4H", "1D", "1W" from any timeframe string
f_tfName(string tf) =>
    int sec = timeframe.in_seconds(tf)
    sec < 60 ? str.tostring(sec) + "s" : sec < 3600 ? str.tostring(sec / 60) + "m" : sec < 86400 ? str.tostring(sec / 3600) + "H" : sec < 604800 ? str.tostring(sec / 86400) + "D" : sec < 2419200 ? str.tostring(sec / 604800) + "W" : "M"

// label size from the dropdown text
f_size(string s) =>
    s == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : s == "Small" ? size.small : s == "Normal" ? size.normal : size.large

// entry timeframes: 30s, 1m, 2m, 3m, 5m
f_isEntryTf(int sec) =>
    sec == 30 or sec == 60 or sec == 120 or sec == 180 or sec == 300

// IFVG generation is allowed ONLY on 1m / 2m / 3m / 5m (HTF FVG scanning is not affected)
isIFVGAllowedTF(int sec) =>
    sec == 60 or sec == 120 or sec == 180 or sec == 300

// two price ranges overlap (touching at one boundary is NOT overlap)
fvgRangesOverlap(float aTop, float aBot, float bTop, float bBot) =>
    math.max(aBot, bBot) < math.min(aTop, bTop)

// indexes of the FVGs of ONE pool that the close c inverts (close through the far boundary + buffer),
// same direction as dirWanted (0 = any), inside the relevance window, and (optionally) overlapping [uBot, uTop]
getCandidateFVGs(array<RawFVG> pool, float c, float buf, int dirWanted, float uTop, float uBot, bool useUnion) =>
    array<int> out = array.new_int()
    for [i, rf] in pool
        bool inv = rf.dir == -1 ? c > rf.top + buf : c < rf.bottom - buf
        bool dOk = dirWanted == 0 or rf.dir == dirWanted
        bool uOk = not useUnion or fvgRangesOverlap(rf.top, rf.bottom, uTop, uBot)
        if inv and dOk and uOk and rf.age <= maxFvgToIfvgBars
            array.push(out, i)
    out

// is at least one pair of the candidates stacked (overlapping ranges)?
f_anyStacked(array<RawFVG> pool, array<int> idx) =>
    bool out = false
    int n = array.size(idx)
    if n > 1
        for i = 0 to n - 2
            RawFVG a = array.get(pool, array.get(idx, i))
            for j = i + 1 to n - 1
                RawFVG b = array.get(pool, array.get(idx, j))
                out := out or fvgRangesOverlap(a.top, a.bottom, b.top, b.bottom)
    out

// deterministic pick among candidates: most recent formation, then the larger gap
f_pickDeterministic(array<RawFVG> pool, array<int> idx) =>
    int best = -1
    for k in idx
        RawFVG a = array.get(pool, k)
        RawFVG b = array.get(pool, best < 0 ? k : best)
        best := best < 0 or a.formT > b.formT or (a.formT == b.formT and (a.top - a.bottom) > (b.top - b.bottom)) ? k : best
    best

// union range of the candidates
f_unionRange(array<RawFVG> pool, array<int> idx) =>
    float uTop = na
    float uBot = na
    for k in idx
        RawFVG a = array.get(pool, k)
        uTop := na(uTop) ? a.top : math.max(uTop, a.top)
        uBot := na(uBot) ? a.bottom : math.min(uBot, a.bottom)
    [uTop, uBot]

nameSw = f_tfName(swTf)

// length of one bar of an HTF slot, in seconds (slot 9 = NDOG = one trading day)
f_slotSec(int slot) =>
    slot == 1 ? timeframe.in_seconds(htfTf1) : slot == 2 ? timeframe.in_seconds(htfTf2) : slot == 3 ? timeframe.in_seconds(htfTf3) : slot == 4 ? timeframe.in_seconds(htfTf4) : slot == 5 ? timeframe.in_seconds(htfTf5) : slot == 6 ? timeframe.in_seconds(htfTf6) : slot == 7 ? timeframe.in_seconds(htfTf7) : slot == 8 ? timeframe.in_seconds(htfTf8) : 86400

// tags are stored as |5m|15m| so that "5m" is never confused with "15m"
f_tagAdd(string tag, string name) =>
    str.contains(tag, "|" + name + "|") ? tag : tag == "" ? "|" + name + "|" : tag + name + "|"

f_tagText(string tag) =>
    tag == "" ? "" : str.replace_all(str.substring(tag, 1, str.length(tag) - 1), "|", "+")

// does this SMT pass the enabled validity filter (key level)?
f_passes(SMTSetup s) =>
    bool keyOk = s.isKey or (keyHtfTap and s.htfTap)
    not keyFilter or keyOk

// confluence score of a signal: HTF gap + SMT + SMT confirmed + displacement + HTF direction aligned (0..5)
f_score(bool htf, bool smt, bool smtConf, bool disp, bool aligned) =>
    (htf ? 1 : 0) + (smt ? 1 : 0) + (smtConf ? 1 : 0) + (disp ? 1 : 0) + (aligned ? 1 : 0)

// swing structure of one market in a pivot SMT: HH / LH (bearish) or LL / HL (bullish)
f_pivStruct(bool isBull, int sweeper, bool forA) =>
    bool madeIt = forA ? sweeper == 1 : sweeper == 2
    isBull ? (madeIt ? "LL" : "HL") : (madeIt ? "HH" : "LH")

f_lineStyle(string s) =>
    s == "Dashed" ? line.style_dashed : s == "Dotted" ? line.style_dotted : line.style_solid

// ---- IFVG confluence score: grade, color, gate (score = rule-based confluence, not a probability) ----
f_getIFVGGrade(int s) =>
    s >= 90 ? "A+" : s >= 80 ? "A" : s >= 70 ? "B" : s >= 60 ? "C" : "D"

f_getIFVGColor(string g, color base) =>
    not i_colorByIFVGScore ? base : g == "A+" or g == "A" ? color.new(color.lime, 75) : g == "B" ? color.new(color.blue, 75) : g == "C" ? color.new(color.orange, 75) : color.new(color.gray, 80)

f_ifvgPassesThreshold(int s) =>
    s >= i_minProbScore

// compact machine-readable tag for the strategy trade list: score, components, session, HTF, SMT
f_ifvgLogTag(IFVGZone z, string smtName, string tf) =>
    tf + "|S" + str.tostring(z.confScore) + z.grade + "|H" + str.tostring(z.sHtf) + "|M" + str.tostring(z.sSmt) + "|K" + str.tostring(z.sSess) + "|D" + str.tostring(z.sDisp) + "|L" + str.tostring(z.sLiq) + "|T" + str.tostring(z.sStruct) + "|htf:" + (z.htfTag != "" ? f_tagText(z.htfTag) : "-") + "|P:" + (z.primaryTag != "" ? z.primaryTag : "-") + "|sess:" + (z.sessName != "" ? z.sessName : "-") + "|smt:" + smtName

f_ifvgScoreText(IFVGZone z, bool breakdown) =>
    string out = z.grade + " " + str.tostring(z.confScore) + "/100"
    out += not breakdown ? "" : "\nHTF " + str.tostring(z.sHtf) + "/25 · SMT " + str.tostring(z.sSmt) + "/20 · Session " + str.tostring(z.sSess) + "/15" + (z.sessName != "" ? " (" + z.sessName + ")" : "") + "\nDisplacement " + str.tostring(z.sDisp) + "/15 · Liquidity " + str.tostring(z.sLiq) + "/15 · Structure " + str.tostring(z.sStruct) + "/10"
    out

// ---- HTF FVG / NDOG lifecycle ----
//   FRESH -> TOUCHED -> PARTIALLY_MITIGATED -> CE_50_MITIGATED -> DEFENDED / FILLED (-> INVALIDATED)
// Evaluated on every CONFIRMED chart bar with that bar's own OHLC (no lookahead).  CE is the fixed
// 50% of the ORIGINAL gap.  DEFENDED / FILLED / INVALIDATED zones keep their box (existing rules)
// but lose HTF-confluence eligibility.  Existing 'removed when price' invalidation is untouched.
f_hzStateName(int st) =>
    st == HZ_FRESH ? "FRESH" : st == HZ_TOUCHED ? "TOUCHED" : st == HZ_PARTIAL ? "PARTIAL" : st == HZ_CE50 ? "CE50" : st == HZ_DEFENDED ? "DEFENDED" : st == HZ_FILLED ? "FILLED" : "INVALIDATED"

f_hzVisual(HtfFVG z) =>
    if not na(z.b) and not z.hiddenBySel
        box.set_text(z.b, z.tf + " · " + f_hzStateName(z.state) + (z.ageExpired ? " · AGED" : ""))
        if not z.eligible or z.ageExpired
            box.set_border_style(z.b, line.style_dashed)
    true

f_hzSetState(HtfFVG z, int st) =>
    if st != z.state
        z.state := st
        z.eligible := z.eligible and st < HZ_DEFENDED
        f_hzVisual(z)
    true

// one confirmed chart bar (o/h/l/c, chart ATR) against one zone
f_hzUpdate(HtfFVG z, float o, float h, float l, float c, float atrV) =>
    // deepest penetration of the ORIGINAL gap so far (0 = untouched, 1 = traded through), for the freshness score
    float gapH = math.max(z.top - z.bottom, syminfo.mintick)
    float pen = z.isBull ? (z.top - l) / gapH : (h - z.bottom) / gapH
    z.deepest := math.max(z.deepest, math.min(1.0, pen))
    if z.state < HZ_FILLED
        bool touched = z.isBull ? l <= z.top : h >= z.bottom
        bool ceHit = z.isBull ? l <= z.ce : h >= z.ce
        bool filled = z.isBull ? l <= z.bottom : h >= z.top
        bool closedInGap = c <= z.top and c >= z.bottom
        float edge = z.isBull ? l : h
        // first interaction / first CE hit: recorded once, never overwritten
        if touched and na(z.firstTouchBar)
            z.firstTouchTime := time
            z.firstTouchBar := bar_index
            z.firstTouchPrice := edge
        if ceHit and na(z.firstCEHitBar)
            z.firstCEHitTime := time
            z.firstCEHitBar := bar_index
        if filled
            f_hzSetState(z, HZ_FILLED)
        else if z.state < HZ_DEFENDED
            if ceHit and z.state < HZ_CE50
                f_hzSetState(z, HZ_CE50)
            else if touched and z.state < HZ_CE50
                f_hzSetState(z, closedInGap ? HZ_PARTIAL : math.max(z.state, HZ_TOUCHED))
            // rejection / defense test: on the CE-hit bar and every bar after it
            if z.state == HZ_CE50
                bool defSide = z.isBull ? c > z.ce : c < z.ce
                float body = math.abs(c - o)
                float rng = math.max(h - l, syminfo.mintick)
                float safeAtr = na(atrV) or atrV <= 0.0 ? syminfo.mintick : atrV
                bool dispAway = body >= dispAtrMult * safeAtr and body / rng >= dispBodyRatio and (z.isBull ? c > o : c < o)
                bool defended = htfCeMethod == "Wick Rejection" ? ceHit and defSide : htfCeMethod == "Close Back Across CE" ? defSide : htfCeMethod == "Displacement Away From CE" ? dispAway : dispAway and (defSide or z.ceCloseBack)
                z.ceCloseBack := z.ceCloseBack or defSide
                if defended
                    f_hzSetState(z, HZ_DEFENDED)
    // ---- Phase 2a: first retest = OUTSIDE -> INSIDE transition (never the creation bar) ----
    bool inside = h >= z.bottom and l <= z.top
    bool outside = not inside
    if inside and z.wasOutside
        z.retestCount := z.retestCount + 1
        if not z.firstRetestAvailable and not z.firstRetestUsed
            z.firstRetestAvailable := true
            z.firstRetestTime := time
            z.firstRetestBar := bar_index
        else if z.firstRetestAvailable
            z.firstRetestUsed := true
    z.firstRetestUsed := z.firstRetestUsed or (outside and z.firstRetestAvailable and z.retestCount > 0)
    z.wasOutside := outside
    // ---- Phase 2b: age in the zone's OWN timeframe bars (timestamp based, never chart bars) ----
    if not na(z.createdTime) and not na(z.tfSec) and z.tfSec > 0
        z.ageBars := int(math.floor((time - z.createdTime) / (z.tfSec * 1000)))
        bool wasExp = z.ageExpired
        z.ageExpired := htfMaxAgeBars > 0 and z.ageBars > htfMaxAgeBars
        if z.ageExpired and not wasExp
            f_hzVisual(z)
    true

// ---- final HTF eligibility = lifecycle AND age AND first retest (each switchable, lifecycle state untouched) ----
f_hzLifeOk(HtfFVG z) =>
    not htfEligOn or z.eligible

f_hzAgeOk(HtfFVG z) =>
    htfMaxAgeBars == 0 or not z.ageExpired

f_hzRetestOk(HtfFVG z) =>
    not htfFirstRetest or (z.firstRetestAvailable and not z.firstRetestUsed)

// candidate for the selection engine = the existing lifecycle AND age AND first-retest rules
f_hzCandidate(HtfFVG z) =>
    f_hzLifeOk(z) and f_hzAgeOk(z) and f_hzRetestOk(z)

// does this zone count for HTF confluence right now?  candidate AND selected by the selection engine
// (section 2b): this is the single gate every downstream consumer (IFVG-in-HTF test, SMT tap, primary
// context, used-marking, checklist) goes through, so a non-selected overlapping zone can never fire anything.
f_hzEligible(HtfFVG z) =>
    f_hzCandidate(z) and z.selected

// 50% consequent encroachment of a zone (fixed at creation, kept as a function for the CE selection mode)
f_getConsequentEncroachment(HtfFVG z) =>
    z.ce

// two zones overlap (touching at one boundary is NOT overlap)
f_isOverlapping(HtfFVG a, HtfFVG b) =>
    math.max(a.bottom, b.bottom) < math.min(a.top, b.top)

// selection visuals: reuse the existing box, never create / delete.  Hidden = fully transparent, no text;
// selected candidate = 2-px border; everything else = the existing lifecycle visuals (f_hzVisual).
f_hzApplySelection(HtfFVG z) =>
    if not na(z.b)
        color clr = z.isBull ? htfBull : htfBear
        bool hide = i_htfHideLosers and z.candidate and not z.selected
        if hide != z.hiddenBySel
            z.hiddenBySel := hide
            box.set_bgcolor(z.b, hide ? color.new(clr, 100) : clr)
            box.set_border_color(z.b, hide ? color.new(clr, 100) : clr)
            box.set_text(z.b, "")
            f_hzVisual(z)
        box.set_border_width(z.b, not hide and z.candidate and z.selected ? 2 : 1)
    true

// ---- Phase 2c: PRIMARY zone among eligible zones overlapping [bot, top] at reference price 'px' ----
// Deterministic hierarchy: (1) eligible, (2) higher timeframe, (3) more recent creation,
// (4) smaller |px - CE|, (5) more recent first interaction.  Returns the list index or -1.
f_hzBetter(HtfFVG a, HtfFVG b, float px) =>
    float da = math.abs(px - a.ce)
    float db = math.abs(px - b.ce)
    a.tfSec != b.tfSec ? a.tfSec > b.tfSec : a.createdTime != b.createdTime ? a.createdTime > b.createdTime : da != db ? da < db : nz(a.firstTouchTime, 0) > nz(b.firstTouchTime, 0)

// does an ELIGIBLE zone match the IFVG box [bot, top] under the direction / containment inputs?
f_hzMatch(HtfFVG z, float top, float bot, bool isBull) =>
    bool dirOk = not htfMatchDir or z.isBull == isBull
    bool inside = bot >= z.bottom and top <= z.top
    bool overlap = top >= z.bottom and bot <= z.top
    dirOk and (htfContain == "Fully inside" ? inside : overlap) and f_hzEligible(z)

f_htfPrimaryIdx(float top, float bot, bool isBull, float px) =>
    int best = -1
    for [i, z] in htfList
        if f_hzMatch(z, top, bot, isBull) and (best < 0 or f_hzBetter(z, array.get(htfList, best), px))
            best := i
    best

// tag of the primary zone for an IFVG box (context only; the signal still accepts any eligible zone)
f_htfPrimaryTag(float top, float bot, bool isBull, float px) =>
    int idx = f_htfPrimaryIdx(top, bot, isBull, px)
    idx >= 0 ? array.get(htfList, idx).tf : ""

// direction of that primary zone (true = bullish); false when there is none
f_htfPrimaryBull(float top, float bot, bool isBull, float px) =>
    int idx = f_htfPrimaryIdx(top, bot, isBull, px)
    idx >= 0 ? array.get(htfList, idx).isBull : false

// tags of ELIGIBLE HTF zones whose area overlaps [lo, hi] (a "tap")
f_htfOverlap(float lo, float hi, bool isBull) =>
    string tag = ""
    for z in htfList
        bool dirOk = not htfMatchDir or z.isBull == isBull
        bool hit = hi >= z.bottom and lo <= z.top
        tag := dirOk and hit and f_hzEligible(z) ? f_tagAdd(tag, z.tf) : tag
    tag

// tags of ELIGIBLE HTF zones that contain the IFVG box (overlapping or fully inside)
f_htfContain(float top, float bot, bool isBull) =>
    string tag = ""
    for z in htfList
        tag := f_hzMatch(z, top, bot, isBull) ? f_tagAdd(tag, z.tf) : tag
    tag

// remember which HTF zones a signal used (so their boxes can stay on the chart)
f_markHtfUsed(float top, float bot, bool isBull) =>
    for z in htfList
        z.used := z.used or f_hzMatch(z, top, bot, isBull)
    true

// an HTF FVG box leaves the active list: freeze it at the current bar (keep) or delete it.
// Boxes are time-anchored (xloc.bar_time), so the right edge is a TIME, never a bar_index.
f_retireHtfBox(box b, bool keep) =>
    if not na(b) and keep and htfExtendMode == "Extend with price"
        box.set_right(b, time)
    if not keep
        box.delete(b)
    true

// keep only the newest htfMaxPerTf zones of one HTF slot
f_capHtf(int slot) =>
    int kept = 0
    if array.size(htfList) > 0
        for i = array.size(htfList) - 1 to 0
            HtfFVG z = array.get(htfList, i)
            if z.slot == slot
                kept += 1
                if kept > htfMaxPerTf
                    f_retireHtfBox(z.b, keepHistory and z.used)
                    array.remove(htfList, i)
    true

// zones older than htfMaxDays (timestamp from the chart bar that created them) leave the active list
f_expireHtfByDays() =>
    if array.size(htfList) > 0
        for i = array.size(htfList) - 1 to 0
            HtfFVG z = array.get(htfList, i)
            if not na(z.bornT) and time - z.bornT > htfMaxDays * dayMs
                f_retireHtfBox(z.b, keepHistory and z.used)
                array.remove(htfList, i)
    true

// remove zones of ONE HTF slot only when THAT slot's own just-closed bar invalidates them.
// isNew is only true once per closed bar of that specific timeframe, so a 1m candle can never
// trigger this for a 1H zone -- only an actual closed 1H candle (hC/lC/cC = that 1H bar's own
// high/low/close) can.
f_invalidateHtf(int slot, bool isNew, float hC, float lC, float cC) =>
    if isNew and array.size(htfList) > 0
        for i = array.size(htfList) - 1 to 0
            HtfFVG hz = array.get(htfList, i)
            bool hzMit = htfInvalidate == "Close through" ? (hz.isBull ? cC < hz.bottom : cC > hz.top) : (hz.isBull ? lC < hz.bottom : hC > hz.top)
            if hz.slot == slot and hzMit
                f_hzSetState(hz, HZ_INVALID)
                f_retireHtfBox(hz.b, keepHistory and hz.used)
                array.remove(htfList, i)
    true

// a new HTF bar just opened -> look at the three closed HTF bars before it
//   hC / lC   = candle 3 (last closed HTF bar),   hA / lA = candle 1 (two bars before it)
//   tA / tM   = OPEN time of candle 1 / candle 2,  tcC     = CLOSE time of candle 3
// The box is anchored with xloc.bar_time on those historical candles, so it sits on the gap
// candle on ANY chart timeframe instead of starting at the current bar and floating ahead of price.
f_addHtf(bool isNew, bool en, string name, int slot, float hC, float lC, float hA, float lA, int tA, int tM, int tcC, float o2, float h2, float l2, float c2, float atr2, float v2, float va2) =>
    bool valid = isNew and en and not na(hC) and not na(lC) and not na(hA) and not na(lA) and not na(tA) and not na(tM) and not na(tcC)
    // displacement metrics of the gap candle (candle 2), normalised by that timeframe's own ATR
    float atrS = na(atr2) or atr2 <= 0.0 ? na : atr2
    float rng2 = na(h2) or na(l2) ? na : math.max(h2 - l2, syminfo.mintick)
    float rangeAtr2 = na(atrS) or na(rng2) ? na : rng2 / atrS
    float bodyR2 = na(rng2) or na(o2) or na(c2) ? na : math.abs(c2 - o2) / rng2
    float relV2 = na(v2) or na(va2) or va2 <= 0.0 ? na : v2 / va2
    float minGap = htfMinGapTicks * syminfo.mintick
    bool bullGap = valid and lC > hA and (lC - hA) >= minGap
    bool bearGap = valid and hC < lA and (lA - hC) >= minGap
    box hbBull = na
    box hbBear = na
    int leftT = htfAnchor == "Candle 1 (first of the 3)" ? tA : tM
    int rightT = htfExtendMode == "Extend with price" ? time + fvgExtend * chartMs : tcC
    if bullGap
        if showHTF
            hbBull := box.new(left = leftT, top = lC, right = rightT, bottom = hA, xloc = xloc.bar_time, border_color = htfBull, bgcolor = htfBull, text = name, text_size = size.small, text_color = color.new(color.white, 10), text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top)
        array.push(htfList, HtfFVG.new(isBull = true, top = lC, bottom = hA, tf = name, slot = slot, b = hbBull, ce = (lC + hA) / 2, bornT = time, tfSec = f_slotSec(slot), createdBar = bar_index, createdTime = time, gapAtr = na(atrS) ? na : (lC - hA) / atrS, rangeAtr = rangeAtr2, bodyRatio = bodyR2, relVol = relV2))
    if bearGap
        if showHTF
            hbBear := box.new(left = leftT, top = lA, right = rightT, bottom = hC, xloc = xloc.bar_time, border_color = htfBear, bgcolor = htfBear, text = name, text_size = size.small, text_color = color.new(color.white, 10), text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top)
        array.push(htfList, HtfFVG.new(isBull = false, top = lA, bottom = hC, tf = name, slot = slot, b = hbBear, ce = (lA + hC) / 2, bornT = time, tfSec = f_slotSec(slot), createdBar = bar_index, createdTime = time, gapAtr = na(atrS) ? na : (lA - hC) / atrS, rangeAtr = rangeAtr2, bodyRatio = bodyR2, relVol = relV2))
    if bullGap or bearGap
        f_capHtf(slot)
    true

// NDOG = New Day Opening Gap: previous day's last close -> new day's first open, read from the chart's
// own confirmed bars (slot 9).  Gap up = bullish zone (support), gap down = bearish (resistance).
f_addNdog(bool newDay, float prevClose, float dayOpen, float atrC) =>
    bool valid = useNdog and newDay and not na(prevClose) and not na(dayOpen)
    float minGap = htfMinGapTicks * syminfo.mintick
    bool gapUp = valid and dayOpen > prevClose and (dayOpen - prevClose) >= minGap
    bool gapDn = valid and dayOpen < prevClose and (prevClose - dayOpen) >= minGap
    if gapUp or gapDn
        float top = gapUp ? dayOpen : prevClose
        float bot = gapUp ? prevClose : dayOpen
        color clr = gapUp ? htfBull : htfBear
        int rightT = htfExtendMode == "Extend with price" ? time + fvgExtend * chartMs : time_close
        box nb = na
        if showHTF
            nb := box.new(left = time, top = top, right = rightT, bottom = bot, xloc = xloc.bar_time, border_color = clr, bgcolor = clr, text = "NDOG", text_size = size.small, text_color = color.new(color.white, 10), text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top)
        array.push(htfList, HtfFVG.new(isBull = gapUp, top = top, bottom = bot, tf = "NDOG", slot = 9, b = nb, ce = (top + bot) / 2, bornT = time, tfSec = 86400, createdBar = bar_index, createdTime = time, gapAtr = na(atrC) or atrC <= 0.0 ? na : (top - bot) / atrC))
        f_capHtf(9)
    true

withinLookback(int refBar) =>
    not na(refBar) and (bar_index - refBar) <= confluenceBars

// is an IFVG that formed on invBar close enough in time to this SMT?
f_timingOk(SMTSetup s, int invBar) =>
    bool okAfter = invBar >= s.sweepBar and invBar - s.legBar <= confluenceBars
    bool okBefore = invBar < s.sweepBar and s.sweepBar - invBar <= confluenceBars
    ifvgAfterSweep ? okAfter : okAfter or okBefore

// is there already an unswept reference at (about) this level pair?
f_hasRef(array<LiqRef> refs, bool isHigh, int kind, float a, float b, float tA, float tB) =>
    bool found = false
    for q in refs
        found := found or (q.kind == kind and q.isHigh == isHigh and q.state == 0 and math.abs(q.lvlA - a) <= tA and math.abs(q.lvlB - b) <= tB)
    found

// add a swing reference (kind 1 = feed-TF swing, 2 = HTF swing) and trim the pool
f_addSwingRef(array<LiqRef> refs, bool isHigh, int kind, float a, float b, int atBar, int atTime, float tA, float tB) =>
    bool dup = f_hasRef(refs, isHigh, kind, a, b, tA, tB)
    string nm = kind == 2 ? nameSw + " Swing" : "Swing"
    int cap = kind == 2 ? htfSwingMaxRefs : swingMaxRefs
    int kept = 0
    if not dup
        array.push(refs, LiqRef.new(name = nm, isHigh = isHigh, kind = kind, lvlA = a, lvlB = b, lvlBar = atBar, lvlTime = atTime, state = 0))
        for i = array.size(refs) - 1 to 0
            LiqRef q = array.get(refs, i)
            if q.kind == kind and q.isHigh == isHigh
                kept += 1
                if kept > cap and q.state != 1
                    array.remove(refs, i)
    true

// TAKE-PROFIT TARGET from liquidity: the nearest UNSWEPT opposing level beyond the entry.
//   long  -> nearest unswept high above entry, short -> nearest unswept low below entry
//   priority: major (HTF swing / PDH / PDL / PWH / PWL) > feed swing > last HTF pivot (fbH / fbL)
f_swingTarget(array<LiqRef> refs, bool isBull, float entry, float fbH, float fbL) =>
    float major = na
    float minor = na
    for q in refs
        bool sideOk = q.isHigh == isBull
        bool beyond = isBull ? q.lvlA > entry : q.lvlA < entry
        if sideOk and beyond and q.state == 0 and not na(q.lvlA)
            float cur = q.kind != 1 ? major : minor
            float nxt = na(cur) ? q.lvlA : (isBull ? math.min(cur, q.lvlA) : math.max(cur, q.lvlA))
            major := q.kind != 1 ? nxt : major
            minor := q.kind != 1 ? minor : nxt
    float fb = isBull ? fbH : fbL
    float fbOk = not na(fb) and (isBull ? fb > entry : fb < entry) ? fb : na
    na(major) ? (na(minor) ? fbOk : minor) : major

// why has this SMT not produced a signal (yet)?
f_reason(Engine e, SMTSetup s) =>
    string out = ""
    int rej = s.isBull ? e.lastRejBullBar : e.lastRejBearBar
    bool rejHit = not na(rej) and rej >= s.sweepBar and rej - s.legBar <= confluenceBars
    bool keyOk = s.isKey or (keyHtfTap and s.htfTap)
    out += reqConfirmedSMT and not s.confirmed ? "SMT not confirmed yet; " : ""
    out += keyFilter and not keyOk ? "not at key level; " : ""
    out += reqDisp and not s.dispDone ? "no displacement; " : ""
    out += reqSetupFvg and not s.fvgDone ? "no FVG after sweep; " : ""
    out += reqMSS and not s.mssDone ? "no MSS; " : ""
    out += s.note != "" ? s.note + "; " : not s.ifvgSeen ? (rejHit ? "IFVG failed quality filter; " : "no IFVG yet; ") : ""
    out == "" ? "IFVG closed back through or expired; " : out

// one-line status of an engine for the tables
f_engSummary(Engine e) =>
    not e.enabled ? e.tfName + ": off" : e.tfName + ": smt " + str.tostring(e.cntSmtConf) + "/" + str.tostring(e.cntSmtDev) + (e.entryTf ? " buy " + str.tostring(e.cntBuy) + " sell " + str.tostring(e.cntSell) : " (SMT only)")

// ---- SMT label de-duplication by extreme edge ----
// One label per (direction, extreme price).  A later SMT at the same edge (another reference, another
// engine timeframe) is appended to that label instead of drawing an overlapping one.  Labels only.
f_anchorGet(int id) =>
    SmtAnchor out = na
    for a in smtAnchors
        if a.id == id and id >= 0
            out := a
    out

f_anchorFind(bool isBull, float price) =>
    int out = -1
    float tol = smtMergeTicks * syminfo.mintick + syminfo.mintick * 0.01
    for a in smtAnchors
        if out < 0 and a.alive and a.isBull == isBull and not na(a.lbl) and math.abs(a.price - price) <= tol
            out := a.id
    out

f_anchorNew(bool isBull, float price, label lb) =>
    if array.size(smtAnchors) > 0
        for i = array.size(smtAnchors) - 1 to 0
            SmtAnchor a = array.get(smtAnchors, i)
            if not a.alive
                array.remove(smtAnchors, i)
    int id = array.get(smtAnchorSeq, 0) + 1
    array.set(smtAnchorSeq, 0, id)
    array.push(smtAnchors, SmtAnchor.new(id = id, isBull = isBull, price = price, lbl = lb))
    while array.size(smtAnchors) > 200
        array.shift(smtAnchors)
    id

f_anchorKill(int id) =>
    SmtAnchor a = f_anchorGet(id)
    if not na(a)
        a.alive := false
    true

// ---- methods that change objects ----
// label.delete / line.delete / box.delete accept na, so no guards are needed
method kill(SMTSetup this) =>
    this.dead := true
    label.delete(this.lbl)
    this.lbl := na
    line.delete(this.ln)
    this.ln := na
    label.delete(this.mk)
    this.mk := na
    f_anchorKill(this.anchorId)
    true

// (re)arm a fixed level reference (PDH, PDL, PWH, PWL) with fresh levels
method arm(LiqRef this, float a, float b, int atBar, int atTime) =>
    bool ok = not na(a) and not na(b)
    if ok and this.state == 1
        if not na(this.cur)
            this.cur.kill()
        this.state := 3
    if ok
        this.lvlA := a
        this.lvlB := b
        this.lvlBar := atBar
        this.lvlTime := atTime
        this.state := 0
    true

// draw / update / remove the label + connector of one SMT depending on the filters.
// Everything is TIME-anchored (xloc.bar_time) so an SMT found by a 15m feed lands on the right
// candle of a 1m chart.  With 'Show SMT label shapes' OFF the label keeps its text (in the SMT
// color) but uses label.style_none, so nothing else (line, tooltip, logs, engine) changes.
method draw(SMTSetup this, Engine e) =>
    bool keyOk = this.isKey or (keyHtfTap and this.htfTap)
    bool pass = f_passes(this)
    bool showOk = showSMT and e.smtOk and not this.dead and pass and (this.confirmed or showDeveloping)
    bool showRej = showSMT and e.smtOk and not this.dead and not pass and showRejected
    color base = showRej ? color.gray : this.isBull ? smtBullClr : smtBearClr
    color col = not this.confirmed and not showRej ? color.new(base, 60) : base
    string rejTxt = keyFilter and not keyOk ? "KEY " : ""
    string head = showRej ? "SMT✗ " + rejTxt : "SMT" + (this.confirmed ? "" : "?")
    string txt = head + " [" + e.tfName + "] · " + this.refName + (this.htfTag != "" ? " · @" + f_tagText(this.htfTag) : "")
    string tt = "Timeframe: " + e.tfName + "\n" + this.tip + (showRej ? "\nHIDDEN BY FILTER: " + rejTxt : "")
    string sty = not showSmtShapes ? label.style_none : this.isBull ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down
    color txtCol = showSmtShapes ? color.white : col
    if showOk or showRej
        // de-duplication: a new label at an extreme that already carries a live SMT label joins that label
        if smtMerge and showOk and na(this.lbl) and this.hostId < 0
            int hid = f_anchorFind(this.isBull, this.legPrice)
            if hid >= 0 and hid != this.anchorId
                SmtAnchor host = f_anchorGet(hid)
                if not na(host)
                    this.hostId := hid
                    string add = " +" + this.refName + "[" + e.tfName + "]"
                    host.extra := host.extra + add
                    label.set_text(host.lbl, label.get_text(host.lbl) + add)
        if this.hostId >= 0
            SmtAnchor hostA = f_anchorGet(this.hostId)
            if na(hostA) or not hostA.alive or na(hostA.lbl)
                this.hostId := -1
        if this.hostId < 0
            string extraTxt = ""
            if this.anchorId >= 0
                SmtAnchor own = f_anchorGet(this.anchorId)
                if not na(own)
                    extraTxt := own.extra
            string txtAll = txt + extraTxt
            if na(this.lbl)
                this.lbl := label.new(x = this.legTime, y = this.legPrice, text = txtAll, xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = sty, color = col, textcolor = txtCol, size = f_size(smtLabelSize), tooltip = tt)
            else
                label.set_xy(this.lbl, this.legTime, this.legPrice)
                label.set_text(this.lbl, txtAll)
                label.set_color(this.lbl, col)
                label.set_textcolor(this.lbl, txtCol)
                label.set_tooltip(this.lbl, tt)
            if smtMerge and showOk
                if this.anchorId < 0
                    this.anchorId := f_anchorNew(this.isBull, this.legPrice, this.lbl)
                else
                    SmtAnchor own2 = f_anchorGet(this.anchorId)
                    if not na(own2)
                        own2.price := this.legPrice
                        own2.lbl := this.lbl
                        own2.alive := true
        // connector: swept level -> sweep extreme (sweep SMT) or previous swing -> new swing (pivot SMT trendline)
        bool lineOn = this.pivMode ? pivShowLine : showSmtLines
        string lsty = this.pivMode ? f_lineStyle(pivLineStyle) : line.style_dotted
        int lw = this.pivMode ? pivLineWidth : 1
        if showOk and lineOn and not na(this.lvlTime)
            if na(this.ln)
                this.ln := line.new(this.lvlTime, this.lvlA, this.legTime, this.legPrice, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = col, width = lw, style = lsty)
            else
                line.set_xy1(this.ln, this.lvlTime, this.lvlA)
                line.set_xy2(this.ln, this.legTime, this.legPrice)
                line.set_color(this.ln, col)
        else
            line.delete(this.ln)
            this.ln := na
        // pivot SMT marker: the correlated market's side of the divergence, written at the previous swing
        if showOk and this.pivMode and pivShowMarker and not na(this.lvlTime)
            string mkTxt = "◆ " + corrName + " " + str.tostring(this.prevB, format.mintick) + " → " + str.tostring(this.curB, format.mintick) + " " + f_pivStruct(this.isBull, this.sweeper, false)
            if na(this.mk)
                this.mk := label.new(x = this.lvlTime, y = this.lvlA, text = mkTxt, xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = this.isBull ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = color.new(col, 100), textcolor = col, size = size.tiny, tooltip = tt)
            else
                label.set_xy(this.mk, this.lvlTime, this.lvlA)
                label.set_text(this.mk, mkTxt)
                label.set_textcolor(this.mk, col)
                label.set_tooltip(this.mk, tt)
        else
            label.delete(this.mk)
            this.mk := na
    else
        label.delete(this.lbl)
        this.lbl := na
        line.delete(this.ln)
        this.ln := na
        label.delete(this.mk)
        this.mk := na
        f_anchorKill(this.anchorId)
    true

// ---- universal pivot SMT (section 3b) ----
// One confirmed swing of one track against the previous swing of the same track.  A track = one side
// (high / low) anchored on one market: vA / vB are both markets' prices on the swing candle (the anchoring
// market's pivot, the other market's aligned extreme); postA / postB are their extremes over the bars after
// that candle up to now.  Bearish: one market's higher high while the other fails to make one.  Bullish:
// one market's lower low while the other fails to make one.  The failing market must not have taken its
// previous swing since (postA / postB), otherwise both took it and there is no SMT.  Creates the SMTSetup
// (same pipeline as the sweep SMTs) or returns na; the track always moves to the new swing.
f_pivSmt(Engine e, Feed f, PivTrack tr, bool isHigh, float vA, float vB, float postA, float postB, int pivIdx, int pivT, float tolA, float tolB) =>
    SMTSetup out = na
    bool ok = not na(vA) and not na(vB)
    if ok and not na(tr.pA) and not na(tr.pB) and not na(tr.bar) and pivIdx > tr.bar and (pivMaxGap == 0 or pivIdx - tr.bar <= pivMaxGap)
        bool aBeyond = isHigh ? vA > tr.pA + tolA : vA < tr.pA - tolA
        bool bBeyond = isHigh ? vB > tr.pB + tolB : vB < tr.pB - tolB
        bool aTookSince = not na(postA) and (isHigh ? postA > tr.pA + tolA : postA < tr.pA - tolA)
        bool bTookSince = not na(postB) and (isHigh ? postB > tr.pB + tolB : postB < tr.pB - tolB)
        int sw = aBeyond and not bBeyond and not bTookSince ? 1 : bBeyond and not aBeyond and not aTookSince ? 2 : 0
        if sw > 0
            bool sBull = not isHigh
            // one pivot SMT per (direction, swing): the other market anchoring the same swing does not add another
            bool dup = false
            for q in e.setups
                dup := dup or (q.pivMode and q.isBull == sBull and not q.dead and not q.expired and math.abs(q.sweepBar - pivIdx) <= pivotRight)
            if not dup
                float ext = sw == 1 ? vA : vB
                float fail = sw == 1 ? tr.pB : tr.pA
                string swName = sw == 1 ? syminfo.ticker : corrName
                string flName = sw == 1 ? corrName : syminfo.ticker
                string sA = f_pivStruct(sBull, sw, true)
                string sB = f_pivStruct(sBull, sw, false)
                string nm = "Pivot " + sA + "/" + sB
                string tap = f_htfOverlap(vA, vA, sBull)
                string tipTxt = (sBull ? "Bullish" : "Bearish") + " pivot SMT [" + e.tfName + "]: " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(tr.pA, format.mintick) + " → " + str.tostring(vA, format.mintick) + " (" + sA + "), " + corrName + " " + str.tostring(tr.pB, format.mintick) + " → " + str.tostring(vB, format.mintick) + " (" + sB + "). " + swName + " made the new " + (isHigh ? "high" : "low") + ", " + flName + " did not"
                out := SMTSetup.new(isBull = sBull, refName = nm, isKey = false, sweeper = sw, sweepBar = pivIdx, legBar = pivIdx, legTime = pivT, legExt = ext, legPrice = vA, sweepExt = vA, lvlA = tr.pA, lvlTime = tr.t, detectTime = f.t, sweepTime = pivT, sweepPrice = ext, sweptLevel = sw == 1 ? tr.pA : tr.pB, mssLevel = isHigh ? e.lastPLA : e.lastPHA, htfTap = tap != "", htfTag = tap, tip = tipTxt, pivMode = true, failLvl = fail, prevB = tr.pB, curB = vB)
                array.push(e.setups, out)
                e.cntSmtDev := e.cntSmtDev + 1
                e.cntPivSmt := e.cntPivSmt + 1
                bool recHi = sw == 1 and isHigh
                bool recLo = sw == 1 and not isHigh
                e.lastSweepHiBar := recHi ? pivIdx : e.lastSweepHiBar
                e.lastSweepHiExt := recHi ? false : e.lastSweepHiExt
                e.lastSweepLoBar := recLo ? pivIdx : e.lastSweepLoBar
                e.lastSweepLoExt := recLo ? false : e.lastSweepLoExt
                e.logSmt := (sBull ? "Bull" : "Bear") + " pivot SMT developing (" + nm + ": " + swName + " made the new " + (isHigh ? "high" : "low") + ")"
    if ok
        tr.pA := vA
        tr.pB := vB
        tr.bar := pivIdx
        tr.t := pivT
    out

// a fresh engine with its 4 fixed liquidity references and 4 empty pivot-SMT tracks
f_newEngine(string name, bool enabled, bool entryTf, bool smtOk, int sec, bool isChart) =>
    Engine e = Engine.new(tfName = name, enabled = enabled, entryTf = entryTf, smtOk = smtOk, rawList = array.new<RawFVG>(), ifvgList = array.new<IFVGZone>(), setups = array.new<SMTSetup>(), refs = array.new<LiqRef>(), ifvgTf = isIFVGAllowedTF(sec), isChart = isChart, tfSec = sec, tHiA = PivTrack.new(), tLoA = PivTrack.new(), tHiB = PivTrack.new(), tLoB = PivTrack.new())
    array.push(e.refs, LiqRef.new(name = "PDH", isHigh = true, kind = 0))
    array.push(e.refs, LiqRef.new(name = "PDL", isHigh = false, kind = 0))
    array.push(e.refs, LiqRef.new(name = "PWH", isHigh = true, kind = 0))
    array.push(e.refs, LiqRef.new(name = "PWL", isHigh = false, kind = 0))
    e

// ============================== DATA (runs on every bar) ==============================
chartSec = timeframe.in_seconds()
minSmtSec = timeframe.in_seconds(minSmtTf)
allowedEntryTF = f_isEntryTf(chartSec)

atrValue = ta.atr(atrLen)

// the correlated market on the chart timeframe, bar-for-bar aligned with the chart (only read on closed bars)
[corrHigh, corrLow, corrTickRaw] = request.security(correlatedSym, timeframe.period, [high, low, syminfo.mintick], gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
corrTick = nz(corrTickRaw, syminfo.mintick)

// chart-TF swings. Both markets can anchor a swing; the other market's level = its extreme within +/- syncEff bars
syncEff = math.min(syncBars, pivotRight)
postLen = math.max(pivotRight - syncEff, 1)
phA = ta.pivothigh(high, pivotLeft, pivotRight)
plA = ta.pivotlow(low, pivotLeft, pivotRight)
phB = ta.pivothigh(corrHigh, pivotLeft, pivotRight)
plB = ta.pivotlow(corrLow, pivotLeft, pivotRight)
winHiA = ta.highest(high, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff]
winLoA = ta.lowest(low, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff]
winHiB = ta.highest(corrHigh, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff]
winLoB = ta.lowest(corrLow, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff]
postHiA = ta.highest(high, postLen)
postLoA = ta.lowest(low, postLen)
postHiB = ta.highest(corrHigh, postLen)
postLoB = ta.lowest(corrLow, postLen)

// session component of the IFVG score, evaluated on the current confirmed chart bar in the selected zone
f_inScoreSess(string sess) =>
    not na(time(timeframe.period, sess + ":1234567", i_scoreTz == "Exchange" ? syminfo.timezone : i_scoreTz))
sessNyAmIn = f_inScoreSess(i_sessNyAm)
sessLdnIn  = f_inScoreSess(i_sessLdn)
sessNyPmIn = f_inScoreSess(i_sessNyPm)
sessOtherIn = f_inScoreSess(i_sessOther)
sessPtsNow = sessNyAmIn ? 15 : sessLdnIn ? 15 : sessNyPmIn ? 10 : sessOtherIn ? 5 : 0
sessNameNow = sessNyAmIn ? "NY AM" : sessLdnIn ? "London" : sessNyPmIn ? "NY PM" : sessOtherIn ? "Other" : ""

// universal pivot SMT alignment (chart TF): both markets' extreme within +/- pivSyncEff bars of the swing candle
// (pivSync = 0 -> exactly the swing candle, i.e. high[pivotRight] / corrHigh[pivotRight]: same timestamp on both)
// and their extreme over the bars after that window up to the current bar (has the failing market taken its swing since?)
pivSyncEff = math.min(pivSync, pivotRight)
pivPostLen = math.max(pivotRight - pivSyncEff, 1)
pvHiA = ta.highest(high, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff]
pvLoA = ta.lowest(low, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff]
pvHiB = ta.highest(corrHigh, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff]
pvLoB = ta.lowest(corrLow, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff]
pvPostHiA = ta.highest(high, pivPostLen)
pvPostLoA = ta.lowest(low, pivPostLen)
pvPostHiB = ta.highest(corrHigh, pivPostLen)
pvPostLoB = ta.lowest(corrLow, pivPostLen)

// HTF swings (confirmed HTF pivots, last closed HTF bar only: [1] + lookahead_on = no future data)
swSyncEff = math.min(swSync, swR)
swPostLen = math.max(swR - swSyncEff, 1)
[aPH, aPL, aWinH, aWinL, aPostH, aPostL, aPT, aTc] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, swTf, [ta.pivothigh(high, swL, swR)[1], ta.pivotlow(low, swL, swR)[1], ta.highest(high, 2 * swSyncEff + 1)[swR - swSyncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * swSyncEff + 1)[swR - swSyncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, swPostLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, swPostLen)[1], time[swR + 1], time[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[bPH, bPL, bWinH, bWinL, bPostH, bPostL] = request.security(correlatedSym, swTf, [ta.pivothigh(high, swL, swR)[1], ta.pivotlow(low, swL, swR)[1], ta.highest(high, 2 * swSyncEff + 1)[swR - swSyncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * swSyncEff + 1)[swR - swSyncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, swPostLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, swPostLen)[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
newSw = not na(aTc) and (na(aTc[1]) or aTc != aTc[1])

// previous day / week levels of BOTH markets (last CLOSED bar, same on history and realtime)
[pdhA, pdlA] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", [high[1], low[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[pdhB, pdlB] = request.security(correlatedSym, "D", [high[1], low[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[pwhA, pwlA] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "W", [high[1], low[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[pwhB, pwlB] = request.security(correlatedSym, "W", [high[1], low[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
// first confirmed chart bar of a new trading day (chart's own daily session, no request.security)
dayT = time("D")
bool newDay = not na(dayT) and not na(dayT[1]) and dayT != dayT[1]
bool pdNew = not na(pdhA) and not na(pdlA) and not na(pdhB) and not na(pdlB) and (na(pdhA[1]) or pdhA != pdhA[1] or pdlA != pdlA[1] or pdhB != pdhB[1] or pdlB != pdlB[1])
bool pwNew = not na(pwhA) and not na(pwlA) and not na(pwhB) and not na(pwlB) and (na(pwhA[1]) or pwhA != pwhA[1] or pwlA != pwlA[1] or pwhB != pwhB[1] or pwlB != pwlB[1])

// HTF FVG data: last CLOSED HTF bars only ([1] offsets + lookahead_on = no future data, same on history and realtime)
//   [1] = candle 3 (last closed), [2] = candle 2 (the gap candle), [3] = candle 1
//   time[3] / time[2] = open time of candle 1 / 2 (box anchors), time_close[1] = close of candle 3 (fixed-width box)
//   o2/h2/l2/c2 = candle 2 OHLC, atr2 = ATR on that timeframe at candle 2, v2/va2 = its volume and 20-candle average
//   (displacement metrics of the selection engine; all from CLOSED HTF candles, same on history and realtime)
nameH1 = f_tfName(htfTf1)
nameH2 = f_tfName(htfTf2)
nameH3 = f_tfName(htfTf3)
nameH4 = f_tfName(htfTf4)
nameH5 = f_tfName(htfTf5)
nameH6 = f_tfName(htfTf6)
nameH7 = f_tfName(htfTf7)
nameH8 = f_tfName(htfTf8)
[hC1, lC1, cC1, hA1, lA1, tC1, tA1, tM1, tX1, o21, h21, l21, c21, atr21, v21, va21] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTf1, [high[1], low[1], close[1], high[3], low[3], time[1], time[3], time[2], time_close[1], open[2], high[2], low[2], close[2], ta.atr(atrLen)[2], volume[2], ta.sma(volume, 20)[2]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[hC2, lC2, cC2, hA2, lA2, tC2, tA2, tM2, tX2, o22, h22, l22, c22, atr22, v22, va22] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTf2, [high[1], low[1], close[1], high[3], low[3], time[1], time[3], time[2], time_close[1], open[2], high[2], low[2], close[2], ta.atr(atrLen)[2], volume[2], ta.sma(volume, 20)[2]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[hC3, lC3, cC3, hA3, lA3, tC3, tA3, tM3, tX3, o23, h23, l23, c23, atr23, v23, va23] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTf3, [high[1], low[1], close[1], high[3], low[3], time[1], time[3], time[2], time_close[1], open[2], high[2], low[2], close[2], ta.atr(atrLen)[2], volume[2], ta.sma(volume, 20)[2]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[hC4, lC4, cC4, hA4, lA4, tC4, tA4, tM4, tX4, o24, h24, l24, c24, atr24, v24, va24] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTf4, [high[1], low[1], close[1], high[3], low[3], time[1], time[3], time[2], time_close[1], open[2], high[2], low[2], close[2], ta.atr(atrLen)[2], volume[2], ta.sma(volume, 20)[2]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[hC5, lC5, cC5, hA5, lA5, tC5, tA5, tM5, tX5, o25, h25, l25, c25, atr25, v25, va25] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTf5, [high[1], low[1], close[1], high[3], low[3], time[1], time[3], time[2], time_close[1], open[2], high[2], low[2], close[2], ta.atr(atrLen)[2], volume[2], ta.sma(volume, 20)[2]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[hC6, lC6, cC6, hA6, lA6, tC6, tA6, tM6, tX6, o26, h26, l26, c26, atr26, v26, va26] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTf6, [high[1], low[1], close[1], high[3], low[3], time[1], time[3], time[2], time_close[1], open[2], high[2], low[2], close[2], ta.atr(atrLen)[2], volume[2], ta.sma(volume, 20)[2]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[hC7, lC7, cC7, hA7, lA7, tC7, tA7, tM7, tX7, o27, h27, l27, c27, atr27, v27, va27] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTf7, [high[1], low[1], close[1], high[3], low[3], time[1], time[3], time[2], time_close[1], open[2], high[2], low[2], close[2], ta.atr(atrLen)[2], volume[2], ta.sma(volume, 20)[2]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[hC8, lC8, cC8, hA8, lA8, tC8, tA8, tM8, tX8, o28, h28, l28, c28, atr28, v28, va28] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTf8, [high[1], low[1], close[1], high[3], low[3], time[1], time[3], time[2], time_close[1], open[2], high[2], low[2], close[2], ta.atr(atrLen)[2], volume[2], ta.sma(volume, 20)[2]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
newH1 = not na(tC1) and (na(tC1[1]) or tC1 != tC1[1])
newH2 = not na(tC2) and (na(tC2[1]) or tC2 != tC2[1])
newH3 = not na(tC3) and (na(tC3[1]) or tC3 != tC3[1])
newH4 = not na(tC4) and (na(tC4[1]) or tC4 != tC4[1])
newH5 = not na(tC5) and (na(tC5[1]) or tC5 != tC5[1])
newH6 = not na(tC6) and (na(tC6[1]) or tC6 != tC6[1])
newH7 = not na(tC7) and (na(tC7[1]) or tC7 != tC7[1])
newH8 = not na(tC8) and (na(tC8[1]) or tC8 != tC8[1])

// ============================== FEEDS ==============================
// chart feed = the current confirmed chart bar, every bar
Feed fChart = Feed.new(isNew = true, t = time, tMid = time[1], pivT = time[pivotRight], o = open, h = high, l = low, c = close, h2 = high[2], l2 = low[2], atr = atrValue, phA = phA, plA = plA, winHiA = winHiA, winLoA = winLoA, postHiA = postHiA, postLoA = postLoA, ch = corrHigh, cl = corrLow, phB = phB, plB = plB, winHiB = winHiB, winLoB = winLoB, postHiB = postHiB, postLoB = postLoB, corrTick = corrTick, pvHiA = pvHiA, pvLoA = pvLoA, pvHiB = pvHiB, pvLoB = pvLoB, pvPostHiA = pvPostHiA, pvPostLoA = pvPostLoA, pvPostHiB = pvPostHiB, pvPostLoB = pvPostLoB)

// higher-timeframe feeds: the LAST CLOSED candle of that timeframe ([1] + lookahead_on = no future data)
// for both the chart symbol and the correlated symbol, with the same pivot / window / ATR values the
// chart engine uses, computed ON that timeframe.  A feed only runs when it is higher than the chart TF.
enF1 = useMtf and useF1 and timeframe.in_seconds(tfF1) > chartSec
enF2 = useMtf and useF2 and timeframe.in_seconds(tfF2) > chartSec
enF3 = useMtf and useF3 and timeframe.in_seconds(tfF3) > chartSec
enF4 = useMtf and useF4 and timeframe.in_seconds(tfF4) > chartSec
[a1o, a1h, a1l, a1c, a1h2, a1l2, a1t, a1tm, a1pt, a1atr, a1ph, a1pl, a1wh, a1wl, a1posh, a1posl, a1pvh, a1pvl, a1pph, a1ppl] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tfF1, [open[1], high[1], low[1], close[1], high[3], low[3], time[1], time[2], time[pivotRight + 1], ta.atr(atrLen)[1], ta.pivothigh(high, pivotLeft, pivotRight)[1], ta.pivotlow(low, pivotLeft, pivotRight)[1], ta.highest(high, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, postLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, postLen)[1], ta.highest(high, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, pivPostLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, pivPostLen)[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[b1h, b1l, b1ph, b1pl, b1wh, b1wl, b1posh, b1posl, b1tick, b1pvh, b1pvl, b1pph, b1ppl] = request.security(correlatedSym, tfF1, [high[1], low[1], ta.pivothigh(high, pivotLeft, pivotRight)[1], ta.pivotlow(low, pivotLeft, pivotRight)[1], ta.highest(high, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, postLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, postLen)[1], syminfo.mintick, ta.highest(high, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, pivPostLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, pivPostLen)[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[a2o, a2h, a2l, a2c, a2h2, a2l2, a2t, a2tm, a2pt, a2atr, a2ph, a2pl, a2wh, a2wl, a2posh, a2posl, a2pvh, a2pvl, a2pph, a2ppl] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tfF2, [open[1], high[1], low[1], close[1], high[3], low[3], time[1], time[2], time[pivotRight + 1], ta.atr(atrLen)[1], ta.pivothigh(high, pivotLeft, pivotRight)[1], ta.pivotlow(low, pivotLeft, pivotRight)[1], ta.highest(high, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, postLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, postLen)[1], ta.highest(high, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, pivPostLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, pivPostLen)[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[b2h, b2l, b2ph, b2pl, b2wh, b2wl, b2posh, b2posl, b2tick, b2pvh, b2pvl, b2pph, b2ppl] = request.security(correlatedSym, tfF2, [high[1], low[1], ta.pivothigh(high, pivotLeft, pivotRight)[1], ta.pivotlow(low, pivotLeft, pivotRight)[1], ta.highest(high, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, postLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, postLen)[1], syminfo.mintick, ta.highest(high, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, pivPostLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, pivPostLen)[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[a3o, a3h, a3l, a3c, a3h2, a3l2, a3t, a3tm, a3pt, a3atr, a3ph, a3pl, a3wh, a3wl, a3posh, a3posl, a3pvh, a3pvl, a3pph, a3ppl] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tfF3, [open[1], high[1], low[1], close[1], high[3], low[3], time[1], time[2], time[pivotRight + 1], ta.atr(atrLen)[1], ta.pivothigh(high, pivotLeft, pivotRight)[1], ta.pivotlow(low, pivotLeft, pivotRight)[1], ta.highest(high, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, postLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, postLen)[1], ta.highest(high, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, pivPostLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, pivPostLen)[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[b3h, b3l, b3ph, b3pl, b3wh, b3wl, b3posh, b3posl, b3tick, b3pvh, b3pvl, b3pph, b3ppl] = request.security(correlatedSym, tfF3, [high[1], low[1], ta.pivothigh(high, pivotLeft, pivotRight)[1], ta.pivotlow(low, pivotLeft, pivotRight)[1], ta.highest(high, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, postLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, postLen)[1], syminfo.mintick, ta.highest(high, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, pivPostLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, pivPostLen)[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[a4o, a4h, a4l, a4c, a4h2, a4l2, a4t, a4tm, a4pt, a4atr, a4ph, a4pl, a4wh, a4wl, a4posh, a4posl, a4pvh, a4pvl, a4pph, a4ppl] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tfF4, [open[1], high[1], low[1], close[1], high[3], low[3], time[1], time[2], time[pivotRight + 1], ta.atr(atrLen)[1], ta.pivothigh(high, pivotLeft, pivotRight)[1], ta.pivotlow(low, pivotLeft, pivotRight)[1], ta.highest(high, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, postLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, postLen)[1], ta.highest(high, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, pivPostLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, pivPostLen)[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[b4h, b4l, b4ph, b4pl, b4wh, b4wl, b4posh, b4posl, b4tick, b4pvh, b4pvl, b4pph, b4ppl] = request.security(correlatedSym, tfF4, [high[1], low[1], ta.pivothigh(high, pivotLeft, pivotRight)[1], ta.pivotlow(low, pivotLeft, pivotRight)[1], ta.highest(high, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * syncEff + 1)[pivotRight - syncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, postLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, postLen)[1], syminfo.mintick, ta.highest(high, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff + 1], ta.lowest(low, 2 * pivSyncEff + 1)[pivotRight - pivSyncEff + 1], ta.highest(high, pivPostLen)[1], ta.lowest(low, pivPostLen)[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
newF1 = enF1 and not na(a1t) and (na(a1t[1]) or a1t != a1t[1])
newF2 = enF2 and not na(a2t) and (na(a2t[1]) or a2t != a2t[1])
newF3 = enF3 and not na(a3t) and (na(a3t[1]) or a3t != a3t[1])
newF4 = enF4 and not na(a4t) and (na(a4t[1]) or a4t != a4t[1])
Feed fF1 = Feed.new(isNew = newF1, t = a1t, tMid = a1tm, pivT = a1pt, o = a1o, h = a1h, l = a1l, c = a1c, h2 = a1h2, l2 = a1l2, atr = a1atr, phA = a1ph, plA = a1pl, winHiA = a1wh, winLoA = a1wl, postHiA = a1posh, postLoA = a1posl, ch = b1h, cl = b1l, phB = b1ph, plB = b1pl, winHiB = b1wh, winLoB = b1wl, postHiB = b1posh, postLoB = b1posl, corrTick = nz(b1tick, syminfo.mintick), pvHiA = a1pvh, pvLoA = a1pvl, pvHiB = b1pvh, pvLoB = b1pvl, pvPostHiA = a1pph, pvPostLoA = a1ppl, pvPostHiB = b1pph, pvPostLoB = b1ppl)
Feed fF2 = Feed.new(isNew = newF2, t = a2t, tMid = a2tm, pivT = a2pt, o = a2o, h = a2h, l = a2l, c = a2c, h2 = a2h2, l2 = a2l2, atr = a2atr, phA = a2ph, plA = a2pl, winHiA = a2wh, winLoA = a2wl, postHiA = a2posh, postLoA = a2posl, ch = b2h, cl = b2l, phB = b2ph, plB = b2pl, winHiB = b2wh, winLoB = b2wl, postHiB = b2posh, postLoB = b2posl, corrTick = nz(b2tick, syminfo.mintick), pvHiA = a2pvh, pvLoA = a2pvl, pvHiB = b2pvh, pvLoB = b2pvl, pvPostHiA = a2pph, pvPostLoA = a2ppl, pvPostHiB = b2pph, pvPostLoB = b2ppl)
Feed fF3 = Feed.new(isNew = newF3, t = a3t, tMid = a3tm, pivT = a3pt, o = a3o, h = a3h, l = a3l, c = a3c, h2 = a3h2, l2 = a3l2, atr = a3atr, phA = a3ph, plA = a3pl, winHiA = a3wh, winLoA = a3wl, postHiA = a3posh, postLoA = a3posl, ch = b3h, cl = b3l, phB = b3ph, plB = b3pl, winHiB = b3wh, winLoB = b3wl, postHiB = b3posh, postLoB = b3posl, corrTick = nz(b3tick, syminfo.mintick), pvHiA = a3pvh, pvLoA = a3pvl, pvHiB = b3pvh, pvLoB = b3pvl, pvPostHiA = a3pph, pvPostLoA = a3ppl, pvPostHiB = b3pph, pvPostLoB = b3ppl)
Feed fF4 = Feed.new(isNew = newF4, t = a4t, tMid = a4tm, pivT = a4pt, o = a4o, h = a4h, l = a4l, c = a4c, h2 = a4h2, l2 = a4l2, atr = a4atr, phA = a4ph, plA = a4pl, winHiA = a4wh, winLoA = a4wl, postHiA = a4posh, postLoA = a4posl, ch = b4h, cl = b4l, phB = b4ph, plB = b4pl, winHiB = b4wh, winLoB = b4wl, postHiB = b4posh, postLoB = b4posl, corrTick = nz(b4tick, syminfo.mintick), pvHiA = a4pvh, pvLoA = a4pvl, pvHiB = b4pvh, pvLoB = b4pvl, pvPostHiA = a4pph, pvPostLoA = a4ppl, pvPostHiB = b4pph, pvPostLoB = b4ppl)

// one engine per feed (state lives across bars)
var Engine eC = f_newEngine(f_tfName(timeframe.period), true, allowedEntryTF, chartSec >= minSmtSec, chartSec, true)
var Engine e1 = f_newEngine(f_tfName(tfF1), enF1, f_isEntryTf(timeframe.in_seconds(tfF1)), timeframe.in_seconds(tfF1) >= minSmtSec, timeframe.in_seconds(tfF1), false)
var Engine e2 = f_newEngine(f_tfName(tfF2), enF2, f_isEntryTf(timeframe.in_seconds(tfF2)), timeframe.in_seconds(tfF2) >= minSmtSec, timeframe.in_seconds(tfF2), false)
var Engine e3 = f_newEngine(f_tfName(tfF3), enF3, f_isEntryTf(timeframe.in_seconds(tfF3)), timeframe.in_seconds(tfF3) >= minSmtSec, timeframe.in_seconds(tfF3), false)
var Engine e4 = f_newEngine(f_tfName(tfF4), enF4, f_isEntryTf(timeframe.in_seconds(tfF4)), timeframe.in_seconds(tfF4) >= minSmtSec, timeframe.in_seconds(tfF4), false)

// escalation ladder for stacked-FVG resolution: enabled feed engines on 2m / 3m / 5m that are HIGHER than
// the chart, in ascending order. Built once; never contains anything above 5m.
var array<Engine> ifvgLadder = array.new<Engine>()
if barstate.isfirst
    array<Engine> cand = array.from(e1, e2, e3, e4)
    for sec in array.from(120, 180, 300)
        if sec > chartSec
            for k = 0 to 3
                Engine ek = array.get(cand, k)
                if ek.enabled and ek.tfSec == sec
                    array.push(ifvgLadder, ek)

// ============================== IFVG CONFLUENCE SCORE (section 1c) ==============================
// Computed ONCE on the inversion candle of every IFVG from what the engine knows on that candle: the SELECTED
// HTF zone (f_hzEligible = candidate AND selected, never a different zone), the live SMT setups, the session of
// the current chart bar, the inversion candle itself, the last liquidity sweep by the chart market and the
// feed's own FVG / IFVG pools.  Stored on the IFVGZone and never recomputed, so a later sweep or SMT can never
// raise an old score.  0-100, graded A+ .. D.  It ranks rule-based confluence; it is NOT a probability.

// A. selected HTF FVG confluence (25): best eligible (= selected) zone overlapping or within prox of the IFVG.
//    fully inside 22-25, >= 50% overlap 18-22, partial overlap 10-17, only near a boundary 10-14, none 0.
//    The 0..3 / 0..4 / 0..7 / 0..4 extra comes from the zone's selection-engine composite score (0..1).
f_calculateIFVGHTFScore(float top, float bot, bool isBull, float px, float prox) =>
    int best = -1
    for [i, z] in htfList
        bool dirOk = not htfMatchDir or z.isBull == isBull
        bool near = top >= z.bottom - prox and bot <= z.top + prox
        if dirOk and near and f_hzEligible(z) and (best < 0 or f_hzBetter(z, array.get(htfList, best), px))
            best := i
    int pts = 0
    if best >= 0
        HtfFVG zb = array.get(htfList, best)
        float h = math.max(top - bot, syminfo.mintick)
        float ov = math.max(0.0, math.min(top, zb.top) - math.max(bot, zb.bottom)) / h
        float q = math.max(0.0, math.min(1.0, nz(zb.score, 0.0)))
        pts := ov >= 0.999 ? 22 + int(math.round(3.0 * q)) : ov >= 0.5 ? 18 + int(math.round(4.0 * q)) : ov > 0.0 ? 10 + int(math.round(7.0 * q)) : 10 + int(math.round(4.0 * q))
    pts

// B. SMT alignment (20): best same-direction live SMT that passes the filters and started at/before the IFVG.
//    age = feed bars since the SMT's latest extreme.  Confirmed and age <= half of 'Max bars from SMT to IFVG'
//    = 20, confirmed inside the window = 15, developing inside the window = 10, up to twice the window = 5,
//    none / only opposite-direction SMTs = 0.
f_calculateIFVGSMTScore(Engine e, bool isBull) =>
    int pts = 0
    for q in e.setups
        int age = e.idx - q.legBar
        int cand = age <= confluenceBars ? (q.confirmed ? (age <= math.max(1, confluenceBars / 2) ? 20 : 15) : 10) : age <= 2 * confluenceBars ? 5 : 0
        bool ok = not q.dead and not q.expired and not q.used and q.isBull == isBull and f_passes(q) and q.sweepBar <= e.idx
        pts := ok ? math.max(pts, cand) : pts
    pts

// C. session (15): points of the session the inversion candle falls in (global sessPtsNow, see DATA)

// D. objective displacement (15) of the inversion candle: body / feed ATR and body / range against the
//    section 6 thresholds, in the IFVG's direction.  >= 1.5x ATR mult and body ratio = 15, >= thresholds = 12,
//    half the ATR mult OR the body ratio = 7, else 0.  Opposite-direction candle = 0.
f_calculateIFVGDisplacementScore(Feed f, bool isBull, float atrF) =>
    float body = math.abs(f.c - f.o)
    float rng = math.max(f.h - f.l, syminfo.mintick)
    float bodyAtr = body / atrF
    float ratio = body / rng
    bool dirOk = isBull ? f.c > f.o : f.c < f.o
    not dirOk ? 0 : bodyAtr >= 1.5 * dispAtrMult and ratio >= dispBodyRatio ? 15 : bodyAtr >= dispAtrMult and ratio >= dispBodyRatio ? 12 : bodyAtr >= 0.5 * dispAtrMult or ratio >= dispBodyRatio ? 7 : 0

// E. preceding liquidity sweep (15): the chart market's last sweep on the IFVG's side (sell-side lows for a
//    bullish IFVG, buy-side highs for a bearish one), recorded by the SMT reference engine and the pivot SMT.
//    External level inside the lookback = 15, internal (feed swing) = 10, up to twice the lookback = 5, else 0.
f_calculateIFVGLiquidityScore(Engine e, bool isBull) =>
    int swBar = isBull ? e.lastSweepLoBar : e.lastSweepHiBar
    bool ext = isBull ? e.lastSweepLoExt : e.lastSweepHiExt
    int age = e.idx - swBar
    na(swBar) or swBar > e.idx ? 0 : age <= i_liqLookbackBars ? (ext ? 15 : 10) : age <= 2 * i_liqLookbackBars ? 5 : 0

// F. clean structure / HTF step-up (10): 5 - 1.5 per other not-yet-inverted feed FVG overlapping the IFVG
//    - 2 per live opposite-direction IFVG overlapping it (clamped 0..5) + 3 when the inversion close also
//    breaks the last feed swing (MSS) + 2 when the primary selected HTF zone has the IFVG's direction.
f_calculateIFVGStructureScore(Engine e, Feed f, float top, float bot, bool isBull, bool htfAligned) =>
    int noise = 0
    for rf in e.rawList
        noise += fvgRangesOverlap(rf.top, rf.bottom, top, bot) ? 1 : 0
    int conflict = 0
    for iz in e.ifvgList
        conflict += iz.isBull != isBull and not iz.used and fvgRangesOverlap(iz.top, iz.bottom, top, bot) ? 1 : 0
    float clean = math.max(0.0, math.min(5.0, 5.0 - 1.5 * noise - 2.0 * conflict))
    bool mss = isBull ? (not na(e.lastPHA) and f.c > e.lastPHA) : (not na(e.lastPLA) and f.c < e.lastPLA)
    int(math.round(clean)) + (mss ? 3 : 0) + (htfAligned ? 2 : 0)

// composite: the six components and the clamped total.  Called once per new IFVG, before it joins the list.
f_calculateIFVGConfluenceScore(Engine e, Feed f, float top, float bot, bool isBull, float atrF, bool htfAligned) =>
    int sHtf = f_calculateIFVGHTFScore(top, bot, isBull, f.c, i_confProxAtr * nz(atrValue, 0.0))
    int sSmt = f_calculateIFVGSMTScore(e, isBull)
    int sSess = sessPtsNow
    int sDisp = f_calculateIFVGDisplacementScore(f, isBull, atrF)
    int sLiq = f_calculateIFVGLiquidityScore(e, isBull)
    int sStruct = f_calculateIFVGStructureScore(e, f, top, bot, isBull, htfAligned)
    int total = math.max(0, math.min(100, sHtf + sSmt + sSess + sDisp + sLiq + sStruct))
    [total, sHtf, sSmt, sSess, sDisp, sLiq, sStruct]

// ---- small helpers that keep f_runEngine under the local-scope limit (a helper's scopes count once) ----
// swing reference pair: the anchoring market's pivot + the other market's window extreme, accepted only when
// the other market's post-window extreme did not exceed that window (it also made a local extreme there)
f_swingPair(array<LiqRef> refs, bool isHigh, int kind, bool anchorA, float piv, float win, float post, int atBar, int atTime, float tolA, float tolB) =>
    float tolO = anchorA ? tolB : tolA
    bool ok = not na(piv) and not na(win) and not na(post) and (isHigh ? post <= win + tolO : post >= win - tolO)
    if ok
        f_addSwingRef(refs, isHigh, kind, anchorA ? piv : win, anchorA ? win : piv, atBar, atTime, tolA, tolB)
    true

// one pivot-SMT track: detect, draw, return whether a filter-passing SMT was created
f_pivRun(Engine e, Feed f, PivTrack tr, bool isHigh, float vA, float vB, float postA, float postB, int pivIdx, int pivT, float tolA, float tolB) =>
    SMTSetup p = f_pivSmt(e, f, tr, isHigh, vA, vB, postA, postB, pivIdx, pivT, tolA, tolB)
    bool out = false
    if not na(p)
        p.draw(e)
        out := f_passes(p)
    out

// ============================== ENGINE (one call = one feed) ==============================
// Runs the complete SMT + IFVG logic for ONE timeframe.  Fixed references (PDH/PDL, PWH/PWL, HTF
// swings) are armed on every chart bar because their events come from chart bars; everything else
// only runs when the feed has a NEW closed candle (f.isNew).  Bar counts (confirmation, lifetime,
// ages) use e.idx = the feed's own bar counter; drawings use the feed candle's TIME.
f_runEngine(Engine e, Feed f) =>
    SigInfo sig = na
    bool bullDet = false
    bool bearDet = false
    bool bullConf = false
    bool bearConf = false
    if e.enabled
        bool corrOkF = not na(f.ch) and not na(f.cl)
        float tolA = tolTicks * syminfo.mintick
        float tolB = tolTicks * nz(f.corrTick, syminfo.mintick)
        float safeAtrF = na(f.atr) or f.atr <= 0.0 ? syminfo.mintick : f.atr

        // ---------- C1. fixed / HTF-swing liquidity references (every chart bar) ----------
        LiqRef rPDH = array.get(e.refs, 0)
        LiqRef rPDL = array.get(e.refs, 1)
        LiqRef rPWH = array.get(e.refs, 2)
        LiqRef rPWL = array.get(e.refs, 3)
        if usePD and pdNew
            rPDH.arm(pdhA, pdhB, e.idx, time)
            rPDL.arm(pdlA, pdlB, e.idx, time)
        if usePW and pwNew
            rPWH.arm(pwhA, pwhB, e.idx, time)
            rPWL.arm(pwlA, pwlB, e.idx, time)
        if useHtfSwing and newSw
            f_swingPair(e.refs, true, 2, true, aPH, bWinH, bPostH, e.idx, aPT, tolA, tolB)
            f_swingPair(e.refs, false, 2, true, aPL, bWinL, bPostL, e.idx, aPT, tolA, tolB)
            f_swingPair(e.refs, true, 2, false, bPH, aWinH, aPostH, e.idx, aPT, tolA, tolB)
            f_swingPair(e.refs, false, 2, false, bPL, aWinL, aPostL, e.idx, aPT, tolA, tolB)

        if f.isNew
            e.idx := e.idx + 1
            e.lastPHA := na(f.phA) ? e.lastPHA : f.phA
            e.lastPLA := na(f.plA) ? e.lastPLA : f.plA
            int pivIdx = e.idx - pivotRight

            // ---------- C2. feed-TF swings (both markets can anchor the swing) ----------
            if corrOkF and useSwing
                f_swingPair(e.refs, true, 1, true, f.phA, f.winHiB, f.postHiB, pivIdx, f.pivT, tolA, tolB)
                f_swingPair(e.refs, false, 1, true, f.plA, f.winLoB, f.postLoB, pivIdx, f.pivT, tolA, tolB)
                f_swingPair(e.refs, true, 1, false, f.phB, f.winHiA, f.postHiA, pivIdx, f.pivT, tolA, tolB)
                f_swingPair(e.refs, false, 1, false, f.plB, f.winLoA, f.postLoA, pivIdx, f.pivT, tolA, tolB)

            // ---------- C3. universal pivot SMT: every confirmed swing of EITHER market vs the other market on the same candle ----------
            // Four tracks: highs / lows anchored on the chart market (its pivot + the correlated market's aligned
            // extreme) and highs / lows anchored on the correlated market (its pivot + the chart market's aligned extreme).
            // A track whose pivot is na this bar is skipped inside f_pivSmt (no detection, no track update).
            if corrOkF and usePivSmt
                bearDet := f_pivRun(e, f, e.tHiA, true, f.phA, f.pvHiB, f.pvPostHiA, f.pvPostHiB, pivIdx, f.pivT, tolA, tolB) or bearDet
                bullDet := f_pivRun(e, f, e.tLoA, false, f.plA, f.pvLoB, f.pvPostLoA, f.pvPostLoB, pivIdx, f.pivT, tolA, tolB) or bullDet
                bearDet := f_pivRun(e, f, e.tHiB, true, f.pvHiA, f.phB, f.pvPostHiA, f.pvPostHiB, pivIdx, f.pivT, tolA, tolB) or bearDet
                bullDet := f_pivRun(e, f, e.tLoB, false, f.pvLoA, f.plB, f.pvPostLoA, f.pvPostLoB, pivIdx, f.pivT, tolA, tolB) or bullDet

            // ---------- D. SMT state machine over every reference ----------
            if corrOkF
                SMTSetup devBullS = na
                SMTSetup devBearS = na
                for q in e.setups
                    if q.active and not q.dead
                        if q.isBull
                            devBullS := q
                        else
                            devBearS := q
                for r in e.refs
                    bool tkA = r.state == 0 and (r.isHigh ? f.h > r.lvlA + tolA : f.l < r.lvlA - tolA)
                    bool tkB = r.state == 0 and (r.isHigh ? f.ch > r.lvlB + tolB : f.cl < r.lvlB - tolB)
                    int sw = tkA ? 1 : 2
                    bool sBull = not r.isHigh
                    bool rKey = r.kind != 1
                    // the chart market took this level (alone or together with the other market): last sweep per side
                    e.lastSweepHiBar := tkA and r.isHigh ? e.idx : e.lastSweepHiBar
                    e.lastSweepHiExt := tkA and r.isHigh ? rKey : e.lastSweepHiExt
                    e.lastSweepLoBar := tkA and not r.isHigh ? e.idx : e.lastSweepLoBar
                    e.lastSweepLoExt := tkA and not r.isHigh ? rKey : e.lastSweepLoExt
                    SMTSetup ex = devBearS
                    if sBull
                        ex := devBullS
                    SMTSetup cs = r.cur
                    if tkA and tkB
                        r.state := 3
                    else if tkA or tkB
                        if not na(ex)
                            // a same-direction SMT is already developing: this sweep joins it (key level upgrades it)
                            ex.tip := ex.tip + " | also swept " + r.name
                            bool upg = ex.sweeper == sw and rKey and not ex.isKey
                            ex.isKey := ex.isKey or upg
                            ex.refName := not upg ? ex.refName : ex.pivMode ? r.name + " + " + ex.refName : r.name
                            ex.lvlA := upg and not ex.pivMode ? r.lvlA : ex.lvlA
                            ex.lvlTime := upg and not ex.pivMode ? r.lvlTime : ex.lvlTime
                            r.state := 3
                        else
                            float ext = sw == 1 ? (r.isHigh ? f.h : f.l) : (r.isHigh ? f.ch : f.cl)
                            string swName = sw == 1 ? syminfo.ticker : corrName
                            string flName = sw == 1 ? corrName : syminfo.ticker
                            string tap = f_htfOverlap(f.l, f.h, sBull)
                            SMTSetup ns = SMTSetup.new(isBull = sBull, refName = r.name, isKey = rKey, sweeper = sw, sweepBar = e.idx, legBar = e.idx, legTime = f.t, legExt = ext, legPrice = r.isHigh ? f.h : f.l, sweepExt = r.isHigh ? f.h : f.l, lvlA = r.lvlA, lvlTime = r.lvlTime, detectTime = f.t, sweepTime = f.t, sweepPrice = ext, sweptLevel = r.lvlA, mssLevel = r.isHigh ? e.lastPLA : e.lastPHA, htfTap = tap != "", htfTag = tap, tip = (sBull ? "Bullish" : "Bearish") + " SMT [" + e.tfName + "] at " + r.name + ": " + swName + " took the level, " + flName + " did not")
                            array.push(e.setups, ns)
                            r.cur := ns
                            r.state := 1
                            e.cntSmtDev := e.cntSmtDev + 1
                            e.logSmt := (sBull ? "Bull" : "Bear") + " SMT developing @" + r.name + " (" + swName + " swept)"
                            if sBull
                                devBullS := ns
                            else
                                devBearS := ns
                            ns.draw(e)
                            bullDet := bullDet or (sBull and f_passes(ns))
                            bearDet := bearDet or (not sBull and f_passes(ns))
                    else if r.state == 1
                        if na(cs)
                            r.state := 3
                        else if cs.dead or cs.expired
                            cs.active := false
                            r.state := 3
                        else
                            bool otherTakes = cs.sweeper == 1 ? (r.isHigh ? f.ch > r.lvlB + tolB : f.cl < r.lvlB - tolB) : (r.isHigh ? f.h > r.lvlA + tolA : f.l < r.lvlA - tolA)
                            if otherTakes
                                cs.active := false
                                r.state := 3
                                e.cntSmtInv := e.cntSmtInv + 1
                                e.logSmt := (cs.isBull ? "Bull" : "Bear") + " SMT @" + r.name + " INVALIDATED" + (cs.confirmed ? " after confirmation" : "") + ": other market took its level"
                                if removeInvalidatedSMT
                                    cs.kill()
                            else
                                float swExt = cs.sweeper == 1 ? (r.isHigh ? f.h : f.l) : (r.isHigh ? f.ch : f.cl)
                                bool newExt = r.isHigh ? swExt > cs.legExt : swExt < cs.legExt
                                cs.legExt := newExt ? swExt : cs.legExt
                                cs.legBar := newExt ? e.idx : cs.legBar
                                cs.legTime := newExt ? f.t : cs.legTime
                                cs.legPrice := newExt ? (r.isHigh ? f.h : f.l) : cs.legPrice
                                string tg = cs.htfTap ? "" : f_htfOverlap(f.l, f.h, cs.isBull)
                                cs.htfTap := cs.htfTap or tg != ""
                                cs.htfTag := tg != "" ? tg : cs.htfTag
                                bool confNow = not cs.confirmed and e.idx - cs.sweepBar >= smtConfirmBars
                                if confNow
                                    cs.confirmed := true
                                    cs.confirmBar := e.idx
                                    cs.confirmTime := f.t
                                    e.cntSmtConf := e.cntSmtConf + 1
                                    e.logSmt := (cs.isBull ? "Bull" : "Bear") + " SMT confirmed @" + cs.refName
                                    bullConf := bullConf or (cs.isBull and f_passes(cs))
                                    bearConf := bearConf or (not cs.isBull and f_passes(cs))
                                if cs.confirmed and not confNow and e.idx - cs.legBar >= smtConfirmBars
                                    cs.active := false
                                    r.state := 3
                                cs.draw(e)

                // ---------- D2. pivot SMT state machine: invalidation, deeper extreme, confirmation ----------
                // sweeper = the market that made the new swing; the SMT dies when the OTHER market takes its own
                // previous swing (failLvl) by more than its tolerance, exactly like a sweep SMT.
                for ps in e.setups
                    if ps.pivMode and ps.active and not ps.dead and not ps.expired
                        bool isHi = not ps.isBull
                        bool oTakes = ps.sweeper == 1 ? (isHi ? f.ch > ps.failLvl + tolB : f.cl < ps.failLvl - tolB) : (isHi ? f.h > ps.failLvl + tolA : f.l < ps.failLvl - tolA)
                        if oTakes
                            ps.active := false
                            e.cntSmtInv := e.cntSmtInv + 1
                            e.logSmt := (ps.isBull ? "Bull" : "Bear") + " pivot SMT " + ps.refName + " INVALIDATED" + (ps.confirmed ? " after confirmation" : "") + ": " + (ps.sweeper == 1 ? corrName : syminfo.ticker) + " took its swing"
                            if removeInvalidatedSMT
                                ps.kill()
                        else
                            float pExt = ps.sweeper == 1 ? (isHi ? f.h : f.l) : (isHi ? f.ch : f.cl)
                            bool deeper = isHi ? pExt > ps.legExt : pExt < ps.legExt
                            ps.legExt := deeper ? pExt : ps.legExt
                            ps.legBar := deeper ? e.idx : ps.legBar
                            ps.legTime := deeper ? f.t : ps.legTime
                            ps.legPrice := deeper ? (isHi ? f.h : f.l) : ps.legPrice
                            ps.curB := deeper and ps.sweeper == 2 ? pExt : ps.curB
                            string tgP = ps.htfTap ? "" : f_htfOverlap(f.l, f.h, ps.isBull)
                            ps.htfTap := ps.htfTap or tgP != ""
                            ps.htfTag := tgP != "" ? tgP : ps.htfTag
                            bool confNowP = not ps.confirmed and e.idx - ps.sweepBar >= smtConfirmBars
                            if confNowP
                                ps.confirmed := true
                                ps.confirmBar := e.idx
                                ps.confirmTime := f.t
                                e.cntSmtConf := e.cntSmtConf + 1
                                e.logSmt := (ps.isBull ? "Bull" : "Bear") + " pivot SMT confirmed (" + ps.refName + ")"
                                bullConf := bullConf or (ps.isBull and f_passes(ps))
                                bearConf := bearConf or (not ps.isBull and f_passes(ps))
                            ps.active := ps.active and not (ps.confirmed and not confNowP and e.idx - ps.legBar >= smtConfirmBars)
                            ps.draw(e)
                // drop used-up swing references (fixed levels stay)
                for i = array.size(e.refs) - 1 to 0
                    LiqRef q2 = array.get(e.refs, i)
                    bool agedOut = q2.kind == 1 and e.idx - q2.lvlBar > swingRefMaxAge
                    bool dropRef = q2.kind != 0 and q2.state != 1 and (q2.state == 3 or agedOut)
                    if dropRef
                        array.remove(e.refs, i)

            // ---------- P3. objective displacement events (feed candles, own ATR, direction-aware) ----------
            // bullish: close > open, body >= x ATR, body / range >= y, N consecutive, optional swing break.
            // Recorded (bar + time) on the last candle of the run; never required unless the filter is REQUIRED.
            float p3Body = math.abs(f.c - f.o)
            float p3Rng = math.max(f.h - f.l, syminfo.mintick)
            bool p3Atr = dispAtrMultP3 <= 0.0 or p3Body >= dispAtrMultP3 * safeAtrF
            bool p3Pct = dispBodyPctP3 <= 0.0 or p3Body / p3Rng >= dispBodyPctP3
            bool p3Bull = f.c > f.o and p3Atr and p3Pct
            bool p3Bear = f.c < f.o and p3Atr and p3Pct
            e.bullRun := p3Bull ? e.bullRun + 1 : 0
            e.bearRun := p3Bear ? e.bearRun + 1 : 0
            bool bullSwingOk = not dispReqSwing or (not na(e.lastPHA) and f.c > e.lastPHA)
            bool bearSwingOk = not dispReqSwing or (not na(e.lastPLA) and f.c < e.lastPLA)
            bool bullDispEv = e.bullRun >= dispConsec and bullSwingOk
            bool bearDispEv = e.bearRun >= dispConsec and bearSwingOk
            e.lastBullDispBar := bullDispEv ? e.idx : e.lastBullDispBar
            e.lastBullDispTime := bullDispEv ? f.t : e.lastBullDispTime
            e.lastBearDispBar := bearDispEv ? e.idx : e.lastBearDispBar
            e.lastBearDispTime := bearDispEv ? f.t : e.lastBearDispTime

            // ---------- B. IFVG engine (hidden FVG memory -> inversion) ----------
            SMTSetup newestLive = na
            if array.size(e.setups) > 0
                for i = array.size(e.setups) - 1 to 0
                    SMTSetup ql = array.get(e.setups, i)
                    if na(newestLive) and not ql.dead and not ql.expired
                        newestLive := ql

            if array.size(e.rawList) > 0
                for i = array.size(e.rawList) - 1 to 0
                    RawFVG rfa = array.get(e.rawList, i)
                    rfa.age := rfa.age + 1
                    if rfa.age > maxFvgAge
                        array.remove(e.rawList, i)

            float minGap = minGapTicks * syminfo.mintick
            float candleBody = math.abs(f.c - f.o)
            float candleRange = math.max(f.h - f.l, syminfo.mintick)
            float candleBodyRatio = candleBody / candleRange
            float candleRangeAtr = candleRange / safeAtrF
            bool rawBullFVG = false
            bool rawBearFVG = false
            // explicit timeframe gate: raw FVGs (the IFVG candidate pool) only on 1m / 2m / 3m / 5m
            if e.ifvgTf and not na(f.h2) and not na(f.l2)
                rawBullFVG := f.l > f.h2 and (f.l - f.h2) >= minGap
                rawBearFVG := f.h < f.l2 and (f.l2 - f.h) >= minGap
            if rawBullFVG
                e.fvgSeq := e.fvgSeq + 1
                array.push(e.rawList, RawFVG.new(top = f.l, bottom = f.h2, dir = 1, age = 0, gapAtr = (f.l - f.h2) / safeAtrF, bodyRatio = candleBodyRatio, rangeAtr = candleRangeAtr, formT = f.tMid, id = e.fvgSeq, formBar = e.idx))
            if rawBearFVG
                e.fvgSeq := e.fvgSeq + 1
                array.push(e.rawList, RawFVG.new(top = f.l2, bottom = f.h, dir = -1, age = 0, gapAtr = (f.l2 - f.h) / safeAtrF, bodyRatio = candleBodyRatio, rangeAtr = candleRangeAtr, formT = f.tMid, id = e.fvgSeq, formBar = e.idx))
            while array.size(e.rawList) > maxHiddenFVG
                array.shift(e.rawList)

            // inversion: a failed quality check drops that FVG but the loop keeps looking, so a valid older FVG is not lost
            float cleanBreakBuffer = safeAtrF * f_breakBufferAtr()
            bool foundInv = false
            bool newBullIFVG = false
            bool newBearIFVG = false
            float newTop = na
            float newBot = na
            int newFormT = na
            string newResTf = e.tfName
            int newFvgId = na
            bool resolvedMode = ifvgResolve != "Per-feed (legacy)"
            bool doInvert = resolvedMode ? e.isChart : true
            if resolvedMode and e.isChart and e.ifvgTf
                // ---- resolveStackedFVG: chart pool -> 2m -> 3m -> 5m, ONE anchor, confirmed by THIS close ----
                array<int> c0 = getCandidateFVGs(e.rawList, f.c, cleanBreakBuffer, 0, na, na, false)
                int n0 = array.size(c0)
                if n0 > 0
                    // direction of the event = direction of the most recent inverted FVG; keep that direction only
                    int pick0 = f_pickDeterministic(e.rawList, c0)
                    int dirEv = array.get(e.rawList, pick0).dir
                    array<int> cD = getCandidateFVGs(e.rawList, f.c, cleanBreakBuffer, dirEv, na, na, false)
                    bool stacked0 = f_anyStacked(e.rawList, cD)
                    array<RawFVG> anchorPool = e.rawList
                    bool anchorFromLadder = false
                    int anchorIdx = -1
                    string resTf = e.tfName
                    string dbgSteps = e.tfName + ": " + str.tostring(array.size(cD)) + (stacked0 ? " stacked" : "")
                    if array.size(cD) == 1 or not stacked0
                        anchorIdx := f_pickDeterministic(e.rawList, cD)
                    else
                        [uTop, uBot] = f_unionRange(e.rawList, cD)
                        array<RawFVG> prevPool = e.rawList
                        array<int> prevIdx = cD
                        bool done = false
                        if array.size(ifvgLadder) > 0
                            for L = 0 to array.size(ifvgLadder) - 1
                                if not done
                                    Engine eL = array.get(ifvgLadder, L)
                                    array<int> cL = getCandidateFVGs(eL.rawList, f.c, cleanBreakBuffer, dirEv, uTop, uBot, true)
                                    dbgSteps += " → " + eL.tfName + ": " + str.tostring(array.size(cL))
                                    if array.size(cL) == 1
                                        anchorPool := eL.rawList
                                        anchorFromLadder := true
                                        anchorIdx := array.get(cL, 0)
                                        resTf := eL.tfName
                                        done := true
                                    else if array.size(cL) == 0
                                        // nothing at this level: resolve deterministically at the previous level
                                        anchorIdx := f_pickDeterministic(prevPool, prevIdx)
                                        anchorPool := prevPool
                                        anchorFromLadder := L > 0
                                        done := true
                                    else
                                        [uT2, uB2] = f_unionRange(eL.rawList, cL)
                                        uTop := uT2
                                        uBot := uB2
                                        prevPool := eL.rawList
                                        prevIdx := cL
                                        resTf := eL.tfName
                        if not done
                            // ladder exhausted (5m is the last rung): deterministic final pick at the last level
                            anchorIdx := f_pickDeterministic(prevPool, prevIdx)
                            anchorPool := prevPool
                            anchorFromLadder := true
                    if anchorIdx >= 0
                        RawFVG ra = array.get(anchorPool, anchorIdx)
                        bool qOkA = f_qualityPass(ra.gapAtr, ra.bodyRatio, ra.rangeAtr)
                        if qOkA
                            foundInv := true
                            newBullIFVG := ra.dir == -1
                            newBearIFVG := ra.dir == 1
                            newTop := ra.top
                            newBot := ra.bottom
                            newFormT := ra.formT
                            newResTf := resTf
                            newFvgId := ra.id
                            e.ifvgDbg := "steps " + dbgSteps + " | RESOLVED " + resTf + " #" + str.tostring(ra.id) + " " + (ra.dir == 1 ? "bull FVG" : "bear FVG") + " top " + str.tostring(ra.top, format.mintick) + " bot " + str.tostring(ra.bottom, format.mintick) + " CE " + str.tostring((ra.top + ra.bottom) / 2, format.mintick) + " | close " + str.tostring(f.c, format.mintick) + (ra.dir == -1 ? " > " : " < ") + str.tostring(ra.dir == -1 ? ra.top : ra.bottom, format.mintick) + " | IFVG CONFIRMED bar " + str.tostring(e.idx)
                        else
                            e.cntIfvgRej := e.cntIfvgRej + 1
                            if ra.dir == -1
                                e.lastRejBullBar := e.idx
                            else
                                e.lastRejBearBar := e.idx
                            e.logIfvg := (ra.dir == -1 ? "Bull" : "Bear") + " IFVG anchor rejected by quality filter (" + filterMode + ")"
                            e.ifvgDbg := "steps " + dbgSteps + " | anchor " + resTf + " #" + str.tostring(ra.id) + " REJECTED by quality filter (" + filterMode + ")"
                        // the inversion event is consumed: the anchor leaves its pool, the chart-level candidates leave theirs
                        if anchorFromLadder
                            array.remove(anchorPool, anchorIdx)
                    if array.size(e.rawList) > 0
                        for i = array.size(e.rawList) - 1 to 0
                            if array.includes(cD, i)
                                array.remove(e.rawList, i)
                    // FVGs inverted by this close but ignored as too old are dropped (existing rule)
                    if array.size(e.rawList) > 0
                        for i = array.size(e.rawList) - 1 to 0
                            RawFVG ro = array.get(e.rawList, i)
                            bool invO = ro.dir == -1 ? f.c > ro.top + cleanBreakBuffer : f.c < ro.bottom - cleanBreakBuffer
                            if invO and ro.age > maxFvgToIfvgBars
                                e.cntIfvgOld := e.cntIfvgOld + 1
                                array.remove(e.rawList, i)
            else if not doInvert
                // resolved mode: feed engines only maintain their FVG pool for the ladder; no IFVG, no signal here
                if array.size(e.rawList) > 0
                    for i = array.size(e.rawList) - 1 to 0
                        RawFVG rp = array.get(e.rawList, i)
                        bool invP = rp.dir == -1 ? f.c > rp.top + cleanBreakBuffer : f.c < rp.bottom - cleanBreakBuffer
                        if invP
                            array.remove(e.rawList, i)
            if doInvert and not (resolvedMode and e.isChart and e.ifvgTf) and array.size(e.rawList) > 0
                for i = array.size(e.rawList) - 1 to 0
                    RawFVG rf = array.get(e.rawList, i)
                    bool bullInv = rf.dir == -1 and f.c > rf.top + cleanBreakBuffer
                    bool bearInv = rf.dir == 1 and f.c < rf.bottom - cleanBreakBuffer
                    bool qOk = false
                    if (bullInv or bearInv) and not foundInv
                        if rf.age > maxFvgToIfvgBars
                            // inverted too long after it formed: expired, no IFVG box, no Buy/Sell
                            e.cntIfvgOld := e.cntIfvgOld + 1
                            e.logIfvg := (bullInv ? "Bull" : "Bear") + " inversion ignored: FVG too old (" + str.tostring(rf.age) + " > " + str.tostring(maxFvgToIfvgBars) + " bars)"
                        else
                            qOk := f_qualityPass(rf.gapAtr, rf.bodyRatio, rf.rangeAtr)
                            if qOk
                                foundInv := true
                                newBullIFVG := bullInv
                                newBearIFVG := bearInv
                                newTop := rf.top
                                newBot := rf.bottom
                                newFormT := rf.formT
                            else
                                e.cntIfvgRej := e.cntIfvgRej + 1
                                if bullInv
                                    e.lastRejBullBar := e.idx
                                else
                                    e.lastRejBearBar := e.idx
                                e.logIfvg := (bullInv ? "Bull" : "Bear") + " IFVG rejected by quality filter (" + filterMode + ")"
                        array.remove(e.rawList, i)

            string ifTag = ""
            string ifDir = newBullIFVG ? "Bull" : "Bear"
            string pairMsg = ""
            bool showNote = false
            color zClr = newBullIFVG ? ifvgBullClr : ifvgBearClr
            box zoneBox = na
            if newBullIFVG or newBearIFVG
                ifTag := f_htfContain(newTop, newBot, newBullIFVG)
                string ifPrimary = f_htfPrimaryTag(newTop, newBot, newBullIFVG, f.c)
                bool ifPrimBull = f_htfPrimaryBull(newTop, newBot, newBullIFVG, f.c)
                // Phase 3: same-direction displacement that precedes (or is) this inversion candle
                int ifDispBar = newBullIFVG ? e.lastBullDispBar : e.lastBearDispBar
                int ifDispTime = newBullIFVG ? e.lastBullDispTime : e.lastBearDispTime
                bool ifDispOk = not na(ifDispBar) and (dispMaxToIfvg == 0 or e.idx - ifDispBar <= dispMaxToIfvg)
                e.lastIfvgTag := ifTag
                e.lastIfvgBar := e.idx
                e.lastIfvgTime := f.t
                e.cntIfvgBull := e.cntIfvgBull + (newBullIFVG ? 1 : 0)
                e.cntIfvgBear := e.cntIfvgBear + (newBullIFVG ? 0 : 1)
                // ---- confluence score (section 1c): once, on this inversion candle, from what is known now ----
                [scTot, scHtf, scSmt, scSess, scDisp, scLiq, scStruct] = f_calculateIFVGConfluenceScore(e, f, newTop, newBot, newBullIFVG, safeAtrF, ifPrimary != "" and ifPrimBull == newBullIFVG)
                string scGrade = f_getIFVGGrade(scTot)
                bool scPass = f_ifvgPassesThreshold(scTot)
                e.cntIfvgScoreRej := e.cntIfvgScoreRej + (scPass ? 0 : 1)
                e.logIfvg := ifDir + " IFVG formed, in HTF: " + (ifTag != "" ? f_tagText(ifTag) : "none") + " · score " + scGrade + " " + str.tostring(scTot) + "/100" + (scPass ? "" : " (< min " + str.tostring(i_minProbScore) + ": no signal)")
                IFVGZone newZone = IFVGZone.new(isBull = newBullIFVG, top = newTop, bottom = newBot, invBar = e.idx, htfTag = ifTag, primaryTag = ifPrimary, resTf = newResTf, fvgId = newFvgId, primaryBull = ifPrimBull, dispBar = ifDispBar, dispTime = ifDispTime, dispOk = ifDispOk, confScore = scTot, sHtf = scHtf, sSmt = scSmt, sSess = scSess, sDisp = scDisp, sLiq = scLiq, sStruct = scStruct, grade = scGrade, sessName = sessNameNow)
                if showIFVG
                    // time-anchored: left = the feed candle that inverted the gap (or the original gap candle)
                    int leftT = ifvgAnchor == "Inversion candle" or na(newFormT) ? f.t : newFormT
                    string boxTxt = "IFVG " + newResTf + (ifTag != "" ? " in " + f_tagText(ifTag) + (ifPrimary != "" ? " · P:" + ifPrimary : "") : "") + (i_showIFVGScoreLabels ? " · " + f_ifvgScoreText(newZone, i_showIFVGScoreDebug) : "")
                    zoneBox := box.new(left = leftT, top = newTop, right = time + fvgExtend * chartMs, bottom = newBot, xloc = xloc.bar_time, border_color = color.new(zClr, ifTag != "" ? 0 : 20), border_width = ifTag != "" ? 2 : 1, bgcolor = f_getIFVGColor(scGrade, zClr), text = boxTxt, text_size = size.tiny, text_color = color.white)
                    newZone.b := zoneBox
                array.push(e.ifvgList, newZone)
                // pairing diagnostics against every live SMT of the same direction
                for qn in e.setups
                    bool liveQ = not qn.dead and not qn.used and not qn.expired
                    if liveQ and qn.isBull == newBullIFVG
                        bool tOk = f_timingOk(qn, e.idx)
                        qn.note := not tOk ? (e.idx < qn.sweepBar ? "IFVG formed BEFORE the SMT (rule: at/after)" : "IFVG too far from SMT: " + str.tostring(e.idx - qn.legBar) + " bars (max " + str.tostring(confluenceBars) + ")") : requireHTF and ifTag == "" ? "IFVG not in an HTF FVG (" + htfContain + ")" : not scPass ? "IFVG confluence score " + str.tostring(scTot) + " < min " + str.tostring(i_minProbScore) : ""
                        qn.ifvgSeen := qn.ifvgSeen or (tOk and qn.note == "")
                if not na(newestLive)
                    pairMsg := newestLive.isBull != newBullIFVG ? "IFVG " + ifDir + " but live SMT is " + (newestLive.isBull ? "Bull" : "Bear") + ": DIRECTION MISMATCH" : newestLive.note != "" ? newestLive.note : "IFVG pairs with live SMT (timing + HTF ok)"
                    e.logPair := pairMsg
                    showNote := showDebug and (newestLive.note != "" or newestLive.isBull != newBullIFVG)
                    if showNote
                        label.new(x = f.t, y = newBullIFVG ? f.l : f.h, text = "[" + e.tfName + "] " + pairMsg, xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = newBullIFVG ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = color.new(color.gray, 20), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)

            if array.size(e.ifvgList) > 0
                for i = array.size(e.ifvgList) - 1 to 0
                    IFVGZone iz = array.get(e.ifvgList, i)
                    bool zoneInvalid = iz.isBull ? f.c < iz.bottom : f.c > iz.top
                    bool zoneExpired = e.idx - iz.invBar > ifvgMaxAge
                    if zoneInvalid or zoneExpired
                        if not na(iz.b)
                            if keepAllIfvg or (keepHistory and iz.used)
                                box.set_right(iz.b, time)
                            else
                                box.delete(iz.b)
                        array.remove(e.ifvgList, i)

            // ---------- E. per-setup structure flags, sweep extreme, expiry, clean-up ----------
            float dispBody = math.abs(f.c - f.o)
            float dispRng = math.max(f.h - f.l, syminfo.mintick)
            bool dispOkF = dispBody >= dispAtrMult * safeAtrF and dispBody / dispRng >= dispBodyRatio
            bool bullDispF = f.c > f.o and dispOkF
            bool bearDispF = f.c < f.o and dispOkF
            bool bullFvgF = not na(f.h2) and f.l > f.h2
            bool bearFvgF = not na(f.l2) and f.h < f.l2
            if array.size(e.setups) > 0
                for i = array.size(e.setups) - 1 to 0
                    SMTSetup se = array.get(e.setups, i)
                    if not se.dead and not se.expired
                        // chart-market extreme of the sweep leg = the "Sweep High/Low" stop
                        se.sweepExt := se.used ? se.sweepExt : se.isBull ? math.min(se.sweepExt, f.l) : math.max(se.sweepExt, f.h)
                        bool after = e.idx > se.sweepBar
                        se.dispDone := se.dispDone or (after and (se.isBull ? bullDispF : bearDispF))
                        se.fvgDone := se.fvgDone or (e.idx - 2 >= se.sweepBar and (se.isBull ? bullFvgF : bearFvgF))
                        se.mssDone := se.mssDone or (after and not na(se.mssLevel) and (se.isBull ? f.c > se.mssLevel : f.c < se.mssLevel))
                        // age in DAYS from the fixed detection timestamp (works on any chart timeframe)
                        bool ageOut = smtMaxDays > 0 and (time - se.detectTime) / 86400000.0 > smtMaxDays
                        se.ageExpired := se.ageExpired or ageOut
                        bool expNow = e.idx - se.legBar > smtLifeBars or ageOut
                        se.expired := se.expired or expNow
                        if expNow and not se.used
                            e.cntSmtExp := e.cntSmtExp + 1
                            e.logSmt := (se.isBull ? "Bull" : "Bear") + " SMT @" + se.refName + " expired: " + f_reason(e, se)
                            if not na(se.lbl)
                                label.set_tooltip(se.lbl, "Timeframe: " + e.tfName + "\n" + se.tip + "\nNO SIGNAL: " + f_reason(e, se))
                    // expired (lifetime OR age) setups leave the active list on EVERY feed bar
                    if se.expired and not keepHistory
                        se.kill()
                    if se.dead or se.expired
                        array.remove(e.setups, i)

            // ---------- F. Buy / Sell: valid SMT + IFVG that sits in an HTF FVG ----------
            // ('Require SMT' ON, or OFF with an SMT available: the SMT path is always tried first)
            if e.entryTf and array.size(e.setups) > 0 and array.size(e.ifvgList) > 0
                for i = array.size(e.setups) - 1 to 0
                    SMTSetup sf = array.get(e.setups, i)
                    bool stateOk = not sf.dead and not sf.expired and not sf.used
                    bool smtOk = sf.confirmed or not reqConfirmedSMT
                    bool filtersOk = f_passes(sf) and (not reqDisp or sf.dispDone) and (not reqSetupFvg or sf.fvgDone) and (not reqMSS or sf.mssDone)
                    if stateOk and smtOk and filtersOk
                        for j = array.size(e.ifvgList) - 1 to 0
                            IFVGZone zf = array.get(e.ifvgList, j)
                            bool sameDir = zf.isBull == sf.isBull
                            bool timeOk = f_timingOk(sf, zf.invBar)
                            bool htfOkF = not requireHTF or zf.htfTag != ""
                            // ---- Phase 3 gates (every one is true with its filter OFF) ----
                            bool dirOkP3 = htfDirFilter != "REQUIRE SAME DIRECTION" or zf.primaryTag == "" or zf.primaryBull == sf.isBull
                            bool dispOkP3 = dispFilter != "REQUIRED" or zf.dispOk
                            bool dispReq = dispFilter == "REQUIRED"
                            bool sweepToSmt = seqMaxSweepSmt == 0 or sf.sweepBar - sf.sweepBar <= seqMaxSweepSmt
                            bool confOk = sf.confirmed and not na(sf.confirmBar) and sf.confirmBar >= sf.sweepBar
                            bool orderOk = confOk and zf.invBar >= sf.confirmBar and (not dispReq or (not na(zf.dispBar) and zf.dispBar >= sf.confirmBar and zf.invBar >= zf.dispBar))
                            bool winOk = seqMaxSmtDisp == 0 or (dispReq ? (not na(zf.dispBar) and zf.dispBar - sf.confirmBar <= seqMaxSmtDisp) : zf.invBar - sf.confirmBar <= seqMaxSmtDisp)
                            bool seqOkP3 = not seqFilter or (sweepToSmt and orderOk and winOk)
                            int score = f_score(zf.htfTag != "", true, sf.confirmed, zf.dispOk, zf.primaryTag != "" and zf.primaryBull == sf.isBull)
                            bool scoreOk = score >= minScore
                            // section 1c gate: the IFVG's frozen confluence score must reach the minimum
                            bool confOkF = f_ifvgPassesThreshold(zf.confScore)
                            string info = ""
                            if sameDir and not zf.used and timeOk and htfOkF and dirOkP3 and dispOkP3 and seqOkP3 and scoreOk and confOkF
                                sf.used := true
                                zf.used := true
                                f_markHtfUsed(zf.top, zf.bottom, zf.isBull)
                                info := sf.refName + " · IFVG in " + (zf.htfTag != "" ? f_tagText(zf.htfTag) : "n/a") + (zf.primaryTag != "" ? " (primary " + zf.primaryTag + (zf.primaryBull ? " ▲" : " ▼") + ")" : "") + " · sweeper " + (sf.sweeper == 1 ? syminfo.ticker : corrName) + (dispFilter != "OFF" ? " · disp " + (zf.dispOk ? "yes @" + str.tostring(zf.dispBar) : "no") : "") + " · score " + str.tostring(score) + "/5 · IFVG " + f_ifvgScoreText(zf, i_showIFVGScoreDebug)
                                e.ifvgDbg := e.ifvgDbg + " | SIGNAL bar " + str.tostring(e.idx) + " (same candle)"
                                e.lastSeq := "SWEEP(" + str.tostring(sf.sweepBar) + ") → SMT(" + str.tostring(sf.sweepBar) + ") → CONF(" + str.tostring(sf.confirmBar) + ")" + (zf.dispOk ? " → DISP(" + str.tostring(zf.dispBar) + ")" : "") + " → IFVG(" + str.tostring(zf.invBar) + ") → SIGNAL(" + str.tostring(e.idx) + ")"
                                if not na(sf.lbl)
                                    label.set_tooltip(sf.lbl, "Timeframe: " + e.tfName + "\n" + sf.tip + "\nSIGNAL: " + info)
                                // everything the risk module needs: entry = feed close, both stop candidates, swing target
                                sig := SigInfo.new(isBull = sf.isBull, tfName = e.tfName, entry = f.c, slSweep = sf.sweepExt, slIfvg = sf.isBull ? zf.bottom : zf.top, tpSwing = f_swingTarget(e.refs, sf.isBull, f.c, aPH, aPL), info = info, tag = f_ifvgLogTag(zf, sf.refName + (sf.confirmed ? "+" : "~"), e.tfName))
                                e.lastBuyBar := sf.isBull ? e.idx : e.lastBuyBar
                                e.lastSellBar := sf.isBull ? e.lastSellBar : e.idx
                                e.cntBuy := e.cntBuy + (sf.isBull ? 1 : 0)
                                e.cntSell := e.cntSell + (sf.isBull ? 0 : 1)
                                e.logPair := (sf.isBull ? "BUY" : "SELL") + " fired: " + info
                                break
                    if not na(sig)
                        break

            // ---------- F2. 'Require SMT' OFF: the IFVG that formed on THIS candle fires on its own ----------
            // Same HTF / HTF-direction / displacement gates as F; a same-direction live SMT inside the pairing
            // window is optional confluence only (it raises the score and is consumed by the signal).
            if not i_requireSMT and na(sig) and e.entryTf and (newBullIFVG or newBearIFVG) and array.size(e.ifvgList) > 0
                IFVGZone zn = array.get(e.ifvgList, array.size(e.ifvgList) - 1)
                if zn.invBar == e.idx and not zn.used
                    bool htfOkN = not requireHTF or zn.htfTag != ""
                    bool dirOkN = htfDirFilter != "REQUIRE SAME DIRECTION" or zn.primaryTag == "" or zn.primaryBull == zn.isBull
                    bool dispOkN = dispFilter != "REQUIRED" or zn.dispOk
                    bool confOkN = f_ifvgPassesThreshold(zn.confScore)
                    SMTSetup bestS = na
                    bool bestConf = false
                    for sc in e.setups
                        bool liveC = not sc.dead and not sc.expired and not sc.used and sc.isBull == zn.isBull and f_passes(sc) and f_timingOk(sc, zn.invBar)
                        if liveC and (na(bestS) or (sc.confirmed and not bestConf))
                            bestS := sc
                            bestConf := sc.confirmed
                    bool hasS = not na(bestS)
                    int scoreN = f_score(zn.htfTag != "", hasS, bestConf, zn.dispOk, zn.primaryTag != "" and zn.primaryBull == zn.isBull)
                    if htfOkN and dirOkN and dispOkN and scoreN >= minScore and confOkN
                        zn.used := true
                        f_markHtfUsed(zn.top, zn.bottom, zn.isBull)
                        string smtTxtN = "no SMT (optional)"
                        string slName = ""
                        float slSw = na
                        if hasS
                            smtTxtN := "SMT " + bestS.refName + (bestConf ? " ✔" : " …") + " (optional)"
                            slName := bestS.refName + (bestConf ? "+" : "~")
                            slSw := bestS.sweepExt
                            bestS.used := true
                        string infoN = smtTxtN + " · IFVG in " + (zn.htfTag != "" ? f_tagText(zn.htfTag) : "n/a") + (zn.primaryTag != "" ? " (primary " + zn.primaryTag + (zn.primaryBull ? " ▲" : " ▼") + ")" : "") + (dispFilter != "OFF" ? " · disp " + (zn.dispOk ? "yes @" + str.tostring(zn.dispBar) : "no") : "") + " · score " + str.tostring(scoreN) + "/5 · IFVG " + f_ifvgScoreText(zn, i_showIFVGScoreDebug)
                        if hasS
                            if not na(bestS.lbl)
                                label.set_tooltip(bestS.lbl, "Timeframe: " + e.tfName + "\n" + bestS.tip + "\nSIGNAL: " + infoN)
                        e.ifvgDbg := e.ifvgDbg + " | SIGNAL bar " + str.tostring(e.idx) + " (SMT optional)"
                        e.lastSeq := (hasS ? "SMT(" + str.tostring(bestS.sweepBar) + ") → " : "") + "IFVG(" + str.tostring(zn.invBar) + ") → SIGNAL(" + str.tostring(e.idx) + ")"
                        sig := SigInfo.new(isBull = zn.isBull, tfName = e.tfName, entry = f.c, slSweep = slSw, slIfvg = zn.isBull ? zn.bottom : zn.top, tpSwing = f_swingTarget(e.refs, zn.isBull, f.c, aPH, aPL), info = infoN, tag = f_ifvgLogTag(zn, hasS ? slName : "none", e.tfName))
                        e.lastBuyBar := zn.isBull ? e.idx : e.lastBuyBar
                        e.lastSellBar := zn.isBull ? e.lastSellBar : e.idx
                        e.cntBuy := e.cntBuy + (zn.isBull ? 1 : 0)
                        e.cntSell := e.cntSell + (zn.isBull ? 0 : 1)
                        e.logPair := (zn.isBull ? "BUY" : "SELL") + " fired (SMT optional): " + infoN

        // IFVG boxes follow price on every chart bar (also between feed candles)
        if array.size(e.ifvgList) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(e.ifvgList) - 1
                IFVGZone izx = array.get(e.ifvgList, i)
                if not na(izx.b)
                    box.set_right(izx.b, time + fvgExtend * chartMs)
    [sig, bullDet, bearDet, bullConf, bearConf]

// ============================== RISK MODULE: stop / targets / position size ==============================
// Called once per Buy/Sell.  Draws the ▲/▼ mark (with sizing in its tooltip) and the entry / SL / TP
// lines + a plan label, and returns a one-line summary for the info table.
//   Contract size = Account risk / (stop distance in points x point value), rounded DOWN.
f_onSignal(SigInfo s) =>
    // ----- stop loss -----
    float buf = slBufTicks * syminfo.mintick
    float slRaw = slMode == "Sweep High/Low" ? s.slSweep : s.slIfvg
    if na(slRaw)
        slRaw := slMode == "Sweep High/Low" ? s.slIfvg : s.slSweep
    float sl = s.isBull ? slRaw - buf : slRaw + buf
    float riskPts = math.abs(s.entry - sl)
    if na(riskPts) or riskPts < syminfo.mintick
        riskPts := syminfo.mintick
        sl := s.isBull ? s.entry - riskPts : s.entry + riskPts
    // ----- position size -----
    float pv = autoPointValue ? syminfo.pointvalue : pointValue
    float riskPerCt = riskPts * pv
    int ct = riskPerCt > 0 ? int(math.floor(acctRisk / riskPerCt)) : 0
    float riskUsd = ct * riskPerCt
    // ----- targets -----
    bool useRR = tpMode != "HTF swing"
    bool useSw = tpMode != "Fixed RR"
    float tp1 = na
    float tp2 = na
    float tpSw = na
    if useRR
        tp1 := s.isBull ? s.entry + riskPts * tp1RR : s.entry - riskPts * tp1RR
        if tp2RR > 0
            tp2 := s.isBull ? s.entry + riskPts * tp2RR : s.entry - riskPts * tp2RR
    if useSw
        tpSw := s.tpSwing
    // ----- texts -----
    string dirTxt = s.isBull ? "BUY" : "SELL"
    string sizeTxt = ct > 0 ? str.tostring(ct) + " contract" + (ct > 1 ? "s" : "") + " · risk $" + str.tostring(riskUsd, "#.##") + " of $" + str.tostring(acctRisk, "#.##") : "0 contracts (1 contract risks $" + str.tostring(riskPerCt, "#.##") + " > $" + str.tostring(acctRisk, "#.##") + ")"
    string tpTxt = ""
    if not na(tp1)
        tpTxt += "TP1 " + str.tostring(tp1, format.mintick) + " (1:" + str.tostring(tp1RR, "#.#") + ")"
    if not na(tp2)
        tpTxt += (tpTxt != "" ? " · " : "") + "TP2 " + str.tostring(tp2, format.mintick) + " (1:" + str.tostring(tp2RR, "#.#") + ")"
    if useSw
        tpTxt += (tpTxt != "" ? " · " : "") + (na(tpSw) ? "Swing TP: no unswept level " + (s.isBull ? "above" : "below") : "Swing TP " + str.tostring(tpSw, format.mintick) + " (1:" + str.tostring(math.abs(tpSw - s.entry) / riskPts, "#.#") + ")")
    string planTxt = dirTxt + " " + s.tfName + " · " + sizeTxt + "\nEntry " + str.tostring(s.entry, format.mintick) + " · SL " + str.tostring(sl, format.mintick) + " (" + str.tostring(riskPts, format.mintick) + " pts = $" + str.tostring(riskPerCt, "#.##") + "/ct, " + slMode + ")\n" + tpTxt
    string tt = "Signal timeframe: " + s.tfName + (s.tfName != eC.tfName ? " (drawn on the first " + eC.tfName + " bar after that " + s.tfName + " candle closed)" : "") + "\n" + s.info + "\n" + planTxt
    // ----- ▲ / ▼ mark -----
    if showSignalMarks
        label mk = na
        if s.isBull
            mk := label.new(bar_index, low, "▲\n" + dirTxt + " " + s.tfName, yloc = yloc.belowbar, style = label.style_none, textcolor = color.lime, size = f_size(sigMarkSize), tooltip = tt)
        else
            mk := label.new(bar_index, high, dirTxt + " " + s.tfName + "\n▼", yloc = yloc.abovebar, style = label.style_none, textcolor = color.red, size = f_size(sigMarkSize), tooltip = tt)
        array.push(sigList, SigMark.new(markBar = bar_index, markTime = time, lbl = mk))
    // ----- entry / SL / TP lines + plan label (bar_index anchored: these are chart-native objects) -----
    if showTrade
        int x2 = bar_index + 1
        line lnE = line.new(bar_index, s.entry, x2, s.entry, color = color.gray, style = line.style_dashed)
        line lnS = line.new(bar_index, sl, x2, sl, color = color.red, width = 2)
        line lnT1 = na
        line lnT2 = na
        line lnSw = na
        if not na(tp1)
            lnT1 := line.new(bar_index, tp1, x2, tp1, color = color.green, width = 1)
        if not na(tp2)
            lnT2 := line.new(bar_index, tp2, x2, tp2, color = color.green, width = 1, style = line.style_dotted)
        if not na(tpSw)
            lnSw := line.new(bar_index, tpSw, x2, tpSw, color = color.blue, width = 1, style = line.style_dashed)
        label pl = label.new(x2, sl, planTxt, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(s.isBull ? color.green : color.red, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = size.small, tooltip = tt)
        array.push(plans, TradePlan.new(isBull = s.isBull, tfName = s.tfName, startBar = bar_index, entry = s.entry, sl = sl, tp1 = tp1, tp2 = tp2, tpSw = tpSw, contracts = ct, riskPts = riskPts, riskUsd = riskUsd, txt = planTxt, lnE = lnE, lnS = lnS, lnT1 = lnT1, lnT2 = lnT2, lnSw = lnSw, lbl = pl))
    array.set(lastPlan, 0, s.entry)
    array.set(lastPlan, 1, sl)
    array.set(lastPlan, 2, tp1)
    array.set(lastPlan, 3, tp2)
    array.set(lastPlan, 4, tpSw)
    array.set(lastPlan, 5, ct)
    dirTxt + " " + s.tfName + " · " + str.tostring(ct) + " ct · SL " + str.tostring(riskPts, format.mintick) + " pts · $" + str.tostring(riskUsd, "#.##")

// ============================== HTF FVG SELECTION ENGINE (section 2b) ==============================
// All HTF zones -> candidates (existing lifecycle / age / retest rules) -> clusters of overlapping candidates
// -> ONE winner per cluster (composite score or strict mode) -> HtfFVG.selected -> f_hzEligible() gate.
// Runs on confirmed chart bars only, from closed HTF candles, confirmed pivots and the confirmed close.

// timeframe hierarchy: log-scaled rank between the smallest and the largest ENABLED HTF slot (NDOG = 1 day)
htfSecMin = 0
htfSecMax = 0
if barstate.isfirst
    array<int> secs = array.new_int()
    array<bool> slotOn = array.from(useHtf1, useHtf2, useHtf3, useHtf4, useHtf5, useHtf6, useHtf7, useHtf8, useNdog)
    array<int> slotSec = array.from(timeframe.in_seconds(htfTf1), timeframe.in_seconds(htfTf2), timeframe.in_seconds(htfTf3), timeframe.in_seconds(htfTf4), timeframe.in_seconds(htfTf5), timeframe.in_seconds(htfTf6), timeframe.in_seconds(htfTf7), timeframe.in_seconds(htfTf8), 86400)
    for [k, on] in slotOn
        if on
            array.push(secs, array.get(slotSec, k))
    if array.size(secs) > 0
        htfSecMin := int(array.min(secs))
        htfSecMax := int(array.max(secs))
var int htfSecMinV = htfSecMin
var int htfSecMaxV = htfSecMax

f_clamp01(float x) =>
    na(x) ? na : math.max(0.0, math.min(1.0, x))

// A. freshness / mitigation: lifecycle state x depth of penetration.  DEFENDED / FILLED / INVALIDATED never get here.
f_calculateFreshnessScore(HtfFVG z) =>
    float base = z.state == HZ_FRESH ? 1.0 : z.state == HZ_TOUCHED ? 0.8 : z.state == HZ_PARTIAL ? 0.55 : z.state == HZ_CE50 ? 0.3 : 0.0
    base * (1.0 - 0.5 * z.deepest)

// one level inside the zone or within prox of its edges
f_levelHit(float lvl, float top, float bot, float prox) =>
    not na(lvl) and lvl >= bot - prox and lvl <= top + prox

// B. liquidity / key-level confluence from the levels the script already has: PDH / PDL, PWH / PWL, their 50%
// equilibrium, and the UNSWEPT HTF swings of the chart engine's reference pool.  (Asia / London ranges no
// longer exist in this script; current-day extremes are not computed, so neither is used.)
f_calculateConfluenceScore(HtfFVG z, float prox) =>
    float pts = 0.0
    pts += f_levelHit(pdhA, z.top, z.bottom, prox) ? 1.0 : 0.0
    pts += f_levelHit(pdlA, z.top, z.bottom, prox) ? 1.0 : 0.0
    pts += f_levelHit(pwhA, z.top, z.bottom, prox) ? 1.0 : 0.0
    pts += f_levelHit(pwlA, z.top, z.bottom, prox) ? 1.0 : 0.0
    pts += f_levelHit((pdhA + pdlA) / 2, z.top, z.bottom, prox) ? 0.5 : 0.0
    pts += f_levelHit((pwhA + pwlA) / 2, z.top, z.bottom, prox) ? 0.5 : 0.0
    for q in eC.refs
        pts += q.kind == 2 and q.state == 0 and f_levelHit(q.lvlA, z.top, z.bottom, prox) ? 0.75 : 0.0
    math.min(1.0, pts / i_confSat)

// C. displacement / gap quality from the frozen creation metrics (own-TF ATR normalised): average of the
// available sub-scores, so a symbol's raw price scale never dominates and an NDOG (gap only) still scores.
f_calculateDisplacementScore(HtfFVG z) =>
    bool useV = i_useRelVol and not na(z.relVol)
    float sum = nz(f_clamp01(z.gapAtr / 0.75)) + nz(f_clamp01(z.rangeAtr / 2.0)) + nz(f_clamp01(z.bodyRatio)) + (useV ? f_clamp01((z.relVol - 0.5) / 1.5) : 0.0)
    int n = (na(z.gapAtr) ? 0 : 1) + (na(z.rangeAtr) ? 0 : 1) + (na(z.bodyRatio) ? 0 : 1) + (useV ? 1 : 0)
    n > 0 ? sum / n : 0.0

// D. timeframe hierarchy: 0 for the smallest enabled HTF, 1 for the largest, log-scaled in between
f_calculateTimeframeScore(int sec) =>
    htfSecMaxV > htfSecMinV and htfSecMinV > 0 and sec > 0 ? f_clamp01(math.log(sec * 1.0 / htfSecMinV) / math.log(htfSecMaxV * 1.0 / htfSecMinV)) : 1.0

// composite = weighted average of the four components (weights normalised -> 0..1); stored on the zone
f_calculateFVGProbability(HtfFVG z, float prox) =>
    z.freshS := f_calculateFreshnessScore(z)
    z.confS := f_calculateConfluenceScore(z, prox)
    z.dispS := f_calculateDisplacementScore(z)
    z.tfS := f_calculateTimeframeScore(z.tfSec)
    float wSum = i_wFresh + i_wConf + i_wDisp + i_wTf
    z.score := wSum > 0.0 ? (i_wFresh * z.freshS + i_wConf * z.confS + i_wDisp * z.dispS + i_wTf * z.tfS) / wSum : 0.0
    z.score

// deterministic tie-breaker chain: fresher, higher timeframe, larger displacement, most recently created.
// Returns +1 when a beats b, -1 when b beats a, 0 when identical (the caller then keeps the earlier list index).
f_selChain(HtfFVG a, HtfFVG b) =>
    a.freshS != b.freshS ? (a.freshS > b.freshS ? 1 : -1) : a.tfSec != b.tfSec ? (a.tfSec > b.tfSec ? 1 : -1) : a.dispS != b.dispS ? (a.dispS > b.dispS ? 1 : -1) : a.createdTime != b.createdTime ? (a.createdTime > b.createdTime ? 1 : -1) : 0

// composite score comparison (only when scoring is enabled), then the chain
f_selByScore(HtfFVG a, HtfFVG b) =>
    i_htfScoring and a.score != b.score ? (a.score > b.score ? 1 : -1) : f_selChain(a, b)

// does zone a beat zone b under the selected mode?  px = current confirmed close (CE mode)
f_selBetter(HtfFVG a, HtfFVG b, float px) =>
    float da = math.abs(px - f_getConsequentEncroachment(a))
    float db = math.abs(px - f_getConsequentEncroachment(b))
    float tol = i_ceTieTicks * syminfo.mintick
    int byScore = f_selByScore(a, b)
    int cmp = i_htfSelectionMode == "Strictly Highest Timeframe" ? (a.tfSec != b.tfSec ? (a.tfSec > b.tfSec ? 1 : -1) : byScore) : i_htfSelectionMode == "Strictly Lowest HTF (Refinement)" ? (a.tfSec != b.tfSec ? (a.tfSec < b.tfSec ? 1 : -1) : byScore) : i_htfSelectionMode == "Deepest Consequent Encroachment (CE)" ? (math.abs(da - db) > tol ? (da < db ? 1 : -1) : byScore) : byScore
    cmp > 0

// the selection pass: score every candidate, cluster the overlapping ones, pick ONE winner per cluster,
// write HtfFVG.selected and apply the visuals.  O(n^2) on the active list (at most 'Max active per
// timeframe' x 9 slots), no drawing objects created or deleted.
f_selectBestHTFFVG(float px) =>
    int n = array.size(htfList)
    if n > 0
        float prox = i_confProxAtr * nz(atrValue, 0.0)
        bool allOne = i_htfSelectScope == "All candidate zones (one winner)"
        for z in htfList
            z.candidate := f_hzCandidate(z)
            z.cluster := -1
            z.selected := z.candidate ? z.selected : true
            f_calculateFVGProbability(z, prox)
        // clusters = connected components of the overlap graph (scope 'all' = one component)
        int nComp = 0
        array<int> stack = array.new_int()
        for [i, zi] in htfList
            if zi.candidate and zi.cluster < 0
                zi.cluster := nComp
                array.clear(stack)
                array.push(stack, i)
                while array.size(stack) > 0
                    int j = array.pop(stack)
                    HtfFVG zj = array.get(htfList, j)
                    for [k, zk] in htfList
                        if zk.candidate and zk.cluster < 0 and (allOne or f_isOverlapping(zj, zk))
                            zk.cluster := nComp
                            array.push(stack, k)
                nComp += 1
        // one deterministic winner per cluster
        if nComp > 0
            for c = 0 to nComp - 1
                int best = -1
                for [i, zc] in htfList
                    if zc.cluster == c and (best < 0 or f_selBetter(zc, array.get(htfList, best), px))
                        best := i
                for [i, zs] in htfList
                    zs.selected := zs.cluster == c ? i == best : zs.selected
        for z in htfList
            f_hzApplySelection(z)
    true

// ============================== MAIN (closed bars only) ==============================
bool buySignal   = false
bool sellSignal  = false
bool bullSmtDet  = false
bool bearSmtDet  = false
bool bullSmtConf = false
bool bearSmtConf = false
string buyMsg  = ""
string sellMsg = ""

if barstate.isconfirmed
    // ---------- A. HTF FVG / NDOG zones: age out, invalidate using EACH slot's OWN closed bar, then add any new zone ----------
    f_expireHtfByDays()
    f_invalidateHtf(1, newH1, hC1, lC1, cC1)
    f_invalidateHtf(2, newH2, hC2, lC2, cC2)
    f_invalidateHtf(3, newH3, hC3, lC3, cC3)
    f_invalidateHtf(4, newH4, hC4, lC4, cC4)
    f_invalidateHtf(5, newH5, hC5, lC5, cC5)
    f_invalidateHtf(6, newH6, hC6, lC6, cC6)
    f_invalidateHtf(7, newH7, hC7, lC7, cC7)
    f_invalidateHtf(8, newH8, hC8, lC8, cC8)
    f_invalidateHtf(9, useNdog, high, low, close)
    f_addHtf(newH1, useHtf1, nameH1, 1, hC1, lC1, hA1, lA1, tA1, tM1, tX1, o21, h21, l21, c21, atr21, v21, va21)
    f_addHtf(newH2, useHtf2, nameH2, 2, hC2, lC2, hA2, lA2, tA2, tM2, tX2, o22, h22, l22, c22, atr22, v22, va22)
    f_addHtf(newH3, useHtf3, nameH3, 3, hC3, lC3, hA3, lA3, tA3, tM3, tX3, o23, h23, l23, c23, atr23, v23, va23)
    f_addHtf(newH4, useHtf4, nameH4, 4, hC4, lC4, hA4, lA4, tA4, tM4, tX4, o24, h24, l24, c24, atr24, v24, va24)
    f_addHtf(newH5, useHtf5, nameH5, 5, hC5, lC5, hA5, lA5, tA5, tM5, tX5, o25, h25, l25, c25, atr25, v25, va25)
    f_addHtf(newH6, useHtf6, nameH6, 6, hC6, lC6, hA6, lA6, tA6, tM6, tX6, o26, h26, l26, c26, atr26, v26, va26)
    f_addHtf(newH7, useHtf7, nameH7, 7, hC7, lC7, hA7, lA7, tA7, tM7, tX7, o27, h27, l27, c27, atr27, v27, va27)
    f_addHtf(newH8, useHtf8, nameH8, 8, hC8, lC8, hA8, lA8, tA8, tM8, tX8, o28, h28, l28, c28, atr28, v28, va28)
    f_addNdog(newDay, close[1], open, atrValue)
    // ---------- selection engine: ONE winner per cluster of overlapping candidates, before the engines run ----------
    f_selectBestHTFFVG(close)
    // "Extend with price": the right edge follows the current bar; "Fixed": the box never moves
    if htfExtendMode == "Extend with price" and array.size(htfList) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(htfList) - 1
            HtfFVG hzExt = array.get(htfList, i)
            if not na(hzExt.b)
                box.set_right(hzExt.b, time + fvgExtend * chartMs)

    // ---------- run every engine: chart feed + up to four higher-TF feeds ----------
    // feeds run first so that their raw FVG pools (2m / 3m / 5m) are current when the chart engine resolves a stack
    [sig1, bd1, be1, bc1, bcc1] = f_runEngine(e1, fF1)
    [sig2, bd2, be2, bc2, bcc2] = f_runEngine(e2, fF2)
    [sig3, bd3, be3, bc3, bcc3] = f_runEngine(e3, fF3)
    [sig4, bd4, be4, bc4, bcc4] = f_runEngine(e4, fF4)
    [sigC, bdC, beC, bcC, bccC] = f_runEngine(eC, fChart)
    bullSmtDet  := bdC or bd1 or bd2 or bd3 or bd4
    bearSmtDet  := beC or be1 or be2 or be3 or be4
    bullSmtConf := bcC or bc1 or bc2 or bc3 or bc4
    bearSmtConf := bccC or bcc1 or bcc2 or bcc3 or bcc4

    // ---------- HTF zone lifecycle / 50% CE eligibility on this confirmed chart bar ----------
    // Runs AFTER the engines so an IFVG that forms on the very bar that defends a zone still sees it as
    // eligible; from the next bar on the zone is DEFENDED and no longer counts.
    if array.size(htfList) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(htfList) - 1
            f_hzUpdate(array.get(htfList, i), open, high, low, close, atrValue)
        // re-select with the updated lifecycle states (a winner that just got DEFENDED / FILLED hands over now)
        f_selectBestHTFFVG(close)
        // primary HTF context at the current close (debug / display only)
        int primIdx = f_htfPrimaryIdx(close, close, true, close)
        if htfMatchDir
            int primIdxB = f_htfPrimaryIdx(close, close, false, close)
            if primIdxB >= 0 and (primIdx < 0 or f_hzBetter(array.get(htfList, primIdxB), array.get(htfList, primIdx), close))
                primIdx := primIdxB
        for i = 0 to array.size(htfList) - 1
            HtfFVG zp = array.get(htfList, i)
            zp.isPrimary := i == primIdx

    // ---------- signals -> marks, stop / targets, contracts ----------
    array<SigInfo> sigs = array.new<SigInfo>()
    if not na(sigC)
        array.push(sigs, sigC)
    if not na(sig1)
        array.push(sigs, sig1)
    if not na(sig2)
        array.push(sigs, sig2)
    if not na(sig3)
        array.push(sigs, sig3)
    if not na(sig4)
        array.push(sigs, sig4)
    if array.size(sigs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(sigs) - 1
            SigInfo s = array.get(sigs, i)
            string summary = f_onSignal(s)
            // ---------- strategy twin: orders from the risk module's numbers, tagged with the score components ----------
            bool inWindow = time >= s_from and time <= s_to
            float lastPlanSl = array.get(lastPlan, 1)
            float lastPlanTp1 = array.get(lastPlan, 2)
            float lastPlanTp2 = array.get(lastPlan, 3)
            float lastPlanTpSw = array.get(lastPlan, 4)
            int qty = s_qtyMode == "Fixed 1 contract" ? 1 : int(nz(array.get(lastPlan, 5), 0))
            bool sameSideOpen = s.isBull ? strategy.position_size > 0 : strategy.position_size < 0
            bool otherSideOpen = s.isBull ? strategy.position_size < 0 : strategy.position_size > 0
            bool canEnter = inWindow and qty > 0 and not sameSideOpen and (not otherSideOpen or s_allowRev)
            if not canEnter
                stratSkipped += 1
            if canEnter
                stratOrders += 1
                string oid = (s.isBull ? "L" : "S") + "|" + s.tag
                if otherSideOpen
                    strategy.close_all(comment = "reverse")
                float tpMain = s_exitModel == "TP2" ? (na(lastPlanTp2) ? lastPlanTp1 : lastPlanTp2) : s_exitModel == "Swing TP (fallback TP1)" ? (na(lastPlanTpSw) ? lastPlanTp1 : lastPlanTpSw) : lastPlanTp1
                strategy.entry(oid, s.isBull ? strategy.long : strategy.short, qty = qty, comment = oid, alert_message = s_useAlerts ? "ENTRY " + oid : na)
                if s_exitModel == "Half at TP1, rest at TP2" and qty >= 2 and not na(lastPlanTp2)
                    int half = int(math.floor(qty / 2))
                    strategy.exit("x1|" + oid, from_entry = oid, qty = half, stop = lastPlanSl, limit = lastPlanTp1, comment_profit = "TP1", comment_loss = "SL")
                    strategy.exit("x2|" + oid, from_entry = oid, qty = qty - half, stop = lastPlanSl, limit = lastPlanTp2, comment_profit = "TP2", comment_loss = "SL")
                else if s_exitModel == "Stop / time only" or na(tpMain)
                    strategy.exit("x|" + oid, from_entry = oid, stop = lastPlanSl, comment_loss = "SL")
                else
                    strategy.exit("x|" + oid, from_entry = oid, stop = lastPlanSl, limit = tpMain, comment_profit = "TP", comment_loss = "SL")
            lastSigBar := bar_index
            lastSigBull := s.isBull
            lastSigTxt := (s.isBull ? "BUY " : "SELL ") + s.tfName
            lastPlanTxt := summary
            if s.isBull
                buySignal := true
                buyMsg += (buyMsg != "" ? " | " : "") + summary + " · " + s.info
            else
                sellSignal := true
                sellMsg += (sellMsg != "" ? " | " : "") + summary + " · " + s.info

    // ---------- trade plans: follow price, mark SL / TP hits, freeze when done ----------
    if array.size(plans) > 0
        for i = array.size(plans) - 1 to 0
            TradePlan p = array.get(plans, i)
            if p.open and bar_index > p.startBar
                bool slHit = p.isBull ? low <= p.sl : high >= p.sl
                bool hasTarget = not na(p.tp1) or not na(p.tp2) or not na(p.tpSw)
                if slHit
                    p.open := false
                    p.status := (p.tp1Hit or p.tp2Hit or p.swHit) ? "STOPPED (after a target)" : "STOPPED"
                else
                    p.tp1Hit := p.tp1Hit or (not na(p.tp1) and (p.isBull ? high >= p.tp1 : low <= p.tp1))
                    p.tp2Hit := p.tp2Hit or (not na(p.tp2) and (p.isBull ? high >= p.tp2 : low <= p.tp2))
                    p.swHit := p.swHit or (not na(p.tpSw) and (p.isBull ? high >= p.tpSw : low <= p.tpSw))
                    string hitTxt = (p.tp1Hit ? "TP1 ✓ " : "") + (p.tp2Hit ? "TP2 ✓ " : "") + (p.swHit ? "Swing ✓ " : "")
                    bool allDone = hasTarget and (na(p.tp1) or p.tp1Hit) and (na(p.tp2) or p.tp2Hit) and (na(p.tpSw) or p.swHit)
                    if allDone
                        p.open := false
                        p.status := "DONE " + hitTxt
                    else if bar_index - p.startBar > tradeMaxBars
                        p.open := false
                        p.status := "EXPIRED " + hitTxt
                    else
                        p.status := "OPEN " + hitTxt
                int xr = bar_index + 1
                line.set_x2(p.lnE, xr)
                line.set_x2(p.lnS, xr)
                if not na(p.lnT1)
                    line.set_x2(p.lnT1, xr)
                if not na(p.lnT2)
                    line.set_x2(p.lnT2, xr)
                if not na(p.lnSw)
                    line.set_x2(p.lnSw, xr)
                label.set_x(p.lbl, xr)
                label.set_text(p.lbl, p.status + "\n" + p.txt)
                if not p.open
                    label.set_color(p.lbl, color.new(color.gray, 30))
    while array.size(plans) > maxPlans
        TradePlan old = array.shift(plans)
        line.delete(old.lnE)
        line.delete(old.lnS)
        line.delete(old.lnT1)
        line.delete(old.lnT2)
        line.delete(old.lnSw)
        label.delete(old.lbl)

    // ---------- strategy twin: time stop ----------
    if s_timeStop and strategy.position_size != 0 and strategy.opentrades > 0
        int openedBar = strategy.opentrades.entry_bar_index(strategy.opentrades - 1)
        if bar_index - openedBar > tradeMaxBars
            strategy.close_all(comment = "time")

    // ---------- signal marks clean-up ----------
    if array.size(sigList) > 0
        for i = array.size(sigList) - 1 to 0
            SigMark sm = array.get(sigList, i)
            if not keepHistory and time - sm.markTime > signalMaxDays * dayMs
                label.delete(sm.lbl)
                array.remove(sigList, i)
    while array.size(sigList) > 300
        array.shift(sigList)

// ============================== ALERTS ==============================
alertcondition(bullSmtDet,  title = "Bullish SMT developing", message = "Bullish SMT developing on {{ticker}} ({{interval}} chart, any feed)")
alertcondition(bearSmtDet,  title = "Bearish SMT developing", message = "Bearish SMT developing on {{ticker}} ({{interval}} chart, any feed)")
alertcondition(bullSmtConf, title = "Bullish SMT confirmed", message = "Bullish SMT confirmed on {{ticker}} ({{interval}} chart, any feed)")
alertcondition(bearSmtConf, title = "Bearish SMT confirmed", message = "Bearish SMT confirmed on {{ticker}} ({{interval}} chart, any feed)")
alertcondition(buySignal,   title = "BUY (SMT + IFVG in HTF FVG)", message = "BUY: bullish SMT + bullish IFVG in HTF FVG on {{ticker}} ({{interval}} chart)")
alertcondition(sellSignal,  title = "SELL (SMT + IFVG in HTF FVG)", message = "SELL: bearish SMT + bearish IFVG in HTF FVG on {{ticker}} ({{interval}} chart)")
// dynamic alerts (choose "Any alert() function call" in the alert dialog): include timeframe, contracts, SL distance
if buySignal
    alert("BUY " + syminfo.ticker + ": " + buyMsg, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if sellSignal
    alert("SELL " + syminfo.ticker + ": " + sellMsg, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// ============================== TABLES (last bar) ==============================
// one checklist row: ✅ / ❌ + label
f_ckRow(table t, int r, bool ok, string txt) =>
    table.cell(t, 0, r, ok ? "✅" : "❌", bgcolor = ok ? color.new(color.green, 70) : color.new(color.red, 70), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, r, txt, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 20), text_color = color.white, text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small)
    true

if barstate.islast
    var table infoTable = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 12, border_width = 1, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 20))
    color grayBg = color.new(color.gray, 50)
    array<int> cnt = array.new_int(10, 0)
    array<int> cntE = array.new_int(10, 0)
    string htfTxt = ""
    string smtTxt = "None"
    color smtBg = grayBg
    string ifvgTxt = allowedEntryTF ? "None" : "N/A (TF)"
    SMTSetup newestS = na

    // eligible / total per slot
    if array.size(htfList) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(htfList) - 1
            HtfFVG zc = array.get(htfList, i)
            array.set(cnt, zc.slot, array.get(cnt, zc.slot) + 1)
            if f_hzEligible(zc)
                array.set(cntE, zc.slot, array.get(cntE, zc.slot) + 1)
    if useHtf1
        htfTxt += nameH1 + ":" + str.tostring(array.get(cntE, 1)) + "/" + str.tostring(array.get(cnt, 1)) + " "
    if useHtf2
        htfTxt += nameH2 + ":" + str.tostring(array.get(cntE, 2)) + "/" + str.tostring(array.get(cnt, 2)) + " "
    if useHtf3
        htfTxt += nameH3 + ":" + str.tostring(array.get(cntE, 3)) + "/" + str.tostring(array.get(cnt, 3)) + " "
    if useHtf4
        htfTxt += nameH4 + ":" + str.tostring(array.get(cntE, 4)) + "/" + str.tostring(array.get(cnt, 4)) + " "
    if useHtf5
        htfTxt += nameH5 + ":" + str.tostring(array.get(cntE, 5)) + "/" + str.tostring(array.get(cnt, 5)) + " "
    if useHtf6
        htfTxt += nameH6 + ":" + str.tostring(array.get(cntE, 6)) + "/" + str.tostring(array.get(cnt, 6)) + " "
    if useHtf7
        htfTxt += nameH7 + ":" + str.tostring(array.get(cntE, 7)) + "/" + str.tostring(array.get(cnt, 7)) + " "
    if useHtf8
        htfTxt += nameH8 + ":" + str.tostring(array.get(cntE, 8)) + "/" + str.tostring(array.get(cnt, 8)) + " "
    if useNdog
        htfTxt += "NDOG:" + str.tostring(array.get(cntE, 9)) + "/" + str.tostring(array.get(cnt, 9))

    if array.size(eC.setups) > 0
        for i = array.size(eC.setups) - 1 to 0
            SMTSetup ts = array.get(eC.setups, i)
            if na(newestS) and not ts.dead and not ts.expired
                newestS := ts
    if not na(newestS)
        smtTxt := (newestS.isBull ? "Bullish" : "Bearish") + (newestS.confirmed ? " ✔ " : " … ") + newestS.refName
        smtBg := color.new(newestS.isBull ? smtBullClr : smtBearClr, 30)

    IFVGZone tl = na
    if allowedEntryTF and array.size(eC.ifvgList) > 0
        tl := array.get(eC.ifvgList, array.size(eC.ifvgList) - 1)
        ifvgTxt := (tl.isBull ? "Bullish" : "Bearish") + (tl.htfTag != "" ? " in " + f_tagText(tl.htfTag) : " (no HTF)") + " · " + tl.grade + " " + str.tostring(tl.confScore)

    bool sigRecent = withinLookback(lastSigBar)
    string sigTxt = sigRecent ? lastSigTxt : "No Trade"
    color sigBg = sigRecent ? (lastSigBull ? color.new(color.green, 20) : color.new(color.red, 20)) : grayBg
    string filtTxt = (i_requireSMT ? "" : "SMT-OPTIONAL ") + (minScore > 0 ? "SCORE>=" + str.tostring(minScore) + " " : "") + (keyFilter ? "KEY " : "") + (reqDisp ? "DISP " : "") + (reqSetupFvg ? "FVG " : "") + (reqMSS ? "MSS " : "")
    if filtTxt == ""
        filtTxt := "RAW SMT"
    string feedTxt = eC.tfName + " (chart)" + (enF1 ? ", " + e1.tfName : "") + (enF2 ? ", " + e2.tfName : "") + (enF3 ? ", " + e3.tfName : "") + (enF4 ? ", " + e4.tfName : "")

    // ---- confluence checklist (chart engine, current state) ----
    bool cSmt = not na(newestS)
    bool cSweep = cSmt
    bool cSmtConf = cSmt and newestS.confirmed
    // a live pivot divergence (section 3b) on the chart engine
    bool cPiv = false
    string cPivName = ""
    if array.size(eC.setups) > 0
        for i = array.size(eC.setups) - 1 to 0
            SMTSetup tp = array.get(eC.setups, i)
            if not cPiv and tp.pivMode and not tp.dead and not tp.expired
                cPiv := true
                cPivName := tp.refName + (tp.confirmed ? " ✔" : " …")
    bool cIfvg = not na(tl)
    bool cHtf = cIfvg and tl.htfTag != ""
    bool cDisp = false
    if cSmt
        int dB = newestS.isBull ? eC.lastBullDispBar : eC.lastBearDispBar
        cDisp := not na(dB) and (dispMaxToIfvg == 0 or eC.idx - dB <= dispMaxToIfvg)
    bool cAlign = cIfvg and tl.primaryTag != "" and tl.primaryBull == tl.isBull
    bool cSeq = cSmtConf and cIfvg and tl.isBull == newestS.isBull and tl.invBar >= newestS.confirmBar
    int cN = (cHtf ? 1 : 0) + (cSweep ? 1 : 0) + (cSmt ? 1 : 0) + (cSmtConf ? 1 : 0) + (cPiv ? 1 : 0) + (cDisp ? 1 : 0) + (cIfvg ? 1 : 0) + (cAlign ? 1 : 0)
    string cPivTxt = "Pivot SMT divergence" + (cPiv ? " · " + cPivName : "")
    string cHtfTxt = "Delivering from HTF Gap" + (cHtf ? " (" + f_tagText(tl.htfTag) + ")" : "")
    string cSmtTxt = "SMT" + (cSmt ? " · " + newestS.refName : "")
    string cIfvgTxt = "IFVG" + (cIfvg ? " · " + tl.resTf + (tl.isBull ? " ▲" : " ▼") + " · " + tl.grade + " " + str.tostring(tl.confScore) + "/100" + (f_ifvgPassesThreshold(tl.confScore) ? "" : " ✗") : "")
    f_ckRow(infoTable, 0, cHtf, cHtfTxt)
    f_ckRow(infoTable, 1, cSweep, "Liquidity Sweep / Swing" + (cSmt and not i_requireSMT ? " (SMT optional)" : ""))
    f_ckRow(infoTable, 2, cSmt, cSmtTxt)
    f_ckRow(infoTable, 3, cSmtConf, "SMT Confirmed")
    f_ckRow(infoTable, 4, cPiv, cPivTxt)
    f_ckRow(infoTable, 5, cDisp, "Displacement")
    f_ckRow(infoTable, 6, cIfvg, cIfvgTxt)
    f_ckRow(infoTable, 7, cAlign, "HTF Direction Aligned")
    table.cell(infoTable, 0, 8, "🧠", bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 20), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(infoTable, 1, 8, str.tostring(cN) + "/8 Confluences" + (cSeq ? " · sequence ✓" : ""), bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 20), text_color = color.orange, text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(infoTable, 0, 9, "▶", bgcolor = sigBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(infoTable, 1, 9, "Signal: " + sigTxt, bgcolor = sigBg, text_color = color.white, text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(infoTable, 0, 10, "$", bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(infoTable, 1, 10, lastPlanTxt, bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white, text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(infoTable, 0, 11, "HTF", bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(infoTable, 1, 11, htfTxt + " · " + feedTxt, bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white, text_halign = text.align_left, text_size = size.tiny)

    if showDebug
        var table dbgTable = table.new(position.bottom_right, 2, 15, border_width = 1)
        string htfChk = ""
        string liveTxt = "none live"
        string blockTxt = "-"
        string lastTag = eC.lastIfvgTag
        if useHtf1
            htfChk += nameH1 + (str.contains(lastTag, "|" + nameH1 + "|") ? "✓ " : "✗ ")
        if useHtf2
            htfChk += nameH2 + (str.contains(lastTag, "|" + nameH2 + "|") ? "✓ " : "✗ ")
        if useHtf3
            htfChk += nameH3 + (str.contains(lastTag, "|" + nameH3 + "|") ? "✓ " : "✗ ")
        if useHtf4
            htfChk += nameH4 + (str.contains(lastTag, "|" + nameH4 + "|") ? "✓ " : "✗ ")
        if useHtf5
            htfChk += nameH5 + (str.contains(lastTag, "|" + nameH5 + "|") ? "✓ " : "✗ ")
        if useHtf6
            htfChk += nameH6 + (str.contains(lastTag, "|" + nameH6 + "|") ? "✓ " : "✗ ")
        if useHtf7
            htfChk += nameH7 + (str.contains(lastTag, "|" + nameH7 + "|") ? "✓ " : "✗ ")
        if useHtf8
            htfChk += nameH8 + (str.contains(lastTag, "|" + nameH8 + "|") ? "✓ " : "✗ ")
        if useNdog
            htfChk += "NDOG" + (str.contains(lastTag, "|NDOG|") ? "✓ " : "✗ ")
        // lifecycle state of every active zone (newest first)
        string hzTxt = "none"
        if array.size(htfList) > 0
            hzTxt := ""
            int shown = 0
            for i = array.size(htfList) - 1 to 0
                HtfFVG zs = array.get(htfList, i)
                if shown < 12
                    hzTxt += (hzTxt != "" ? ", " : "") + zs.tf + (zs.isBull ? "▲" : "▼") + " " + f_hzStateName(zs.state)
                shown += 1
            if shown > 12
                hzTxt += " … +" + str.tostring(shown - 12)
        if not na(newestS)
            float smtAgeD = (time - newestS.detectTime) / 86400000.0
            liveTxt := (newestS.isBull ? "Bull " : "Bear ") + (newestS.confirmed ? "confirmed" : "developing") + " @" + newestS.refName + " · " + (newestS.sweeper == 1 ? syminfo.ticker : corrName) + " swept" + (newestS.used ? " · SIGNAL FIRED" : "") + " · age " + str.tostring(smtAgeD, "#.##") + "d / max " + (smtMaxDays > 0 ? str.tostring(smtMaxDays) + "d" : "off") + " · " + (newestS.expired ? "EXPIRED" : "ACTIVE")
            blockTxt := newestS.used ? "signal fired" : f_reason(eC, newestS)
        string cntSmtTxt = "dev " + str.tostring(eC.cntSmtDev) + " (pivot " + str.tostring(eC.cntPivSmt) + ")  conf " + str.tostring(eC.cntSmtConf) + "  inval " + str.tostring(eC.cntSmtInv) + "  exp " + str.tostring(eC.cntSmtExp)
        string cntIfvgTxt = "bull " + str.tostring(eC.cntIfvgBull) + "  bear " + str.tostring(eC.cntIfvgBear) + "  rejected(quality) " + str.tostring(eC.cntIfvgRej) + "  too old " + str.tostring(eC.cntIfvgOld) + "  below min score " + str.tostring(eC.cntIfvgScoreRej)
        string cntSigTxt = "buy " + str.tostring(eC.cntBuy) + "  sell " + str.tostring(eC.cntSell)
        string feedDbg = f_engSummary(e1) + " | " + f_engSummary(e2) + " | " + f_engSummary(e3) + " | " + f_engSummary(e4)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 0, 0, "SMT log (" + eC.tfName + ")", bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 1, 0, eC.logSmt, bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 0, 1, "SMT live", bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 1, 1, liveTxt, bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 0, 2, "Blocker", bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 1, 2, blockTxt, bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 0, 3, "IFVG log", bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 1, 3, eC.logIfvg, bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 0, 4, "Last IFVG in", bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 1, 4, htfChk, bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 0, 5, "Pairing", bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 1, 5, eC.logPair, bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 0, 6, "SMT counts", bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 1, 6, cntSmtTxt, bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 0, 7, "IFVG counts", bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 1, 7, cntIfvgTxt, bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 0, 8, "Signals / filters", bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 1, 8, cntSigTxt + "  |  " + filtTxt, bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 0, 9, "MTF feeds", bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 1, 9, feedDbg, bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 0, 10, "HTF zone states", bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 1, 10, hzTxt, bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white)
        // ---- Phase 3: context + event sequence for the chart engine ----
        string p3Ctx = "no IFVG yet"
        string p3Seq = eC.lastSeq
        if not na(tl)
            string primTxt = tl.primaryTag != "" ? tl.primaryTag + (tl.primaryBull ? " Bullish" : " Bearish") : "none"
            string alignTxt = tl.primaryTag == "" ? "n/a" : (tl.primaryBull == tl.isBull ? "YES" : "NO")
            p3Ctx := "HTF primary: " + primTxt + " · LTF: " + (tl.isBull ? "BULLISH" : "BEARISH") + " · aligned: " + alignTxt + " (" + htfDirFilter + ")"
        string evTxt = "Sweep/SMT: " + (na(newestS) ? "no" : "yes @" + str.tostring(newestS.sweepBar)) + " · SMT conf: " + (na(newestS) or not newestS.confirmed ? "no" : "yes @" + str.tostring(newestS.confirmBar)) + " · Disp: " + (na(newestS) ? "-" : (newestS.isBull ? (na(eC.lastBullDispBar) ? "no" : "yes @" + str.tostring(eC.lastBullDispBar)) : (na(eC.lastBearDispBar) ? "no" : "yes @" + str.tostring(eC.lastBearDispBar)))) + " · IFVG: " + (na(eC.lastIfvgBar) ? "no" : "yes @" + str.tostring(eC.lastIfvgBar)) + " · seq filter " + (seqFilter ? "ON" : "OFF") + " · disp filter " + dispFilter
        table.cell(dbgTable, 0, 11, "P3 context", bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 1, 11, p3Ctx + "\n" + evTxt, bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 0, 12, "P3 last sequence", bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 1, 12, p3Seq, bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white)
        string ladderTxt = ""
        if array.size(ifvgLadder) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(ifvgLadder) - 1
                Engine el = array.get(ifvgLadder, i)
                ladderTxt += (ladderTxt != "" ? " → " : "") + el.tfName + "(" + str.tostring(array.size(el.rawList)) + ")"
        string ifvgDbgTxt = "IFVG TF ok: " + (eC.ifvgTf ? "yes" : "NO (chart > 5m)") + " · mode " + (ifvgResolve == "Per-feed (legacy)" ? "per-feed" : "resolved") + " · chart pool " + str.tostring(array.size(eC.rawList)) + " waiting · ladder " + (ladderTxt == "" ? "none" : ladderTxt) + " · close " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick) + "\nlast: " + eC.ifvgDbg
        table.cell(dbgTable, 0, 13, "IFVG DEBUG", bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 1, 13, ifvgDbgTxt, bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 0, 14, "STRATEGY", bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white)
        table.cell(dbgTable, 1, 14, "orders submitted " + str.tostring(stratOrders) + " · skipped (window / qty / position) " + str.tostring(stratSkipped) + " · closed trades " + str.tostring(strategy.closedtrades) + " · open " + str.tostring(strategy.opentrades) + " · equity " + str.tostring(strategy.equity, "#.##"), bgcolor = grayBg, text_color = color.white)

    // ---- Phase 2 HTF zone table: one row per active zone (newest first, max 20) ----
    if showHtfDebug
        var table hzTable = table.new(position.bottom_left, 12, 21, border_width = 1)
        table.clear(hzTable, 0, 0, 11, 20)
        string hdr = "TF|Type|Dir|State|Elig|Age|AgeExp|Retest|Used|Primary|Sel|Score"
        array<string> hdrs = str.split(hdr, "|")
        for c = 0 to 11
            table.cell(hzTable, c, 0, array.get(hdrs, c), bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
        if array.size(htfList) > 0
            int row = 1
            for i = array.size(htfList) - 1 to 0
                HtfFVG zt = array.get(htfList, i)
                if row <= 20
                    bool el = f_hzEligible(zt)
                    color rowBg = zt.isPrimary ? color.new(color.blue, 40) : el ? color.new(color.green, 70) : color.new(color.gray, 60)
                    table.cell(hzTable, 0, row, zt.tf, bgcolor = rowBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(hzTable, 1, row, zt.slot == 9 ? "NDOG" : "FVG", bgcolor = rowBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(hzTable, 2, row, zt.isBull ? "▲" : "▼", bgcolor = rowBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(hzTable, 3, row, f_hzStateName(zt.state), bgcolor = rowBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(hzTable, 4, row, el ? "yes" : (not f_hzLifeOk(zt) ? "no:state" : not f_hzAgeOk(zt) ? "no:age" : not f_hzRetestOk(zt) ? "no:retest" : "no:not selected"), bgcolor = rowBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(hzTable, 5, row, str.tostring(zt.ageBars), bgcolor = rowBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(hzTable, 6, row, zt.ageExpired ? "yes" : "no", bgcolor = rowBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(hzTable, 7, row, zt.firstRetestAvailable ? "yes" : "no", bgcolor = rowBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(hzTable, 8, row, zt.firstRetestUsed ? "yes" : "no", bgcolor = rowBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(hzTable, 9, row, zt.isPrimary ? "PRIMARY" : "", bgcolor = rowBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(hzTable, 10, row, zt.candidate ? (zt.selected ? "SEL" : "hidden") : "-", bgcolor = rowBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(hzTable, 11, row, zt.candidate ? str.tostring(zt.score, "0.00") : "-", bgcolor = rowBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                row += 1

    // ---- selection engine debug: every candidate with cluster, winner flag, composite score and components ----
    if i_htfSelDebug
        var table selTable = table.new(position.middle_left, 11, 21, border_width = 1)
        table.clear(selTable, 0, 0, 10, 20)
        string selHdr = "Cluster|TF|Dir|State|Sel|Score|Fresh|Conf|Disp|TF wt|CE"
        array<string> selHdrs = str.split(selHdr, "|")
        for c = 0 to 10
            table.cell(selTable, c, 0, array.get(selHdrs, c), bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.cell(selTable, 0, 20, "mode", bgcolor = color.gray, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.cell(selTable, 1, 20, i_htfSelectionMode + " · " + i_htfSelectScope + (i_htfScoring ? "" : " · scoring OFF"), bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 50), text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.merge_cells(selTable, 1, 20, 10, 20)
        if array.size(htfList) > 0
            int srow = 1
            for i = array.size(htfList) - 1 to 0
                HtfFVG zq = array.get(htfList, i)
                if zq.candidate and srow <= 19
                    color sBg = zq.selected ? color.new(color.green, 60) : color.new(color.gray, 70)
                    table.cell(selTable, 0, srow, str.tostring(zq.cluster), bgcolor = sBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(selTable, 1, srow, zq.tf, bgcolor = sBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(selTable, 2, srow, zq.isBull ? "▲" : "▼", bgcolor = sBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(selTable, 3, srow, f_hzStateName(zq.state), bgcolor = sBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(selTable, 4, srow, zq.selected ? "WINNER" : "", bgcolor = sBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(selTable, 5, srow, str.tostring(zq.score, "0.000"), bgcolor = sBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(selTable, 6, srow, str.tostring(zq.freshS, "0.00"), bgcolor = sBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(selTable, 7, srow, str.tostring(zq.confS, "0.00"), bgcolor = sBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(selTable, 8, srow, str.tostring(zq.dispS, "0.00"), bgcolor = sBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(selTable, 9, srow, str.tostring(zq.tfS, "0.00"), bgcolor = sBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    table.cell(selTable, 10, srow, str.tostring(zq.ce, format.mintick), bgcolor = sBg, text_color = color.white, text_size = size.tiny)
                    srow += 1
